MC.add({"enchants:mechanics/reducedurability":{"h":"<h2>Reduce Durability</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Damages the caster&#x27;s item durability by a flat amount or percentage. Can optionally respect the Unbreaking enchantment&#x27;s negate chance.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>amount</code></td><td><code>a</code></td><td>The durability damage amount (flat, or percentage if <code>percent</code> is true)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><code>percent</code></td><td><code>p</code></td><td>If true, <code>amount</code> is treated as a percentage of max durability (0.0–1.0)</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td><code>respectunbreaking</code></td><td><code>unbreaking</code>, <code>ru</code></td><td>Whether to apply unbreaking negate chance before damaging</td><td>true</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Frost Walker durability cost\nFrostWalker:\n  Skills:\n  - reducedurability{a=2} @self ~onTimer:10\n\n# Percentage-based durability cost\nHeavyStrike:\n  Skills:\n  - reducedurability{a=0.05;percent=true;unbreaking=false} @self ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>durabilityreduce</code></li><li><code>itemdamage</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/ReduceDurability"},"enchants:mechanics/soulspeed":{"h":"<h2>Soul Speed</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Applies a movement speed attribute modifier while the caster stands on configurable block types. By default, emulates vanilla Soul Speed on Soul Sand and Soul Soil.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>amount</code></td><td><code>amt</code>, <code>a</code></td><td>The speed modifier amount</td><td>0.0405</td></tr><tr><td><code>operation</code></td><td><code>op</code>, <code>o</code></td><td>The attribute operation: <code>ADD_NUMBER</code>, <code>ADD_SCALAR</code>, or <code>MULTIPLY_SCALAR_1</code></td><td><code>ADD_NUMBER</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>blocks</code></td><td><code>b</code></td><td>Comma-separated list of block material names to activate on</td><td><code>SOUL_SAND,SOUL_SOIL</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>SoulSpeed:\n  Skills:\n    - soulspeed{a=&lt;math.1.2379+0.1808*enchant_level&gt;;op=MULTIPLY;blocks=SOUL_SAND} @self ~onTimer:10\n# Custom speed boost on ice blocks\nIceRunner:\n  Skills:\n  - soulspeed{a=0.06;blocks=ICE,PACKED_ICE,BLUE_ICE} @self ~onTimer:10</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>soulspeedboost</code></li><li><code>blockspeedboost</code></li><li><code>blockspeed</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/SoulSpeed"},"enchants:mechanics/unbreaking":{"h":"<h2>Unbreaking</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Applies vanilla-style unbreaking rolls to the live durability damage event. Each point of unbreaking level gives a chance to negate the durability loss entirely.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>chance</code></td><td><code>negatechance</code>, <code>c</code></td><td>Custom negate chance per level (0.0–1.0). If -1, uses vanilla formula</td><td>-1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>Unbreaking:\n  Skills:\n  - unbreaking{} @self ~onItem_damage</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>unbreakingitem</code></li><li><code>durabilityguard</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/Unbreaking"},"enchants:mechanics/veinminer":{"h":"<h2>VeinMiner</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Breaks all blocks within a configurable cube around the skill origin that match a block tag and/or material list. Each block fires a synthetic <code>BlockBreakEvent</code> so protection plugins can veto individual breaks. Drops respect Fortune and Silk Touch when <code>usetool=true</code>.</p>\n<p>Origin is set automatically by MythicEnchants on <code>~onBlockBreak</code> — point <code>@self</code> at the mechanic and it will center on the block that was broken.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>t</code></td><td><code>type</code>, <code>tag</code>, <code>types</code>, <code>blocks</code></td><td>Comma-separated list of block tags (<code>#minecraft:logs</code>), material names (<code>COAL_ORE</code>), and/or <code>nexo:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>crucible:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>itemsadder:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>craftengine:&lt;id&gt;</code> custom-block ids. All can be mixed freely.</td><td><code>#minecraft:logs</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>rx</code></td><td><code>radiusx</code>, <code>r</code></td><td>Horizontal X radius in blocks</td><td><code>2</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>ry</code></td><td><code>radiusy</code></td><td>Vertical Y radius in blocks</td><td><code>24</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>rz</code></td><td><code>radiusz</code></td><td>Horizontal Z radius in blocks</td><td><code>2</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>drops</code></td><td><code>d</code></td><td>Whether to drop items from broken blocks</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>usetool</code></td><td><code>tool</code></td><td>Use the player&#x27;s held tool for drops, enabling Fortune and Silk Touch</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>maxblocks</code></td><td><code>max</code>, <code>mb</code></td><td>Maximum number of blocks to break per cast. <code>0</code> = unlimited.</td><td><code>0</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>perdrop</code></td><td><code>perdurability</code>, <code>pd</code></td><td>Damage the tool by 1 durability per block broken</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>chanceperdrop</code></td><td><code>chance</code>, <code>dc</code></td><td>0–1 probability per block to consume 1 durability. Overrides <code>perdrop</code> when set (≥ 0).</td><td><code>-1</code> (disabled)</td></tr><tr><td><code>respectunbreaking</code></td><td><code>unbreaking</code>, <code>ru</code></td><td>Apply the vanilla Unbreaking negation roll before consuming durability</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>perblock</code></td><td><code>perblockspertick</code>, <code>bpt</code></td><td>Blocks broken per tick, spreading a large vein across multiple ticks instead of one synchronous loop. <code>0</code> = instant/unthrottled (old behavior).</td><td><code>1</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>tickdelay</code></td><td><code>spreaddelay</code>, <code>spreadticks</code></td><td>Ticks to wait between each batch of <code>perblock</code> blocks. Only relevant when <code>perblock &gt; 0</code>.</td><td><code>1</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Block Matching</h3>\n<p>Each entry in <code>t</code> is resolved at load time:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Example</th><th>Resolves as</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>#namespace:tag</code></td><td><code>#minecraft:logs</code></td><td>Bukkit block tag — matches all tagged materials</td></tr><tr><td><code>#tag</code> (no namespace)</td><td><code>#logs</code></td><td>Shorthand — <code>minecraft:</code> namespace is assumed</td></tr><tr><td><code>MATERIAL</code></td><td><code>COAL_ORE</code></td><td>Exact Bukkit <code>Material</code> match</td></tr><tr><td><code>nexo:&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td><code>nexo:ruby_ore</code></td><td>Matches a specific Nexo custom block by its item id</td></tr><tr><td><code>crucible:&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td><code>crucible:sapphire_ore</code></td><td>Matches a specific MythicCrucible custom block by its internal item id</td></tr><tr><td><code>itemsadder:&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td><code>itemsadder:topaz_ore</code></td><td>Matches a specific ItemsAdder custom block by its namespaced id</td></tr><tr><td><code>craftengine:&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td><code>craftengine:emerald_ore</code></td><td>Matches a specific CraftEngine custom block by its namespaced id</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Unknown tags and materials log a warning at startup and are silently skipped at runtime.</p>\n<h3>Custom Blocks</h3>\n<p>Nexo/MythicCrucible/ItemsAdder/CraftEngine custom blocks matched by <code>t=</code> are broken <b>without ever publishing a real <code>BlockBreakEvent</code> for that addon to see</b> — its own break handling (which would otherwise spawn its configured loot directly, unsuppressably, before any enchant mechanic gets a chance to react) never runs for vein-mined custom blocks. Instead, <code>~onBlockBreak</code>/<code>~onCustomBlockBreak</code> are dispatched directly in-process for each one, and <code>blockdrops</code>/this mechanic&#x27;s own fallback produce the drops — same output as breaking one manually. See <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"blockdrops\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/blockdrops.md\">blockdrops.md#custom-blocks</a> for the full mechanism this builds on.</p>\n<p>Note: <code>?triggerBlockType</code>/<code>?blockType</code> conditions only understand vanilla <code>Material</code> names via MythicMobs&#x27; own built-in parser — they can&#x27;t be given <code>nexo:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>crucible:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>itemsadder:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>craftengine:&lt;id&gt;</code> entries the way <code>veinminer{t=...}</code>&#x27;s own filter can, so scoping a vein-mine enchant to &quot;only ores, including a custom one&quot; has to happen via <code>t=</code> on the mechanic itself, not a condition.</p>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Timber enchant — fell a whole tree when a log is broken\ntimber:\n  Skills:\n    - veinminer{t=#minecraft:logs;rx=2;ry=24;rz=2} @self ~onBlockBreak ?triggerBlockType{t=#minecraft:logs}\n    - sound{s=entity.player.attack.sweep;v=0.7;p=0.8} @self ~onBlockBreak ?triggerBlockType{t=#minecraft:logs}\n\n# Vein miner enchant — break connected ore veins\nvein_miner:\n  Skills:\n    - veinminer{t=#minecraft:coal_ores,#minecraft:iron_ores,#minecraft:gold_ores;rx=3;ry=3;rz=3} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Mixed tag + material\nmushroom_feller:\n  Skills:\n    - veinminer{t=#minecraft:logs,MUSHROOM_STEM,BROWN_MUSHROOM_BLOCK,RED_MUSHROOM_BLOCK;rx=2;ry=24;rz=2} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Vein-mine custom ores from all four addons alongside vanilla ones\ncustom_vein_miner:\n  Skills:\n    - veinminer{t=#minecraft:coal_ores,nexo:ruby_ore,crucible:sapphire_ore,itemsadder:topaz_ore,craftengine:emerald_ore;rx=3;ry=3;rz=3} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Same vein-miner, plus extra drops on just the custom-block portion of the vein\ncustom_vein_miner_bonus:\n  Skills:\n    - veinminer{t=#minecraft:coal_ores,nexo:ruby_ore;rx=3;ry=3;rz=3} @self ~onBlockBreak\n    - blockdrops{mult=2} @self ~onCustomBlockBreak</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>veinminer</code></li><li><code>vein</code></li><li><code>fellblocks</code></li></ul>\n<h3>Notes</h3>\n<ul><li>The mechanic is <code>INoTargetSkill</code> — it reads the skill origin directly and does not use location targets. Always pair it with <code>@self</code>; <code>@origin</code> or <code>@triggerlocation</code> will have no effect on which blocks it breaks.</li><li>The center block (the one the player actually struck) is never included in the break set — it was already broken and already dispatched <code>~onBlockBreak</code> by the real event that fired this skill. Only the surrounding matched blocks are this mechanic&#x27;s to break.</li><li>Each block it breaks (other than the center) fires a real <code>~onBlockBreak</code>/<code>~onCustomBlockBreak</code> dispatch, so other enchants on the tool (Fortune-style <code>blockdrops</code>, <code>fakedrops</code>, etc.) react per-block exactly as if the player had broken each one manually. Because <code>veinminer{}</code> is typically on that same trigger, this dispatch re-fires <code>veinminer{}</code> itself for every block it breaks — a dedicated re-entrancy guard makes any such nested/self-triggered invocation a no-op (it does not break a second cube centered on that block), so only the original player-initiated break ever starts a vein-mine.</li><li>With <code>perblock &gt; 0</code> (default), breaking is spread across ticks — some blocks in the vein may still be standing for a moment after the cast returns. A following skill line on the same <code>~onBlockBreak</code> trigger that depends on the whole vein already being gone should set <code>perblock=0</code> to force the old fully-synchronous behavior.</li><li>Setting <code>drops=false</code> removes blocks with <code>setType(AIR)</code> without any drops or sounds.</li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/VeinMiner"},"enchants:mechanics/windburst":{"h":"<h2>Wind Burst</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Emulates the vanilla Wind Burst mace enchantment. Launches the caster upward and knocks back nearby entities on a smash attack. By default, requires the caster to be falling.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>launchbase</code></td><td><code>lb</code></td><td>Base upward launch velocity</td><td>0.5</td></tr><tr><td><code>launchperlevel</code></td><td><code>lpl</code></td><td>Additional launch velocity per enchantment level</td><td>0.5</td></tr><tr><td><code>knockbackradius</code></td><td><code>kr</code></td><td>Radius around the impact point to knock back entities</td><td>3.5</td></tr><tr><td><code>knockbackstrength</code></td><td><code>ks</code></td><td>Knockback strength applied to nearby entities</td><td>1.0</td></tr><tr><td><code>requirefalling</code></td><td><code>rf</code></td><td>Whether the caster must be falling for the mechanic to activate</td><td>true</td></tr><tr><td><code>particles</code></td><td><code>p</code></td><td>Whether to display wind burst particles</td><td>true</td></tr><tr><td><code>sound</code></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>Whether to play the wind burst sound effect</td><td>true</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>WindBurst:\n  Skills:\n  - windburst{} @self ~onAttack\n\n# Custom wind burst with larger knockback\nHeavyImpact:\n  Skills:\n  - windburst{lb=1.0;lpl=0.75;kr=5.0;ks=2.0} @self ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>windcharge</code></li><li><code>windburstmace</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/WindBurst"},"enchants:targeters/enchantmentitem":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Targets the item casting the enchantment skill.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.\\ If using <a href=\"https://mythiccraft.io/index.php?resources/crucible-custom-items-armor-furniture-blocks-more.2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicCrucible</a>, MythicEnchants also enables this targeter within skills triggered by MythicCrucible item skills.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>none</code></td><td></td><td>This targeter has no attributes currently.</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>specialItemUse:\n  Skills:\n  # This meta-skill&#x27;s original target receives an info message\n  - message{msg=&quot;The item magically repaired itself!&quot;}\n  # But the item that cast the skill receives the durability repair\n  - durability{a=20} @item</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>castingItem</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Targeters/EnchantmentItem"},"enchants:targeters/targeters":{"h":"<p>The Mythic-ecosystem targeters MythicEnchants provides.  These expand on <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/Targeters\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicMob Targeters</a>, which typically may be used as expected within enchantment skills.</p>\n<h3>Enchantment Targeters</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Targeter</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"targeters/enchantmentitem\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Targeters/enchantmentItem\"><code>@enchantmentItem</code></a></td><td>The item casting the enchantment skill</td></tr><tr><td><code>@shotProjectile</code></td><td>Returns the <b>projectile entity</b> of the in-flight shoot/launch/hit event</td></tr><tr><td><code>@projectileOrigin</code></td><td>Returns the projectile&#x27;s <b>launch location</b> (spawn/muzzle point; on a hit event, the impact point)</td></tr><tr><td><code>@projectileDestination</code></td><td>Returns the projectile&#x27;s <b>destination location</b> — on impact, the hit point; on shoot/launch, a ray-trace forward along velocity (up to 64 blocks)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<p>📝 <code>CONFIG.YML SNIPPET</code></p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Targeters/Targeters"},"enchants:conditions/batchedchance":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>A chance that is rolled <b>once</b> and shared across multiple skill lines, so effects on different triggers (and different ticks) fire together — or not at all — on the same probability. A normal per-line <code>[chance]</code> rolls independently on every line, so two different-time events can never be linked to one decision; this condition fixes that. The roll is cached per <b>caster + key</b> and reused until it has been read <code>consume</code> times, then it resets so the next round re-rolls.</p>\n<h3>Auto-keying (zero config)</h3>\n<p>The <code>key</code> is optional. When omitted, it is derived automatically from the <b>firing enchantment&#x27;s ID</b>, so every no-key <code>batchedchance</code> line on the same enchant shares one roll — the enchant procs as a whole or not at all, with no key to type. Provide an explicit <code>key</code> only when one enchant needs several independent batches, or when used outside a MythicEnchants enchant (no enchant context available — falls back to a shared <code>auto</code> key).</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>key</code></td><td><code>k</code>, <code>id</code></td><td>Identifier linking the lines that share one roll.</td><td><i>auto: firing enchant ID</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>chance</code></td><td><code>c</code></td><td>Probability <code>0.0</code>–<code>1.0</code> used on the first (deciding) check.</td><td><code>0.5</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>consume</code></td><td><code>uses</code>, <code>n</code></td><td>How many checks share the cached roll before it resets. Set to the number of lines sharing the key.</td><td><code>2</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Zero-config: both lines auto-link by enchant ID, sharing one 20% roll.\nfrost_combo:\n  Skills:\n  - skill{s=FrostStrike} @target ?batchedchance{chance=0.2} ~onAttack\n  - skill{s=FrostShot}   @self   ?batchedchance{chance=0.2} ~onShoot</code></pre>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Explicit keys: two independent batches on one enchant.\nstorm_brand:\n  Skills:\n  - skill{s=A} @target ?batchedchance{chance=0.2;key=combo1} ~onAttack\n  - skill{s=B} @self   ?batchedchance{chance=0.2;key=combo1} ~onShoot\n  - skill{s=C} @target ?batchedchance{chance=0.5;key=combo2;consume=2} ~onDamaged</code></pre>\n<h3>Notes</h3>\n<ul><li>The <code>chance</code> is decided on the <b>first</b> check; lines sharing a roll should use the same <code>chance</code> (later differing values are ignored until the roll resets).</li><li>Set <code>consume</code> to the number of lines that share the key (default <code>2</code> = a pair). If a paired event sometimes never fires, the cached roll lingers until its <code>consume</code> count is reached.</li><li>The roll is <b>per caster</b>, so players never share each other&#x27;s rolls.</li></ul>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>linkedchance</code></li><li><code>sharedchance</code></li><li><code>batchchance</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/BatchedChance"},"enchants:conditions/conditions":{"h":"<p>The Mythic-ecosystem conditions MythicEnchants provides.  These expand on <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/conditions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicMob Conditions</a>, which typically may be used as expected within enchantment skills, including in-line condition evaluations.</p>\n<p>These registered conditions may be used outside of enchantments as well, such as a mob&#x27;s skills evaluating a player&#x27;s item for enchantments or durability.</p>\n<blockquote><p><a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/mythiccrucible/-/wikis/Skills/Conditions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicCrucible</a> also grants item-related conditions, such as checking an item&#x27;s model.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Enchanted Item Conditions</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Condition</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/mench\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/mench\"><code>hasMythicEnchant</code></a></td><td>Evaluates whether the item has a specific enchantment</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/itemdurability\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/itemDurability\"><code>itemDurability</code></a></td><td>Evaluates the remaining durability available on the enchanted item</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/itemuseddurability\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/itemUsedDurability\"><code>itemUsedDurability</code></a></td><td>Evaluates the amount of lost durability on the enchanted item</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/itemdurabilitypercent\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/itemDurabilityPercent\"><code>itemDurabilityPercent</code></a></td><td>Evaluates the remaining durability percentage on the enchanted item</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/soulbounduses\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/soulbounduses\"><code>soulbounduses</code></a></td><td>Evaluates the remaining <code>recoveritem</code> uses/charges on the trigger item</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/batchedchance\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/BatchedChance\"><code>batchedchance</code></a></td><td>A chance that is rolled <b>once</b> and shared across multiple skill lines</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/lethalcheck\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/lethalcheck\"><code>lethalcheck</code></a></td><td>Evaluates whether the current damage event would kill the target entity</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/customblock\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/customblock\"><code>customblock</code></a></td><td>Evaluates whether the current block-break&#x27;s block is a custom block</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/custombir\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/custombir\"><code>custombir</code></a></td><td>Checks whether Nexo, MythicCrucible, and/or ItemsAdder custom blocks are present within enchanting-table range</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Player Conditions</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Condition</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/hasexperience\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/HasExperience\"><code>hasExperience</code></a></td><td>Evaluates whether the player has a range of exp points or levels</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Skills:\n  # Extra damage to undead mobs\n  - damage{amount=2*&lt;skill.var.enchant_level&gt;} @target ~onAttack ?entitytype{type=ZOMBIE,SKELETON}\n  - potion{p=WEAKNESS;d=100;l=&lt;skill.var.enchant_level&gt;} @target ~onAttack ?entitytype{type=HUSK} ?!mmType{t=SuperHusk,HuskFriend}</code></pre>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>\n  # The item repairs itself when hitting metal enemies, using the MythicCrucible item-skill mechanic for durability.\n  - readucedurability{a=-3} @self ~onAttack ?entitytype{type=IRON_GOLEM} ?itemUsedDurability{damage=&gt;0}</code></pre>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  # Requires 50+ levels to gain bonus drops. \n  - dropitem{i=DIAMOND} @triggerlocation ~onKill ?hasExperience{unit=LEVELS;amount=&gt;50}</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/Conditions"},"enchants:conditions/custombir":{"h":"<h2>Custom Block In Range</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Checks whether Nexo, MythicCrucible, and/or ItemsAdder custom blocks are present within enchanting-table range, using the same scan pattern uses (vanilla&#x27;s 30-cell bookshelf layout, or a chebyshev-cuboid radius). Intended for the <code>Enchanting.Conditions</code> block of an enchantment definition — it evaluates against the enchanting table&#x27;s block location, not the caster.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Addon</code></td><td><code>a</code>, <code>source</code></td><td>Restrict matching to one addon</td><td><i>(any addon)</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>BlockTypes</code></td><td><code>bt</code>, <code>id</code>, <code>ids</code></td><td>Comma-separated <code>nexo:&lt;id&gt;</code> / <code>crucible:&lt;id&gt;</code> / <code>itemsadder:&lt;id&gt;</code> entries. Each entry is checked independently against <code>Count</code> — <code>Require=all</code> means every listed id must independently reach <code>Count</code> somewhere in range, not that a single block matches all of them</td><td><i>(any custom block)</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>Require</code></td><td><code>mode</code></td><td><code>all</code> — every <code>BlockTypes</code> entry must reach <code>Count</code>; <code>any</code> — at least one must. Ignored when <code>BlockTypes</code> is empty</td><td><code>all</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>Count</code></td><td><code>c</code>, <code>min</code>, <code>amount</code></td><td>Minimum number of matching blocks required. Values below 1 are treated as 1</td><td><code>1</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>Radius</code></td><td><code>r</code></td><td>Chebyshev radius (XZ) of the scan. <code>0</code> uses the vanilla 30-cell bookshelf pattern instead of a cuboid</td><td><code>0</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>Los</code></td><td><code>lineofsight</code></td><td>Whether an air gap is required between the table and each candidate block (vanilla&#x27;s line-of-sight rule)</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Addon</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Nexo</code></td><td></td><td>Only Nexo custom blocks</td></tr><tr><td><code>Crucible</code></td><td><code>MythicCrucible</code></td><td>Only MythicCrucible custom blocks</td></tr><tr><td><code>ItemsAdder</code></td><td></td><td>Only ItemsAdder custom blocks</td></tr><tr><td><i>(empty)</i></td><td></td><td>Any of the three addons</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># A specific Crucible ore must be nearby, scanning a 3-block cuboid radius\ncustom_ore_sense:\n  Enchanting:\n    Conditions:\n    - custombir{bt=crucible:sapphire_ore;radius=3}\n\n# Requires at least 3 of a specific Nexo ore nearby (not just one)\ndeep_vein_bonus:\n  Enchanting:\n    Conditions:\n    - custombir{bt=nexo:ruby_ore;count=3}\n\n# Either of two Nexo blocks satisfies it, and only ItemsAdder blocks count otherwise\nmixed_source:\n  Enchanting:\n    Conditions:\n    - custombir{bt=nexo:ruby_ore,nexo:sapphire_ore;require=any}\n    - custombir{addon=itemsadder}</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>custombir</code></li><li><code>cbr</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/custombir"},"enchants:conditions/customblock":{"h":"<h4><code>?customblock</code> Condition</h4>\n<p>A standalone MythicMobs condition (aliases: <code>?custblock</code>, <code>?iscustomblock</code>) for gating <i>any</i> mechanic — not just the drop mechanics above — on whether the current block-break&#x27;s block is a custom block. Reads from the same <code>BlockBreakEvent</code> context as <code>blockdrops</code>/<code>veinminer</code>/etc., so it only evaluates meaningfully inside a <code>~onBlockBreak</code>/<code>~onCustomBlockBreak</code>/<code>~onStartdestroyblock</code> skill line.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>addon</code></td><td><code>a</code>, <code>source</code></td><td>Restrict to one addon: <code>nexo</code>, <code>crucible</code>, or <code>itemsadder</code>.</td><td><code>&quot;&quot;</code> (any addon)</td></tr><tr><td><code>blocktypes</code></td><td><code>bt</code>, <code>id</code>, <code>ids</code></td><td>Comma-separated <code>nexo:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>crucible:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>itemsadder:&lt;id&gt;</code> entries — matches a specific custom block by id, same syntax as <code>blockdrops{bt=...}</code>.</td><td><code>&quot;&quot;</code> (any custom block)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Any custom block, any addon\n- particle{p=totem;a=10} @self ~onBlockBreak ?customblock\n\n# Only Nexo custom blocks\n- sound{s=block.amethyst_block.chime} @self ~onBlockBreak ?customblock{addon=nexo}\n\n# A specific MythicCrucible ore\n- effect:message{m=&quot;&lt;gold&gt;You struck sapphire!&quot;} @self ~onBlockBreak ?customblock{bt=crucible:sapphire_ore}</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/customblock"},"enchants:conditions/hasexperience":{"h":"<hr>\n<p>title: HasExperience</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Has Enchantment</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Checks total XP orb points using the same accurate math as the <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/experience\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/Experience\">ExperienceMechanic</a>.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Unit</code></td><td><code>u</code></td><td>The Type of experience to check</td><td>POINTS</td></tr><tr><td><code>Amount</code></td><td><code>a</code>,</td><td>Range of experience to check</td><td><i>REQUIRED</i></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Unit</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Points</code></td><td><code>Point</code></td><td>Operates in absolute total XP points. Conversions use the real vanilla XP curve, so <code>REMOVE</code> rolls a player down into the previous level&#x27;s bar (e.g. 30 points = lvl 3 with 3/13 bar; <code>REMOVE 5</code> → 25 points = lvl 2 with 9/11 bar, not lvl 3 with an empty bar)</td></tr><tr><td><code>Levels</code></td><td><code>Level</code></td><td>Operates on whole levels, preserving the current bar progress</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Steals experience points based on Enchantment Level\nswiper:\n  Cooldown: 3\n  TriggerConditions:\n  - isPlayer\n  - hasExperience{unit=POINTS;amount=&gt;&lt;math.enchant_level*10+5&gt;}\n  Skills:\n  - experience{mode=REMOVE;unit=POINTS;amount=&lt;math.enchant_level*10+5&gt;}\n  - experience{mode=ADD;unit=POINTS;amount=&lt;math.enchant_level*10+5&gt;} @self\n\n# Deals damage to players who have more than 30 exp levels\nswiper_damage:\n  TriggerConditions:\n  - isPlayer\n  - hasExperience{unit=LEVELS;amount=&gt;30}\n  Skills:\n  - damage{a=10}</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>hasxp</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/HasExperience"},"enchants:conditions/hasmythicenchant":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Evaluates if the target item/slot has a specific enchantment managed by MythicEnchants (which includes custom and vanilla enchantments unless otherwise configured).</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>id</code></td><td><code>enchant</code>, <code>enchantment</code>, <code>e</code></td><td>The Enchantment ID to look for</td><td><i>REQUIRED</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>level</code></td><td><code>lvl</code>, <code>l</code></td><td>The enchantment level(s) to look for, accepts ranges</td><td>&gt;0</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The item slot to evaluate instead of the casting item</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>LunarEnchantCheck:\n  TriggerConditions:\n  - hasMythicEnchant{id=LUNAR_LIGHT;slot=HELMET} true # Checks if the triggering player is wearing helmet enchanted with Lunar Light of any level\n  - hasMythicEnchant{e=LUNAR_LEAPING;slot=LEGS;l=2to3} true # Checks if the trigger player is wearing leggings with the Lunar Leaping enchantment of at level 2 or 3\n  - hasEnch{enchant=SOLAR_SHIELD;s=CHEST} castInstead SolarEnchantDecline # Denies the skill if the triggering player is wearing a chestplate with the Solar Shield enchantment\n  Skills:\n  - message{m=&quot;You truly are blessed by the moon herself!&quot;} @trigger\nSolarEnchantDecline:\n  Skills:\n  - message{m=&quot;Your armor shines too brightly for the moonlight to assist you.&quot;} @trigger</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>MythicEnchants</code></li><li><code>hasMythicEnchantment</code></li><li><code>hasEnch</code>  [⚠️shorthand distinguishes this from Mythic&#x27;s vanilla-only condition <code>hasEnchant</code>]</li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/hasMythicEnchant"},"enchants:conditions/itemdurability":{"h":"<h2>Item Durability</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Evaluates the remaining durability available on the enchanted item. Returns the number of durability points left before the item breaks.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>value</code></td><td><code>v</code>, <code>amount</code>, <code>a</code></td><td>Remaining durability to check against</td><td><code>&gt;0</code> (has durability)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The equipment slot to evaluate</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Value Formats</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exact</td><td>Matches exact remaining durability</td><td><code>100</code></td></tr><tr><td>Range</td><td>Matches a durability range (inclusive)</td><td><code>50to100</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater than</td><td>More than N durability remaining</td><td><code>&gt;50</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater or equal</td><td>At least N durability remaining</td><td><code>&gt;=100</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less than</td><td>Fewer than N durability remaining</td><td><code>&lt;10</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less or equal</td><td>At most N durability remaining</td><td><code>&lt;=50</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Warn when item is about to break\nLowDurabilityWarning:\n  Skills:\n  - message{msg=&quot;&amp;cYour weapon is about to break!&quot;} @self ?itemdurability{value=&lt;10} ~onAttack\n\n# Bonus damage at full durability\nPristineStrike:\n  Skills:\n  - damage{a=&lt;math:enchant_level*2&gt;} @trigger ?itemdurability{value=&gt;=250;slot=HAND} ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>durability</code></li><li><code>remainingdurability</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/itemDurability"},"enchants:conditions/itemdurabilitypercent":{"h":"<h2>Item Durability Percent</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Evaluates the remaining durability percentage on the enchanted item. Returns a value from 0 to 100, where 100 means full durability and 0 means about to break.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>value</code></td><td><code>v</code>, <code>amount</code>, <code>a</code></td><td>Remaining durability percentage to check against (0–100)</td><td><code>&gt;0</code> (has durability)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The equipment slot to evaluate</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Value Formats</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exact</td><td>Matches exact percentage</td><td><code>50</code></td></tr><tr><td>Range</td><td>Matches a percentage range (inclusive)</td><td><code>25to75</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater than</td><td>More than N% remaining</td><td><code>&gt;50</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater or equal</td><td>At least N% remaining</td><td><code>&gt;=25</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less than</td><td>Less than N% remaining</td><td><code>&lt;10</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less or equal</td><td>At most N% remaining</td><td><code>&lt;=50</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Warn when below 10% durability\nCriticalDurability:\n  Skills:\n  - message{msg=&quot;&amp;4&amp;lItem critically damaged!&quot;} @self ?itemdurabilitypercent{value=&lt;10} ~onItem_damage\n\n# Bonus effect when item is above 90%\nWellMaintained:\n  Skills:\n  - potion{t=HASTE;d=40;l=1} @self ?itemdurabilitypercent{value=&gt;=90} ~onBlock_break\n\n# Desperate power when item is nearly broken\nLastStand:\n  Skills:\n  - damage{a=&lt;math:enchant_level*5&gt;} @trigger ?itemdurabilitypercent{value=&lt;25} ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>durabilitypercent</code></li><li><code>durabilitypercentage</code></li><li><code>durabilitypct</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/itemDurabilityPercent"},"enchants:conditions/itemuseddurability":{"h":"<h2>Item Used Durability</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Evaluates the amount of lost durability on the enchanted item. Returns the number of durability points that have been consumed (damage dealt to the item).</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>value</code></td><td><code>v</code>, <code>amount</code>, <code>a</code></td><td>Used durability to check against</td><td><code>&gt;0</code> (has taken damage)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The equipment slot to evaluate</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Value Formats</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exact</td><td>Matches exact used durability</td><td><code>50</code></td></tr><tr><td>Range</td><td>Matches a used durability range (inclusive)</td><td><code>10to50</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater than</td><td>More than N durability used</td><td><code>&gt;100</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater or equal</td><td>At least N durability used</td><td><code>&gt;=50</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less than</td><td>Fewer than N durability used</td><td><code>&lt;10</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less or equal</td><td>At most N durability used</td><td><code>&lt;=25</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Power scales with wear\nBattleHardened:\n  Skills:\n  - damage{a=&lt;math:enchant_level*3&gt;} @trigger ?itemuseddurability{value=&gt;=100} ~onAttack\n\n# Only trigger on pristine items (no durability used)\nMintCondition:\n  Skills:\n  - particles{p=happy_villager} @self ?itemuseddurability{value=0} ~onEquip</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>useddurability</code></li><li><code>lostdurability</code></li><li><code>itemdamaged</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/itemUsedDurability"},"enchants:conditions/lethalcheck":{"h":"<h2>Lethal Check</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Evaluates whether the current damage event would kill the target entity. Returns true when the incoming damage exceeds the target&#x27;s current health plus absorption. Can optionally account for Totem of Undying protection.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>checktotems</code></td><td><code>ct</code>, <code>totemsafe</code>, <code>totemcheck</code></td><td>Whether to check if the target has a Totem of Undying before determining lethality</td><td>true</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote><p>When <code>checktotems</code> is true and the target is holding a Totem of Undying, the condition returns false (damage is not considered lethal since the totem would save them).</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Only trigger soulbound on actual lethal hits\nSoulbound:\n  Skills:\n  - recoveritem{} @trigger ?lethalcheck ~onDamaged\n\n# Execute effect on killing blow (ignore totem protection)\nExecutionStrike:\n  Skills:\n  - particles{p=soul_fire_flame} @self ?lethalcheck{checktotems=false} ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>islethal</code></li><li><code>wouldkill</code></li><li><code>lethal</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/lethalcheck"},"enchants:conditions/mench":{"h":"<h2>Has Enchantment</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Checks whether a player&#x27;s item slot has a specific enchantment at the given level. Supports vanilla, datapack, and MythicEnchants custom enchantments. When slot is <code>TRIGGER</code>, it scopes the condition to the enchanted item that fired the skill, with fallback to mainhand.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>id</code></td><td><code>enchant</code>, <code>enchantment</code>, <code>e</code></td><td>The enchantment ID to check (namespaced or bare)</td><td><i>REQUIRED</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>level</code></td><td><code>lvl</code>, <code>l</code></td><td>Level or range to match</td><td><code>&gt;0</code> (any level)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The equipment slot to evaluate</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Level Formats</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exact</td><td>Matches a specific level</td><td><code>2</code></td></tr><tr><td>Range</td><td>Matches a level range (inclusive)</td><td><code>2to3</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater than</td><td>Matches levels above a value</td><td><code>&gt;1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater or equal</td><td>Matches levels at or above a value</td><td><code>&gt;=2</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less than</td><td>Matches levels below a value</td><td><code>&lt;4</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less or equal</td><td>Matches levels at or below a value</td><td><code>&lt;=4</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>ConditionalSharpness:\n  Skills:\n  - damage{a=5} @trigger ?mench{id=SHARPNESS;level=&gt;=3} ~onAttack\n\n# Check for any level of Fire Aspect\nFireStrike:\n  Skills:\n  - ignite{ticks=60} @trigger ?mench{id=FIRE_ASPECT} ~onAttack\n\n# Check specific slot\nArmorCheck:\n  Skills:\n  - heal{a=2} @self ?mench{id=PROTECTION;level=4;slot=CHEST} ~onDamaged</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>enchant</code></li><li><code>enchantment</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/mench"},"enchants:conditions/soulbounduses":{"h":"<h2>Check Recover Item</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Checks the remaining <code>recoveritem</code> uses/charges on the trigger item. Used to conditionally execute skills based on how many soulbound charges remain.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>uses</code></td><td><code>u</code>, <code>charges</code>, <code>c</code>, <code>value</code>, <code>v</code></td><td>Remaining uses to check against</td><td><code>&gt;0</code> (has charges)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The equipment slot to check</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Uses Formats</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exact</td><td>Matches exact remaining uses</td><td><code>3</code></td></tr><tr><td>Range</td><td>Matches a range (inclusive)</td><td><code>2to5</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater than</td><td>More than N uses remaining</td><td><code>&gt;1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater or equal</td><td>At least N uses remaining</td><td><code>&gt;=3</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less than</td><td>Fewer than N uses remaining</td><td><code>&lt;1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less or equal</td><td>At most N uses remaining</td><td><code>&lt;=2</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>SoulboundWarning:\n  Skills:\n  - message{m=&quot;&amp;cOnly 1 soulbound charge left!&quot;} @self ?checkrecoveritem{uses=1} ~onDamaged\n\nLowCharges:\n  Skills:\n  - particles{p=soul} @self ?checkrecoveritem{uses=&lt;=2} ~onTimer:40</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>recoveruses</code></li><li><code>soulbounduses</code></li><li><code>recovercharges</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/soulbounduses"},"enchants:triggers/onapply":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>When the enchantment is applied to an item.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Trigger may only be utilized within the Skill configuration of an enchantment.\\</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<p>📝 <code>CONFIG.YML SNIPPET</code></p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onApply"},"enchants:triggers/onbowmiss":{"h":"<p>When the enchantment&#x27;s wielder&#x27;s arrow hits a block or misses entirely</p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onbowmiss"},"enchants:triggers/onenchant":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>When the enchantment&#x27;s wielder enchants via the vanilla enchanting table.</p>\n<blockquote><p>If using <a href=\"https://mythiccraft.io/index.php?resources/crucible-custom-items-armor-furniture-blocks-more.2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicCrucible</a>, MythicEnchants also enables this trigger within item Skills.\\ This trigger may also be utilized within player skills powered by <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/mythicrpg/-/wikis/Skills/Triggers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicRPG</a></p></blockquote>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<p>📝 <code>CONFIG.YML SNIPPET</code></p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onEnchant"},"enchants:triggers/onremove":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>When the enchantment is removed from an item.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Trigger may only be utilized within the Skill configuration of an enchantment.\\</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<p>📝 <code>CONFIG.YML SNIPPET</code></p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onRemove"},"enchants:triggers/onshieldblock":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>When the enchantment&#x27;s wielder blocks an attack with a shield.</p>\n<blockquote><p>If using <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/mythiccrucible/-/wikis/Skills/Triggers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicCrucible</a>, MythicEnchants also enables this trigger within item Skills.\\ This trigger may also be utilized within player skills powered by <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/mythicrpg/-/wikis/Skills/Triggers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicRPG</a></p></blockquote>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  # Enchantment Skill. Reflects 50% of blocked damage back at the attacker!\n  - skill{s=shieldreflect;sync=true} @self ~onShieldBlock\n\nshieldreflect:\n  Skills:\n  - damage{a=&lt;trigger.damage*0.5&gt;} @trigger\n  - particle{particle=BLOCK_CRACK;material=IRON_BLOCK;amount=10}</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>onShieldBlock</code></li><li><code>onBlock</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onShieldBlock"},"enchants:triggers/ontrample":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>When the enchantment&#x27;s wielder Tramples farmland or turtle eggs.</p>\n<blockquote><p>If using <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/mythiccrucible/-/wikis/Skills/Triggers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicCrucible</a>, MythicEnchants also enables this trigger within item Skills.\\ This trigger may also be utilized within player skills powered by <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/mythicrpg/-/wikis/Skills/Triggers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicRPG</a></p></blockquote>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  # Enchantment Skill. Has a 50% chance to cancel the trample event!\n  - skill{s=canceltrample;sync=true} @self ~onTrample 0.5\n\ncanceltrample:\n  Skills:\n  - cancelevent\n  - particle{particle=CLOUD;amount=5}</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>onTrampleFarmland</code></li><li><code>onTrampleEgg</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onTrample"},"enchants:triggers/triggers":{"h":"<p>The Mythic-ecosystem triggers MythicEnchants provides.  These expand on <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/Triggers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicMob Triggers</a>, which typically may be used as expected within enchantment skills.</p>\n<p>These registered triggers may be used outside of enchantments as well in some place.  Check specific triggers for details on their usage scope.</p>\n<blockquote><p><a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/mythiccrucible/-/wikis/Skills/Triggers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicCrucible</a> grants extensive item-related triggers, but many are redundant from base MythicMobs and already provided from it directly.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Enchantment Triggers</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Trigger</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"triggers/onapply\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onApply\"><code>~onApply</code></a></td><td>When the enchantment is added to an item</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"triggers/onremove\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onRemove\"><code>~onRemove</code></a></td><td>When the enchantment is removed from an item</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"triggers/onenchant\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onEnchant\"><code>~onEnchant</code></a></td><td>When the enchantment&#x27;s wielder enchants via the vanilla enchanting table</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Player Triggers</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Trigger</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"triggers/ontrample\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onTrample\"><code>~onTrample</code></a></td><td>When the enchantment detects when farmland and turtle eggs have been trampled</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"triggers/onshieldblock\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onShieldBlock\"><code>~onShieldBlock</code></a></td><td>When the enchantment&#x27;s wielder blocks an attack with a shield.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Proj Triggers</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Trigger</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"triggers/onbowmiss\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onbowmiss\"><code>~onBowMiss</code></a></td><td>When the enchantment&#x27;s wielder&#x27;s arrow hits a block or misses entirely</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<p>📝 <code>CONFIG.YML SNIPPET</code></p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/Triggers"},"enchants:placeholders/enchant-description":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>The description of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>Will return the STRING description text of the triggering enchantment, as defined by its <code>Description:</code> field.</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>EnchantUse:\n  Skills:\n  # An enchantment triggering this EnchantUse meta-skill will show some info about itself to its user.\n  - message{msg=&quot;&lt;trigger.name&gt; has activated their &lt;skill.var.enchant-name&gt;! &lt;skill.var.enchant-description&gt;&quot;} @self</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_description&gt;</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Description"},"enchants:placeholders/enchant-id":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>The internal ID of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>Will return the STRING internal ID of the triggering enchantment.</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>EnchantUse:\n  Skills:\n  # An enchantment triggering this EnchantUse meta-skill will show some info about itself to its user.\n  - message{msg=&quot;The &lt;skill.var.enchant-name&gt; &lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt; enchantment was activated, as configured in the &lt;skill.var.enchant-id&gt; config!&quot;} @self</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_id&gt;</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-ID"},"enchants:placeholders/enchant-level":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>The level of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>Will return the INTEGER value of the enchantment level.</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>EnchantUse:\n  Skills:\n  # An enchantment triggering this EnchantUse meta-skill will show some info about itself to its user.\n  - message{msg=&quot;&lt;trigger.name&gt; has activated their &lt;skill.var.enchant-name&gt; &lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt; enchantment!&quot;} @self</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_level&gt;</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Level"},"enchants:placeholders/enchant-maxlevel":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>The maximum allowed level of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>Will return the INTEGER value of the enchantment&#x27;s maximum possible level (regardless of its current level on trigger).</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>EnchantUse:\n  Skills:\n  # An enchantment triggering this EnchantUse meta-skill will show some info about itself to its user.\n  - message{msg=&quot;The &lt;skill.var.enchant-name&gt; of &lt;trigger.name&gt; is Lvl &lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt; out of Max &lt;skill.var.enchant-maxlevel&gt;&quot;} @self</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_maxlevel&gt;</code></li><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-maxlvl&gt;</code></li><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_maxlvl&gt;</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-MaxLevel"},"enchants:placeholders/enchant-name":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>The display name of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>Will return the STRING display name (with formatting and color) of the triggering enchantment.</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>EnchantUse:\n  Skills:\n  # An enchantment triggering this EnchantUse meta-skill will show some info about itself to its user.\n  - message{msg=&quot;&lt;trigger.name&gt; has activated their &lt;skill.var.enchant-name&gt; &lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt; enchantment!&quot;} @self</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_name&gt;</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Name"},"enchants:placeholders/enchant-rarity":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>The STRING tier of enchantment rarity of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>Will return the STRING value of the enchantment rarity.</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>EnchantUse:\n  Skills:\n  # An enchantment triggering this EnchantUse meta-skill will show some info about itself to its user.\n  - message{msg=&quot;&lt;trigger.name&gt; has activated their &lt;skill.var.enchant-rarity&gt; enchantment, &lt;skill.var.enchant-name&gt; &lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt;!&quot;} @self</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_rarity&gt;</code></li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Rarity"},"enchants:placeholders/enchant-totallevel":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>The summed level of the triggering enchantment across every one of the caster&#x27;s equipped slots (hand, off-hand, head, chest, legs, feet).</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>Will return the INT total of all levels of the triggering enchantment currently worn by the caster — e.g. four armor pieces each carrying level 3 of the enchantment returns <code>12</code>, not <code>3</code>.</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>EnchantUse:\n  Skills:\n  # An enchantment with the same ID on multiple worn pieces scales its effect off the combined total, firing once rather than once per piece.\n  - damage{a=&lt;skill.var.enchant-total-levels&gt;} @target ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_total_levels&gt;</code> for it</li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-TotalLevel"},"enchants:placeholders/papi-placeholders":{"h":"<h3>PlaceholderAPI Placeholders</h3>\n<p>When <a href=\"https://www.spigotmc.org/resources/placeholderapi.6245/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">PlaceholderAPI</a> is installed, MythicEnchants registers the following PAPI placeholders:</p>\n<h3>PlaceholderAPI</h3>\n<p>Registered under both <code>%mythicenchants_...%</code> and <code>%mench_...%</code></p>\n<h4>Global</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>total</code></td><td>Total registered enchantment count</td></tr><tr><td><code>enchseed</code></td><td>Current enchanting seed for the placeholder&#x27;s player</td></tr><tr><td><code>enchseed_pin</code></td><td>Currently pinned enchantment id for the placeholder&#x27;s player</td></tr><tr><td><code>enchant_name_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Display name of enchant <code>&lt;id&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>enchant_description_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Description of enchant <code>&lt;id&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>enchant_rarity_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Rarity enum name</td></tr><tr><td><code>enchant_rarity_color_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Rarity color hex string</td></tr><tr><td><code>enchant_rarity_display_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Colored rarity display name</td></tr><tr><td><code>enchant_total_level_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Colored rarity display name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Slot-based (<code>&lt;slot&gt;_...</code>)</h4>\n<p>Slots: <code>mainhand</code>/<code>hand</code>, <code>offhand</code>, <code>head</code>/<code>helm</code>, <code>chest</code>, <code>legs</code>, <code>feet</code>/<code>boots</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_total</code> / <code>&lt;slot&gt;_enchant_count</code></td><td>Number of enchantments on that slot&#x27;s item</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_enchants</code></td><td>Comma-joined list of enchant IDs on that slot&#x27;s item</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_has_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td><code>true</code>/<code>false</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_level_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Level of enchant <code>&lt;id&gt;</code> on that slot (<code>0</code> if absent)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_enchant_&lt;n&gt;</code></td><td>Enchant ID at index <code>&lt;n&gt;</code> (1-indexed)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_enchant_&lt;n&gt;_name</code></td><td>Display name of the enchant at index <code>&lt;n&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_enchant_&lt;n&gt;_level</code></td><td>Level of the enchant at index <code>&lt;n&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_enchant_&lt;n&gt;_description</code> / <code>_desc</code></td><td>Description of the enchant at index <code>&lt;n&gt;</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Example: <code>%mythicenchants_hand_enchant_1_name%</code>, <code>%mench_helm_has_minecraft:protection%</code></p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/PAPI-Placeholders"},"enchants:placeholders/placeholders":{"h":"<h2>Placeholders</h2>\n<p>The Mythic-ecosystem placeholders MythicEnchants provides.  These expand on <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/Placeholders\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicMob Placeholders</a>, which typically may be used as expected within enchantment skills, including in-line condition evaluations.</p>\n<p>Some Mythic triggers contain <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/Placeholders#variable-placeholders\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Integrated Placeholders</a> to provide additional functionality, such as <code>&lt;skill.var.damage-amount&gt;</code> from attack and damage events to evaluate the damage delivered.  Many in-line placeholder usage, especially with variables, require <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Premium-Features\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mythic Premium</a>.</p>\n<p>These registered placeholders may be used outside of enchantments as well, such as a mob&#x27;s skills evaluating a player&#x27;s item for enchantments or durability.</p>\n<blockquote><p><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"info/dependencies\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Info/Dependencies\">MythicCrucible</a> also grants item-related placeholders!</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote><p>All variables support both dash (<code>-</code>) and underscore (<code>_</code>) separators interchangeably.\\ e.g. <code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_level&gt;</code> are equivalent.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Enchantment Placeholders</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-id\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-ID\"><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-id&gt;</code></a></td><td>STRING</td><td>The ID of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-rarity\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Rarity\"><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-rarity&gt;</code></a></td><td>STRING</td><td>The rarity of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-name\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Name\"><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-name&gt;</code></a></td><td>STRING</td><td>The display name of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-description\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Description\"><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-description&gt;</code></a></td><td>STRING</td><td>The description of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-level\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Level\"><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt;</code></a></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>The level of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-maxlevel\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-MaxLevel\"><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-maxlevel&gt;</code></a></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>The maximum level of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-totallevel\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-TotalLevel\"><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-total-levels&gt;</code></a></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>Will return the INT total of all levels of the triggering enchantment currently worn</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote><p><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-*&gt;</code> placeholders only reflect the <b>currently firing</b> enchantment&#x27;s trigger context. To look up a specific enchantment by ID (any enchantment, not just the one that triggered the skill), use the <code>&lt;enchant.ID.field&gt;</code> placeholders below instead.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Enchant Definition Placeholders</h3>\n<p>Look up any registered enchantment&#x27;s definition data by ID — independent of any trigger context, usable anywhere a MythicMobs placeholder is valid.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.ID.name&gt;</code></td><td>STRING</td><td>Display name of enchantment <code>ID</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.ID.description&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;enchant.ID.desc&gt;</code></td><td>STRING</td><td>Description of enchantment <code>ID</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.ID.maxlvl&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;enchant.ID.maxlevel&gt;</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>Maximum level of enchantment <code>ID</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.ID.minlvl&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;enchant.ID.minlevel&gt;</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>Minimum level of enchantment <code>ID</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.ID.rarity&gt;</code></td><td>STRING</td><td>Rarity enum name of enchantment <code>ID</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.ID.totallevel&gt;</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>Will return the INT total of all levels of the named enchantment currently worn by the placeholder&#x27;s entity`</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><code>ID</code> may be a bare key (resolved against the plugin&#x27;s default namespace, then tried raw) or a fully-qualified <code>namespace:key</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>- message{msg=&quot;&lt;trigger.name&gt;&#x27;s target has &lt;enchant.frost_bite.name&gt;: &lt;enchant.frost_bite.description&gt;&quot;} @self</code></pre>\n<h4>Slot-Aware Enchant Placeholders</h4>\n<p>Reads the enchantment&#x27;s level directly off the placeholder context entity&#x27;s equipped item for a given slot — works for any enchantment ID, not just the one that triggered the skill.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.SLOT.ID.level&gt;</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>Level of enchantment <code>ID</code> on the entity&#x27;s <code>SLOT</code> item (<code>0</code> if absent)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.SLOT.ID.has&gt;</code></td><td>BOOLEAN</td><td>Whether the entity&#x27;s <code>SLOT</code> item has enchantment <code>ID</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Valid <code>SLOT</code> values: <code>mainhand</code>/<code>hand</code>, <code>offhand</code>, <code>head</code>/<code>helm</code>/<code>helmet</code>, <code>chest</code>/<code>chestplate</code>, <code>legs</code>/<code>leggings</code>, <code>feet</code>/<code>boots</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>- message{msg=&quot;You have Frost Bite &lt;enchant.mainhand.frost_bite.level&gt; on your weapon!&quot;} @self ?enchant.mainhand.frost_bite.has</code></pre>\n<h3>Bookshelves Placeholders</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Returns</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;caster.var.menchbookshelves&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>The scanned <b>table power</b> — the same <code>count</code> the table feeds into its slot equations. Uses the config&#x27;s scan shape. Uncapped by design (caps live at the slot level)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;bookshelves.radial.4&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>Table power, but scanning a chebyshev ring <code>1..4</code> (Y <code>0..1</code>) instead of the config shape</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;bookshelves.radial.2.5&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>Table power, chebyshev ring <code>inner=2..outer=5</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;bookshelves.cuboid.3&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>Table power, full cube radius <code>3</code> (every <code>dx, dy, dz</code> in <code>-3..3</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;bookshelves.slot.1&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>Slot 1&#x27;s <b>capped base level</b>: slot equation (<code>count</code> = power) → per-slot <code>slot-cap</code> → <code>max-base-level</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;bookshelves.slot.2&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>Slot 2&#x27;s capped base level</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;bookshelves.slot.3&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>Slot 3&#x27;s capped base level</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;bookshelves.radial.4.slot.2&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>Slot 2&#x27;s base level computed from the radial-4 scan</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Caster Placeholders</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.player-health&gt;</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td>The wielder&#x27;s current health</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.player-max-health&gt;</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td>The wielder&#x27;s maximum health</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.fall-distance&gt;</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td>The wielder&#x27;s current accumulated fall distance in blocks</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Target Placeholders</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.target-health&gt;</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td>The skill target&#x27;s current health (when a target entity is present)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.target-max-health&gt;</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td>The skill target&#x27;s maximum health (when a target entity is present)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Trigger-Specific Placeholders</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Trigger(s)</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.damage&gt;</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td><code>~onDamaged</code></td><td>The incoming damage amount from the current damage event</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.item-attack&gt;</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td><code>~onAttack</code></td><td>The equipment&#x27;s attack damage value</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.equip-slot&gt;</code></td><td>STRING</td><td>Most triggers</td><td>The equipment slot of the enchanted item (e.g. <code>HAND</code>, <code>CHEST</code>, <code>FEET</code>)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Enchant Apply/Remove Trigger Placeholders</h3>\n<p>These are injected only during <code>~onEnchantApply</code> and <code>~onEnchantRemove</code> triggers:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.enchantments-applied&gt;</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>Number of enchantments applied (<code>~onEnchantApply</code> only)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.enchantments-removed&gt;</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>Number of enchantments removed (<code>~onEnchantRemove</code> only)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.enchantments&gt;</code></td><td>STRING</td><td>Comma-separated list of enchantment IDs applied or removed</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.enchantment-source&gt;</code></td><td>STRING</td><td>Source of the enchantment change: <code>TABLE</code>, <code>ANVIL</code>, <code>COMMAND</code>, or <code>GRINDSTONE</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.enchantment_applied.N&gt;</code></td><td>STRING</td><td>The Nth enchantment ID in the change (1-based index)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Math Expressions</h3>\n<p>MythicEnchants provides a <code>&lt;math:EXPR&gt;</code> placeholder for evaluating math expressions inline. Any of the above variables can be referenced inside math expressions using their underscore form.</p>\n<h4>Syntax</h4>\n<p>Enchantment File:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>&lt;math:EXPRESSION&gt;</code></pre>\n<p>Metaskill or Skills File (Requires MM Premium):</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>&lt;math.EXPRESSION&gt;</code></pre>\n<h4>Available Variables in Math</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>enchant_level</code></td><td>Level of the triggering enchantment</td></tr><tr><td><code>enchant_maxlevel</code></td><td>Maximum level of the triggering enchantment</td></tr><tr><td><code>player_health</code></td><td>Caster&#x27;s current health</td></tr><tr><td><code>player_max_health</code></td><td>Caster&#x27;s maximum health</td></tr><tr><td><code>fall_distance</code></td><td>Caster&#x27;s accumulated fall distance in blocks</td></tr><tr><td><code>target_health</code></td><td>Target&#x27;s current health (0 if no target)</td></tr><tr><td><code>target_max_health</code></td><td>Target&#x27;s maximum health (0 if no target)</td></tr><tr><td><code>damage</code></td><td>Incoming/outgoing damage value (0 if not applicable)</td></tr><tr><td><code>item_attack</code></td><td>Item attack value (0 if not applicable)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Supported Functions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Function</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>min(a, b)</code></td><td>Returns the smaller of two values</td></tr><tr><td><code>max(a, b)</code></td><td>Returns the larger of two values</td></tr><tr><td><code>clamp(v, min, max)</code></td><td>Clamps a value between min and max</td></tr><tr><td><code>round(x)</code></td><td>Rounds to the nearest integer</td></tr><tr><td><code>floor(x)</code></td><td>Rounds down to the nearest integer</td></tr><tr><td><code>ceil(x)</code></td><td>Rounds up to the nearest integer</td></tr><tr><td><code>abs(x)</code></td><td>Returns the absolute value</td></tr><tr><td><code>sqrt(x)</code></td><td>Square root</td></tr><tr><td><code>random(min, max)</code></td><td>Random float between min and max</td></tr><tr><td><code>randomInt(min, max)</code></td><td>Random integer between min and max (inclusive)</td></tr><tr><td><code>lerp(a, b, t)</code></td><td>Linear interpolation between a and b by factor t</td></tr><tr><td><code>step(edge, x)</code></td><td>Returns 1 if x &gt;= edge, otherwise 0</td></tr><tr><td><code>sin(x)</code>, <code>cos(x)</code>, <code>tan(x)</code></td><td>Trigonometric functions</td></tr><tr><td><code>log(x)</code>, <code>log2(x)</code>, <code>log10(x)</code></td><td>Logarithmic functions</td></tr><tr><td><code>signum(x)</code></td><td>Returns -1, 0, or 1 based on sign</td></tr><tr><td><code>logb(x, base)</code></td><td>Logarithm with custom base</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Supported Operators</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Operator</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>+</code> <code>-</code> <code>*</code> <code>/</code> <code>^</code></td><td>Standard arithmetic</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;</code> <code>&lt;=</code> <code>&gt;</code> <code>&gt;=</code> <code>==</code></td><td>Comparison (returns 1 or 0)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Placeholders"},"enchants:items/slots":{"h":"<p>The valid slots that can be defined in various skill operations.</p>\n<blockquote><p>These slots correspond to <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/EquipSlot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mythic&#x27;s Slot Operations</a></p></blockquote>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Slot</th><th>Aliases</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>HEAD</td><td>HELMET, HELM, HAT</td></tr><tr><td>CHEST</td><td>CHESTPIECE, CHESTPLATE, BODY</td></tr><tr><td>LEGS</td><td>LEGGINGS, PANTS</td></tr><tr><td>FEET</td><td>BOOTS, SHOES</td></tr><tr><td>HAND</td><td>MAINHAND, WEAPON</td></tr><tr><td>OFFHAND</td><td>SHIELD</td></tr><tr><td>TRIGGER</td><td>ITEM</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote><p><code>TRIGGER</code> is unique to MythicEnchants, and refers to the item that triggered the skill.  This is only usable within MythicEnchant placeholders/skills.</p></blockquote>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots"},"enchants:enchants/attributes":{"h":"<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>The <code>Attributes</code> section is a declarative shorthand for applying item attribute modifiers without writing full skill line syntax. Each entry generates a pair of synthetic skill lines — one on <code>~onEnchant</code> to apply the modifier, and one on <code>~onEnchantRemove</code> to clean it up — equivalent to using <code>enchantitemattribute</code> manually in <code>Skills</code>.</p>\n<p>Attribute modifiers are written directly onto the item&#x27;s metadata, so they persist across sessions, appear in the item tooltip, and stack correctly with the item&#x27;s base attributes.</p>\n<h4>Syntax</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Attributes:\n    &lt;SlotGroup&gt;:\n      - &lt;ATTRIBUTE&gt; &lt;AMOUNT&gt; [OPERATION]</code></pre>\n<p>Each line under a slot group follows this format:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Required</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ATTRIBUTE</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>The attribute name (see <span class=\"ilink\">Attributes</span>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>AMOUNT</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>A numeric value or <code>&lt;math:&gt;</code> expression</td></tr><tr><td><code>OPERATION</code></td><td>No</td><td>The modifier operation (see <span class=\"ilink\">Operations</span>). Defaults to <code>ADD_NUMBER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Example</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Attributes:\n    MainHand:\n      - MAX_HEALTH 4\n      - ATTACK_DAMAGE 2 ADD_NUMBER\n      - ATTACK_DAMAGE &lt;math:enchant_level*0.5&gt; ADD_NUMBER\n    Any:\n      - ARMOR 2\n      - ARMOR_TOUGHNESS 1 ADD_NUMBER</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Slot Groups</h4>\n<p>The slot group key determines which equipment slot the attribute modifier is active in. Accepts any valid <code>EquipmentSlotGroup</code> name (case-insensitive).</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>MainHand</code></td><td>Active when held in the main hand</td></tr><tr><td><code>OffHand</code></td><td>Active when held in the off hand</td></tr><tr><td><code>Head</code></td><td>Active when worn on the head</td></tr><tr><td><code>Chest</code></td><td>Active when worn on the chest</td></tr><tr><td><code>Legs</code></td><td>Active when worn on the legs</td></tr><tr><td><code>Feet</code></td><td>Active when worn on the feet</td></tr><tr><td><code>Armor</code></td><td>Active in any armor slot</td></tr><tr><td><code>Any</code></td><td>Active in any slot</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr>\n<h4>Attribute Names</h4>\n<p>Attributes are resolved against the Minecraft attribute registry. Both the full namespaced form and bare shorthand are accepted. The <code>generic_</code> prefix is stripped automatically, so <code>generic_max_health</code>, <code>max_health</code>, and <code>minecraft:generic.max_health</code> all resolve to the same attribute.</p>\n<p>Common attributes:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>MAX_HEALTH</code></td><td>Maximum health points</td></tr><tr><td><code>ATTACK_DAMAGE</code></td><td>Melee attack damage</td></tr><tr><td><code>ATTACK_SPEED</code></td><td>Attack speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>ATTACK_KNOCKBACK</code></td><td>Knockback applied on hit</td></tr><tr><td><code>ARMOR</code></td><td>Armor points</td></tr><tr><td><code>ARMOR_TOUGHNESS</code></td><td>Armor toughness</td></tr><tr><td><code>KNOCKBACK_RESISTANCE</code></td><td>Resistance to knockback</td></tr><tr><td><code>MOVEMENT_SPEED</code></td><td>Movement speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>FLYING_SPEED</code></td><td>Flying speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>BLOCK_BREAK_SPEED</code></td><td>Block breaking speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>LUCK</code></td><td>Luck</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Any attribute registered in the Minecraft attribute registry can be used. Use the full <code>namespace:key</code> form for modded or non-generic attributes.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Operations</h4>\n<p>Controls how the amount is applied to the base attribute value.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ADD_NUMBER</code></td><td><code>ADD</code>, <code>FLAT</code>, <code>BASE</code></td><td>Adds a flat value to the base</td></tr><tr><td><code>ADD_SCALAR</code></td><td><code>SCALAR</code>, <code>PERCENT</code>, <code>PERCENT_BASE</code></td><td>Multiplies the base by <code>(1 + amount)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>MULTIPLY_SCALAR_1</code></td><td><code>MULTIPLY</code>, <code>PERCENT_TOTAL</code></td><td>Multiplies the total (after all additions) by <code>(1 + amount)</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Defaults to <code>ADD_NUMBER</code> if omitted.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Math Expressions</h4>\n<p>The <code>AMOUNT</code> field supports <code>&lt;math:&gt;</code> expressions, allowing level-scaling modifiers.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Attributes:\n    MainHand:\n      - ATTACK_DAMAGE &lt;math:enchant_level*1.5&gt; ADD_NUMBER\n      - MAX_HEALTH &lt;math:enchant_level*2&gt; ADD_NUMBER</code></pre>\n<p>All standard enchantment variables are available: <code>enchant_level</code>, <code>enchant_maxlevel</code>, etc.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Notes</h4>\n<ul><li>Modifiers are written into the item metadata and visible in the tooltip.</li><li>If the item already has a base modifier for the same attribute, operation, and slot group (e.g. a sword&#x27;s default attack damage), the <code>Attributes</code> system will absorb and combine it rather than duplicating it, then restore the original on removal.</li><li><code>Attributes</code> generates <code>enchantitemattribute</code> skill lines internally. For more advanced control — such as targeting a specific item slot, using <code>SET</code> vs <code>ADD</code> mode, or custom modifier keys — use <code>enchantitemattribute</code> directly in <code>Skills</code> instead.</li></ul>\n<p><code>`</code></p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Attributes"},"enchants:enchants/custom-enchantments":{"h":"<h4>File Locations</h4>\n<p>The primary location custom enchantments are stored is in the <code>/plugins/MythicMobs/enchantments/</code> folder.  Enchantments may also be organized into and loaded from the <code>../enchantments/</code> folder of any <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Packs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mythic Pack</a>.</p>\n<blockquote><p>A typical custom enchantment might be located in <code>/plugins/MythicMobs/enchantments/holy_shine.yml</code>.\\ Enchantment files may include multiple enchantments, such as <code>/plugins/MythicMobs/enchantments/lunar.yml</code> containing the <code>lunar_blessing</code> and <code>lunar_light</code> enchantments.\\ A Mythic Pack location might be <code>/plugins/MythicMobs/packs/lemons_enchants/enchantments/sour_strike.yml</code>, featuring the <code>sour_strike</code> enchantment from the &quot;Lemon&#x27;s Enchants&quot; pack.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Enchantment Elements</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/enchantment-config\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Enchantment-Config\">Complete Enchantment Config</a><ul><li><span class=\"ilink\">Internal Name</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Display Name</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Description</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Min Level</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Max Level</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Rarity</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Anvil Cost</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Tags</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Conflicting Enchantments</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Options</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Valid Slots</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Supported Items</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Primary Items</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Enchanting</span><ul><li><span class=\"ilink\">Weight</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Min &amp; Max Cost</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Promised</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Book Offer</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Reagent</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Conditions</span></li></ul></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Attributes</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Skills</span></li></ul></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Examples</span></li></ul>\n<hr>\n<h3>General Settings</h3>\n<h4>Internal Name</h4>\n<p><b>❗️Required.</b> The internal string identifier for the enchantment. Must be a unique name using valid characters and no spaces. Only visible in configurations.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:</code></pre>\n<blockquote><p>The <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-id\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-ID\"><code>enchant-id</code></a> placeholder returns this value in enchantment skills.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Display Name</h4>\n<p>The visible name of the enchantment, shown in rich text locations.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;</code></pre>\n<blockquote><p>The <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-name\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Name\"><code>enchant-name</code></a> placeholder returns this value, including its colors and formatting, in enchantment skills.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Description</h4>\n<p>An optional description for the enchantment. Used for informational purposes.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Description: &quot;Heals the player on attack.&quot;</code></pre>\n<h4>Min Level</h4>\n<p>The minimum level the enchantment starts at. Defaults to <code>1</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  MinLevel: 1</code></pre>\n<h4>Max Level</h4>\n<p><b>❗️Required.</b> The maximum level the enchantment is permitted to reach. Must be a whole number between 1 and 255.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  MaxLevel: 5</code></pre>\n<blockquote><p>The <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-maxlevel\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-MaxLevel\"><code>enchant-maxlevel</code></a> placeholder returns this integer in enchantment skills.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Rarity</h4>\n<p>The <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"rarities\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Rarities\">rarity tier</a> assigned to the enchantment. Creates groupings beyond weight, such as being able to roll a &quot;RARE&quot; enchantment specifically.\\ Rarities are defined in a <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"rarities\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Rarities\">Rarities</a> file.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Rarity: UNCOMMON</code></pre>\n<blockquote><p>The <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-rarity\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Rarity\"><code>enchant-rarity</code></a> placeholder returns this value in enchantment skills.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Anvil Cost</h4>\n<p>The experience cost associated with the enchantment during anvil operations.\\ Half of this value is used for operations on an enchanted book. This cost is multiplied by the enchantment&#x27;s level.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  AnvilCost: 3</code></pre>\n<h4>Tags</h4>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_tag_(Java_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">enchantment tags</a> assigned to the enchantment. Configures many behaviors such as loot table inclusion, exclusivity groups, and more.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Tags:\n    - minecraft:on_random_loot  # appears in general vanilla chest/mob loot\n    - special_group             # example custom tag for grouping</code></pre>\n<blockquote><p>Unlike other config areas, tags do not require the <code>#minecraft:tag</code> syntax — this field takes plain tag name inputs.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Conflicting Enchantments</h4>\n<p>Enchantments considered mutually exclusive with this enchantment. Accepts all lowercase enchantment IDs or <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_tag_(Java_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">enchantment tags</a>. Must include namespace in enchantment ID.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  ConflictingEnchants:\n    - &#x27;#minecraft:exclusive_set/damage&#x27;\n    - minecraft:mending</code></pre>\n<h4>Options</h4>\n<p>A configuration section for behavioral flags.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Enabled</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Enables or disables the enchantment entirely</td></tr><tr><td><code>Cursed</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Applies the <code>#minecraft:curse</code> tag — red name, prevents removal</td></tr><tr><td><code>Treasure</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Applies the <code>#minecraft:treasure</code> tag</td></tr><tr><td><code>RandomLoot</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Whether this enchantment can appear in random loot</td></tr><tr><td><code>Tradeable</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Whether this enchantment can be traded by villagers</td></tr><tr><td><code>TradedEquipment</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Whether this enchantment can appear on villager-traded equipment</td></tr><tr><td><code>MobSpawnEquipment</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Whether this enchantment can appear on mob spawn equipment</td></tr><tr><td><code>PVP</code></td><td><i>(unset)</i></td><td>Override PVP behavior for this enchantment&#x27;s skills</td></tr><tr><td><code>StrictMythicItems</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Restrict application to only the exact Mythic items listed in <code>PrimaryItems</code> (see <span class=\"ilink\">Primary Items</span>)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    Enabled: true\n    Cursed: false\n    Treasure: false\n    RandomLoot: true\n    Tradeable: true\n    StrictMythicItems: false</code></pre>\n<h4>Valid Slots</h4>\n<p><b>❗️Required.</b> The equipped <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\">slot(s)</a> the enchantment takes effect in..</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  ValidSlots:\n    - MAINHAND\n    - OFF_HAND</code></pre>\n<h4>Supported Items</h4>\n<p><b>❗️Required.</b> The item tag defining which items this enchantment can be applied to. Accepts a <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Item_tag_(Java_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">datapack item tag</a> reference.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:swords&#x27;</code></pre>\n<blockquote><p>Enchantments missing this field will fail to load.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Primary Items</h4>\n<p>The specific item material IDs or <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Item_tag_(Java_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">item tags</a> that are the preferred items for this enchantment. Shown first in the enchanting table UI.\\ Also accepts <code>mythic:ID</code> entries to reference MythicMobs/Crucible items by their internal ID.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  PrimaryItems:\n    - &#x27;#minecraft:swords&#x27;\n    - minecraft:diamond_axe\n    - minecraft:netherite_axe\n    - mythic:MY_MYTHIC_ITEM_ID</code></pre>\n<blockquote><p><code>mythic:</code> entries are stored separately and enforced at runtime — datapacks match by material only and cannot distinguish Mythic items from plain ones of the same type.\\ To restrict the enchantment exclusively to the listed Mythic items (blocking plain items of the same material), set <code>Options.StrictMythicItems: true</code>.</p></blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h3><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/enchanting-table\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Enchanting-Table\">Enchanting</a></h3>\n<p>Configure the enchanting weight and table behaviors of the enchantment.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 10\n    MinCost: 15\n    MaxCost: 50\n    Promised: true\n    BookOffer: true\n    Reagent:\n      - LAPIS_LAZULI\n    Conditions:\n      - outside</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>A declarative shorthand for applying attribute modifiers via synthetic skill lines, without writing full skill syntax. See <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/attributes\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Attributes\">Attributes</a>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Attributes:\n    MainHand:\n      - ATTACK_DAMAGE 2</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>MythicStats</h3>\n<p>A declarative shorthand for applying MythicMobs stat modifiers via synthetic skill lines, without writing full skill syntax. See <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/mythicstats\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/MythicStats\">MythicStats</a>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Stats:\n    - POWER 10\n    - CRITICAL_STRIKE_CHANCE 5 ADDITIVE\n    - ATTACK_DAMAGE &lt;math:enchant_level*2&gt;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Skills</h3>\n<p>The primary action section of your enchantment, using the <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/Skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mythic Skill System</a> to define what the enchantment does and when.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Skills:\n    - heal{a=0.5*&lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt;;cooldown=5} @self ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<p>📝 <code>CONFIG.YML SNIPPET</code> <code>`</code></p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Custom-Enchantments"},"enchants:enchants/enchantdata":{"h":"<h2>EnchantData</h2>\n<p><code>EnchantData:</code> is an optional section inside any enchantment YAML that lets you declaratively define <b>vanilla Minecraft datapack effect components</b> — the same JSON that lives in <code>data/&lt;namespace&gt;/enchantment/&lt;key&gt;.json</code>. Instead of writing raw JSON you write YAML; MythicEnchants validates it and generates the correct datapack file at startup.</p>\n<p>Any parse error (typo in a key, missing required field, etc.) is printed to the server log and <b>blocks that enchantment from being written to the datapack entirely</b> until fixed. Other enchantments are unaffected.</p>\n<blockquote><p><b>Minecraft wiki references</b></p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#JSON_format\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Enchantment definition JSON format</a></li><li><a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#Effect_components\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Effect components overview</a></li><li><a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Loot_table#Conditions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Loot table conditions (predicates/requirements)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#Entity_effects\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Entity effects</a></li><li><a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Attribute#Modifiers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Attribute modifiers</a></li><li><a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Particles#Types_of_particles\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Particle types</a></li><li><a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Sounds.json#Sound_events\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sound events</a></li></ul></blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h3>Table of Contents</h3>\n<ol><li><span class=\"ilink\">Version compatibility</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">How it fits together</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Value providers</span> — how numbers are expressed</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Requirements / predicates</span> — conditional gating</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Value effect components</span> — scalar boosts</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Bare value components</span> — crossbow &amp; trident timing</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Entity effect components</span> — on-hit, on-tick, etc.</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Entity effect types</span> — what happens</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Attribute effects</span> — stat modifiers</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Flag components</span> — boolean toggles</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Special components</span> — sounds</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Full examples</span></li></ol>\n<hr>\n<h3>Version compatibility</h3>\n<p>MythicEnchants detects the running server version at startup and generates datapacks at the correct pack format automatically.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Server version</th><th>Pack format</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1.21.11</td><td>94</td><td>Supported. <code>post_piercing_attack</code> and <code>damage_immunity</code> skipped with a warning.</td></tr><tr><td>26.1.x</td><td>101</td><td>Supported. Same component restrictions as 94.</td></tr><tr><td>26.2+</td><td>107</td><td>Full support for all components.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Predicate key format</h4>\n<p>Minecraft changed how sub-keys inside <code>entity_properties</code> predicates are named in pack format 107:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Key purpose</th><th>Pre-107 (1.21.11, 26.1)</th><th>107+ (26.2)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Entity flags</td><td><code>flags</code></td><td><code>minecraft:flags</code></td></tr><tr><td>Location check</td><td><code>location</code></td><td><code>minecraft:location</code></td></tr><tr><td>Entity type</td><td><code>type</code></td><td><code>minecraft:entity_type</code></td></tr><tr><td>Type-specific data</td><td><code>type_specific</code></td><td><code>minecraft:type_specific</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Always write predicates in the 26.2 namespaced form.</b> MythicEnchants automatically rewrites them to the correct bare-key form when generating datapacks for servers on format &lt; 107. You never need to maintain two versions of a predicate.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Write this on any server version — MythicEnchants handles the rest\nrequirements:\n  condition: minecraft:entity_properties\n  entity: this\n  predicate:\n    minecraft:flags:\n      is_on_fire: true</code></pre>\n<h4>Components not available before 26.2</h4>\n<p>These are skipped with a server log warning on format &lt; 107. The enchantment still loads normally — only the datapack component is omitted.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Minimum version</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>post_piercing_attack</code></td><td>26.2 (pack format 107) — added for Lunge</td></tr><tr><td><code>damage_immunity</code></td><td>26.2 (pack format 107)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr>\n<h3>How it fits together</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>my_enchant:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;6My Enchant&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 3\n  ValidSlots: [MAINHAND]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/sword&#x27;\n\n  EnchantData:\n    # Everything under here is datapack generation\n    damage:\n      value:\n        type: linear\n        base: 0.5\n        perLevel: 0.5\n\n  Skills:\n    - ... # normal MythicEnchants skill lines still work alongside EnchantData</code></pre>\n<p><code>EnchantData:</code> and <code>Skills:</code> are independent — you can use both, either, or neither.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Value providers</h3>\n<p>A <b>value provider</b> describes how a number is calculated, usually based on enchantment level. Used anywhere a numeric field appears (value effects, attribute amounts, entity effect parameters, etc.).</p>\n<h4>linear</h4>\n<p>Grows linearly with level. <code>base</code> is the value at level 1; <code>perLevel</code> is added for each level above 1.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: linear\n  base: 1.0\n  perLevel: 0.5\n# level 1 = 1.0, level 2 = 1.5, level 3 = 2.0</code></pre>\n<p>Shorthand (same thing, no <code>type:</code> needed):</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>base: 1.0\nperLevel: 0.5</code></pre>\n<h4>constant</h4>\n<p>Fixed value regardless of level.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: constant\n  value: 2.5</code></pre>\n<p>Bare number shorthand (only on top-level effect keys, not inside nested sections):</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>fishing_luck_bonus: 1.0</code></pre>\n<h4>levels_squared</h4>\n<p>Value = <code>(level - 1)² + added</code>. Vanilla uses this for Protection.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: levels_squared\n  added: 1.0\n# level 1 = 1, level 2 = 2, level 3 = 5, level 4 = 10</code></pre>\n<h4>lookup</h4>\n<p>Returns a fixed value per level from a list. If the level exceeds the list length, <code>fallback</code> is used.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: lookup\n  values: [1.0, 2.5, 4.5, 7.0]\n  fallback: 7.0   # also accepts a nested value provider</code></pre>\n<h4>clamped</h4>\n<p>Clamps another value provider to a <code>[min, max]</code> range.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: clamped\n  value:\n    type: linear\n    base: 0.0\n    perLevel: 2.0\n  min: 0.0\n  max: 6.0</code></pre>\n<h4>fraction</h4>\n<p>Divides one value provider by another. Vanilla uses this for Sweeping Edge.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: fraction\n  numerator:\n    type: linear\n    base: 1.0\n    perLevel: 1.0\n  denominator:\n    type: linear\n    base: 2.0\n    perLevel: 1.0\n# level 1 = 1/2, level 2 = 2/3, level 3 = 3/4</code></pre>\n<p>Bare numbers work for numerator/denominator too:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: fraction\n  numerator: 1.0\n  denominator: 3.0</code></pre>\n<h4>exponent</h4>\n<p>Raises <code>base</code> to the power of <code>power</code>. Both accept nested value providers or bare numbers.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: exponent\n  base: 2.0\n  power:\n    type: linear\n    base: 1.0\n    perLevel: 1.0</code></pre>\n<h4>formula (math)</h4>\n<p>Evaluates a math expression once per level (1 through <code>MaxLevel</code>) and bakes the results into a <code>minecraft:lookup</code> table — vanilla&#x27;s JSON format has no arbitrary-formula value type, so MythicEnchants resolves the expression ahead of time at datapack generation rather than at runtime. Uses the same expression engine (exp4j) and function set as <code>&lt;math:...&gt;</code> skill-line tokens — see the class doc on <code>MenchMathParser</code> for the full operator/function list (<code>min</code>, <code>max</code>, <code>clamp</code>, <code>sqrt</code>, <code>sin</code>, <code>round</code>, <code>lerp</code>, etc.).</p>\n<p>Available variables: <code>level</code> (current enchantment level), <code>max_level</code> (the enchant&#x27;s <code>MaxLevel</code>).</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: formula\n  expression: &quot;1 + sqrt(level) * 2&quot;\n# level 1 = 3, level 2 = 3.83, level 3 = 4.46, ...</code></pre>\n<p><code>math</code> is accepted as an alias for <code>type: formula</code>. A parse/eval error at any level is logged and that level falls back to <code>0</code>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Requirements / predicates</h3>\n<p>Any effect entry can include an optional <code>requirements:</code> block. This is a standard <b>Minecraft Predicate</b> written as YAML — it is serialised directly to JSON without any schema validation, so you can use the full condition vocabulary from the wiki.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Predicate\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Predicate</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>damage:\n  value:\n    base: 2.0\n    perLevel: 1.0\n  requirements:\n    condition: minecraft:entity_properties\n    entity: this\n    predicate:\n      minecraft:flags:\n        is_on_fire: true</code></pre>\n<p>Multiple conditions — wrap them in <code>minecraft:all_of</code>:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>requirements:\n  condition: minecraft:all_of\n  terms:\n    - condition: minecraft:random_chance\n      chance: 0.25\n    - condition: minecraft:weather_check\n      thundering: true</code></pre>\n<p><b>Always write predicates in the 26.2 namespaced form</b> (<code>minecraft:flags</code>, <code>minecraft:location</code>, <code>minecraft:entity_type</code>, etc.). MythicEnchants automatically rewrites them to the correct bare-key form for servers running pre-107 pack formats. See <span class=\"ilink\">Version compatibility</span> for details.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Value effect components</h3>\n<p>These are <b>conditional arrays</b> — each entry has an effect (the number) and an optional requirements predicate. Multiple entries are evaluated in order; all matching entries are summed.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#Value_effect_components\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Value effect components</a></p></blockquote>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>What it affects</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>damage</code></td><td>Extra damage dealt</td></tr><tr><td><code>damage_protection</code></td><td>Damage reduction (Protection family)</td></tr><tr><td><code>armor_effectiveness</code></td><td>How much armor helps against this damage source</td></tr><tr><td><code>knockback</code></td><td>Knockback strength on hit</td></tr><tr><td><code>smash_damage_per_fallen_block</code></td><td>Bonus damage per block fallen before impact (Density)</td></tr><tr><td><code>equipment_drops</code></td><td>Chance modifier for mob equipment drops</td></tr><tr><td><code>ammo_use</code></td><td>Ammo consumption modifier (Infinity uses 0)</td></tr><tr><td><code>projectile_piercing</code></td><td>How many entities a projectile can pierce (Piercing)</td></tr><tr><td><code>projectile_count</code></td><td>Number of projectiles fired (Multishot)</td></tr><tr><td><code>projectile_spread</code></td><td>Spread angle of projectiles in degrees</td></tr><tr><td><code>block_experience</code></td><td>XP dropped from breaking blocks (Fortune)</td></tr><tr><td><code>mob_experience</code></td><td>XP dropped from killing mobs (Looting)</td></tr><tr><td><code>repair_with_xp</code></td><td>Item repair rate from XP (Mending)</td></tr><tr><td><code>item_damage</code></td><td>Durability damage dealt to the item</td></tr><tr><td><code>trident_return_acceleration</code></td><td>Loyalty return speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>fishing_time_reduction</code></td><td>Reduction in fishing wait time (Lure)</td></tr><tr><td><code>fishing_luck_bonus</code></td><td>Luck bonus for fishing loot table (Luck of the Sea)</td></tr><tr><td><code>location_changed</code></td><td>Fires when the player moves to a new block (Frost Walker)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Single entry (most common)</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>damage:\n  value:\n    type: linear\n    base: 0.5\n    perLevel: 0.5</code></pre>\n<h4>With requirements</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>damage_protection:\n  value:\n    type: levels_squared\n    added: 1.0\n  requirements:\n    condition: minecraft:entity_properties\n    entity: this\n    predicate:\n      minecraft:flags:\n        is_on_fire: true</code></pre>\n<h4>Multiple gated entries</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>damage:\n  entries:\n    - value:\n        type: constant\n        value: 2.0\n      requirements:\n        condition: minecraft:random_chance\n        chance: 0.5\n    - value:\n        base: 0.5\n        perLevel: 0.25</code></pre>\n<h4>Bare number shorthand</h4>\n<p>Expands to a constant value with no requirements:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>fishing_luck_bonus: 2.0</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Bare value components</h3>\n<p>These two components take a <b>single bare value object</b> in the datapack JSON — not an array of conditional entries. You cannot add multiple gated entries; use them for a simple scalar override.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#minecraft:crossbow_charge_time\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">crossbow_charge_time</a>, <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#minecraft:trident_spin_attack_strength\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">trident_spin_attack_strength</a></p></blockquote>\n<h4>crossbow_charge_time</h4>\n<p>Changes crossbow charge time. Negative values make it faster (vanilla Quick Charge: −0.25 per level).</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>crossbow_charge_time:\n  value:\n    type: linear\n    base: -0.25\n    perLevel: -0.25</code></pre>\n<p>Shorthand:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>crossbow_charge_time: -0.75</code></pre>\n<h4>trident_spin_attack_strength</h4>\n<p>Strength of the trident spin attack (Riptide).</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>trident_spin_attack_strength:\n  value:\n    type: linear\n    base: 1.5\n    perLevel: 0.75</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Entity effect components</h3>\n<p>These fire in response to game events. Each entry specifies <b>who carries the enchantment</b> (<code>enchanted</code>), <b>who is affected</b> (<code>affected</code>), the <b>effect type</b>, and an optional <code>requirements</code> predicate.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#Entity_effect_components\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Entity effect components</a></p></blockquote>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>When it fires</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>post_attack</code></td><td>After a melee attack connects</td></tr><tr><td><code>tick</code></td><td>Every game tick while equipped in a valid slot</td></tr><tr><td><code>hit_block</code></td><td>When a projectile hits a block</td></tr><tr><td><code>projectile_spawned</code></td><td>When a projectile is fired</td></tr><tr><td><code>post_piercing_attack</code></td><td>After a piercing projectile passes through an entity</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>enchanted / affected values</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>attacker</code></td><td>The entity holding the enchanted item</td></tr><tr><td><code>victim</code></td><td>The entity being attacked</td></tr><tr><td><code>damaging_entity</code></td><td>The direct source of damage (e.g. the arrow itself)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Not all combinations are valid for every component — <code>hit_block</code> has no <code>affected</code>, for example.</p>\n<h4>Single entry</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>post_attack:\n  enchanted: attacker\n  affected: victim\n  effect:\n    type: apply_mob_effect\n    to_apply: minecraft:poison\n    min_duration: 3.0\n    max_duration: 3.0\n    min_amplifier: 0.0\n    max_amplifier: 0.0\n  requirements:\n    condition: minecraft:random_chance\n    chance: 0.15</code></pre>\n<h4>Multiple entries</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>post_attack:\n  entries:\n    - enchanted: attacker\n      affected: victim\n      effect:\n        type: ignite\n        duration: 4.0\n    - enchanted: attacker\n      affected: victim\n      effect:\n        type: apply_mob_effect\n        to_apply: minecraft:slowness\n        min_duration: 2.0\n        max_duration: 2.0\n        min_amplifier: 1.0\n        max_amplifier: 1.0\n      requirements:\n        condition: minecraft:random_chance\n        chance: 0.3</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Entity effect types</h3>\n<p>These go inside the <code>effect:</code> block of an entity effect entry.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#Entity_effects\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Entity effects</a></p></blockquote>\n<h4>apply_mob_effect</h4>\n<p>Applies a potion effect to the target.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Effect#Effect_list\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Effect IDs</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: apply_mob_effect\n  to_apply: minecraft:poison        # required — effect ID or list of IDs\n  min_duration: 3.0                 # seconds (default 5.0)\n  max_duration: 3.0\n  min_amplifier: 0.0                # 0 = level I (default 0.0)\n  max_amplifier: 0.0</code></pre>\n<p><code>to_apply</code> can be a list for random selection:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>to_apply:\n  - minecraft:poison\n  - minecraft:wither</code></pre>\n<p>Duration and amplifier accept value providers:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>min_duration:\n  type: linear\n  base: 2.0\n  perLevel: 1.0\nmax_duration:\n  type: linear\n  base: 3.0\n  perLevel: 1.5</code></pre>\n<h4>ignite</h4>\n<p>Sets the target on fire.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: ignite\n  duration: 8.0    # seconds — accepts a value provider</code></pre>\n<h4>damage_entity</h4>\n<p>Deals direct damage.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Damage_type\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Damage types</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: damage_entity\n  damage_type: minecraft:generic    # required\n  min_damage: 1.0                   # accepts value providers\n  max_damage: 4.0</code></pre>\n<h4>change_item_damage</h4>\n<p>Damages the enchanted item&#x27;s durability.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: change_item_damage\n  amount: 1.0    # accepts a value provider</code></pre>\n<h4>apply_exhaustion</h4>\n<p>Drains the player&#x27;s food exhaustion meter.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: apply_exhaustion\n  amount: 0.1    # accepts a value provider</code></pre>\n<h4>apply_impulse</h4>\n<p>Applies a velocity impulse to the target.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: apply_impulse\n  direction: [0.0, 1.0, 0.0]          # [x, y, z] unit vector\n  coordinate_scale: [1.0, 0.0, 1.0]   # optional — scales each axis by a factor\n  magnitude: 2.0                        # accepts a value provider</code></pre>\n<h4>summon_entity</h4>\n<p>Spawns an entity at the target&#x27;s location.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Java_Edition_data_values#Entities\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Entity IDs</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: summon_entity\n  entity: minecraft:lightning_bolt    # required — entity ID or list\n  join_team: false                    # optional</code></pre>\n<h4>run_function</h4>\n<p>Runs a datapack function.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: run_function\n  function: mynamespace:my_function    # required — function ID</code></pre>\n<h4>play_sound</h4>\n<p>Plays a sound at the target&#x27;s location.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Sounds.json#Sound_events\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sound events</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: play_sound\n  sound: minecraft:entity.lightning_bolt.thunder    # string or list for random pick\n  volume: 5.0    # accepts value providers\n  pitch: 1.0</code></pre>\n<p>Random sound pick:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>sound:\n  - minecraft:entity.lightning_bolt.thunder\n  - minecraft:entity.generic.explode</code></pre>\n<h4>spawn_particles</h4>\n<p>Spawns particles at the target.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Particles#Types_of_particles\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Particle types</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: spawn_particles\n  particle:                      # required — particle definition (pass raw YAML)\n    type: minecraft:flame\n  horizontal_position:           # optional position/velocity sections\n    type: entity_position\n    offset: 0.5\n  vertical_position:\n    type: entity_position\n    offset: 0.5\n  speed: 0.1</code></pre>\n<h4>explode</h4>\n<p>Creates an explosion at the target.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: explode\n  radius: 3.0                          # accepts value provider\n  attribute_to_user: true              # optional\n  damage_type: minecraft:explosion     # optional\n  block_interaction: destroy           # optional: destroy | block | none | trigger_block\n  create_fire: false                   # optional\n  offset: [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]             # optional [x, y, z]\n  immune_blocks: &#x27;#minecraft:dragon_immune&#x27;  # optional — block tag or list\n  knockback_multiplier: 1.0            # optional — value provider\n  sound: minecraft:entity.generic.explode   # optional</code></pre>\n<h4>replace_block</h4>\n<p>Replaces the block at the target location with another block state.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: replace_block\n  block_state:               # the replacement block state as raw YAML\n    Name: minecraft:ice\n  offset: [0.0, -1.0, 0.0]  # optional [x, y, z]\n  predicate:                 # optional block predicate\n    blocks: &#x27;#minecraft:water&#x27;\n  trigger_game_event: minecraft:block_change   # optional</code></pre>\n<h4>replace_disk</h4>\n<p>Same as <code>replace_block</code> but fills a disk area.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: replace_disk\n  block_state:\n    Name: minecraft:frosted_ice\n    Properties:\n      age: &#x27;0&#x27;\n  radius: 2.0          # accepts value provider\n  height: 1.0          # accepts value provider\n  offset: [0.0, -1.0, 0.0]</code></pre>\n<h4>set_block_properties</h4>\n<p>Changes properties of an existing block without replacing it.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: set_block_properties\n  properties:\n    waterlogged: &#x27;true&#x27;\n  offset: [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]\n  trigger_game_event: minecraft:block_change</code></pre>\n<h4>all_of</h4>\n<p>Runs multiple effects together. Effects inside are all applied unconditionally (use outer <code>requirements</code> to gate the group).</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: all_of\n  effects:\n    - type: ignite\n      duration: 4.0\n    - type: apply_mob_effect\n      to_apply: minecraft:poison\n      min_duration: 2.0\n      max_duration: 2.0\n      min_amplifier: 0.0\n      max_amplifier: 0.0</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Attribute effects</h3>\n<p>Attribute modifiers change entity stat values while the enchanted item is equipped. Multiple modifiers are supported.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Attribute\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Attributes</a>, <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Attribute#Modifiers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Attribute modifiers</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>attributes:\n  - attribute: generic.attack_damage    # short alias or full minecraft:... ID\n    operation: add                      # add | add_multiplied_base | add_multiplied_total\n    value:\n      type: linear\n      base: 1.0\n      perLevel: 0.5\n    id: my_namespace:my_enchant/damage  # optional — auto-generated if omitted\n    requirements:                       # optional\n      condition: minecraft:random_chance\n      chance: 1.0</code></pre>\n<h4>Attribute operations</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>YAML value</th><th>Datapack value</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>add</code></td><td><code>add_value</code></td><td>Adds a flat amount to the base value</td></tr><tr><td><code>add_multiplied_base</code></td><td><code>add_multiplied_base</code></td><td>Adds <code>base × amount</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>add_multiplied_total</code></td><td><code>add_multiplied_total</code></td><td>Multiplies the running total</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Attribute#Operations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Modifier operations</a></p></blockquote>\n<h4>Attribute short aliases</h4>\n<p>You can use short names instead of the full <code>minecraft:</code> ID:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Short alias</th><th>Full ID</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>damage</code>, <code>attack_damage</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.attack_damage</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>attack_speed</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.attack_speed</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>armor</code>, <code>armor_points</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.armor</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>armor_toughness</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.armor_toughness</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>knockback_resistance</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.knockback_resistance</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>max_health</code>, <code>health</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.max_health</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>movement_speed</code>, <code>speed</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.movement_speed</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>luck</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.luck</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>reach</code>, <code>block_reach</code>, <code>block_interaction_range</code></td><td><code>minecraft:player.block_interaction_range</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>entity_reach</code>, <code>entity_interaction_range</code></td><td><code>minecraft:player.entity_interaction_range</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>mining_efficiency</code></td><td><code>minecraft:player.mining_efficiency</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>sneaking_speed</code></td><td><code>minecraft:player.sneaking_speed</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>submerged_mining_speed</code></td><td><code>minecraft:player.submerged_mining_speed</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>sweeping_damage_ratio</code>, <code>sweeping</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.sweeping_damage_ratio</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>armor_effectiveness</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.armor_effectiveness</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>gravity</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.gravity</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>jump_strength</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.jump_strength</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>safe_fall_distance</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.safe_fall_distance</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>fall_damage_multiplier</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.fall_damage_multiplier</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>burning_time</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.burning_time</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>explosion_knockback_resistance</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.explosion_knockback_resistance</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>water_movement_efficiency</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.water_movement_efficiency</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>oxygen_bonus</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.oxygen_bonus</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Any unrecognised alias is expanded to <code>minecraft:generic.&lt;alias&gt;</code> — so any future attributes added by Mojang will work automatically.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Flag components</h3>\n<p>Boolean toggles. Set to <code>true</code> to enable; <code>false</code> or omitting the key entirely disables (same result).</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#Flag_components\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Flag components</a></p></blockquote>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>damage_immunity</code></td><td>The enchanted item&#x27;s holder takes no damage from the effect&#x27;s damage type (e.g. Fire Protection vs fire)</td></tr><tr><td><code>prevent_equipment_drop</code></td><td>Mobs with this enchantment do not drop their equipment on death</td></tr><tr><td><code>prevent_armor_change</code></td><td>Players cannot equip or unequip armor while wearing this item</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>damage_immunity: true\nprevent_equipment_drop: true\nprevent_armor_change: true</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Special components</h3>\n<h4>crossbow_charging_sounds</h4>\n<p>Defines the sounds played per Quick Charge level while charging a crossbow. One entry per charge level (vanilla has 3).</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#minecraft:crossbow_charging_sounds\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">crossbow_charging_sounds</a></p></blockquote>\n<p>Full form (control both start and end sounds):</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>crossbow_charging_sounds:\n  - start: minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_1\n    end: minecraft:item.crossbow.loading_end\n  - start: minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_2\n    end: minecraft:item.crossbow.loading_end\n  - start: minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_3\n    end: minecraft:item.crossbow.loading_end</code></pre>\n<p>Shorthand (only specify start sounds; end always defaults to <code>minecraft:item.crossbow.loading_end</code>):</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>crossbow_charging_sounds:\n  - minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_1\n  - minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_2\n  - minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_3</code></pre>\n<h4>trident_sound</h4>\n<p>Sounds played per Riptide level when spinning (one per level, vanilla has 3).</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#minecraft:trident_sound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">trident_sound</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>trident_sound:\n  - minecraft:item.trident.riptide_1\n  - minecraft:item.trident.riptide_2\n  - minecraft:item.trident.riptide_3</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Full examples</h3>\n<h4>Sharpness clone</h4>\n<p>Flat extra damage, grows with level.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>sharp_echo:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;7Sharp Echo&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 5\n  ValidSlots: [MAINHAND]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/sharp_weapon&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    damage:\n      value:\n        type: linear\n        base: 1.0\n        perLevel: 0.5</code></pre>\n<h4>Fire-conditional damage boost</h4>\n<p>Extra damage only when the wielder is on fire.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>inferno_strike:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;cInferno Strike&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 3\n  ValidSlots: [MAINHAND]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/sharp_weapon&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    damage:\n      value:\n        type: linear\n        base: 2.0\n        perLevel: 1.0\n      requirements:\n        condition: minecraft:entity_properties\n        entity: this\n        predicate:\n          minecraft:flags:\n            is_on_fire: true</code></pre>\n<h4>Stat-boosting ring (attribute modifiers)</h4>\n<p>Hypothetical ring item that boosts health and speed.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>vitality_ring:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;aVitality Ring&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 3\n  ValidSlots: [OFFHAND]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#mythicenchants:enchantable/ring&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    attributes:\n      - attribute: max_health\n        operation: add\n        value:\n          type: linear\n          base: 2.0\n          perLevel: 2.0\n      - attribute: movement_speed\n        operation: add_multiplied_total\n        value:\n          type: constant\n          value: 0.05</code></pre>\n<h4>Poisoning strikes (entity effect)</h4>\n<p>Random chance to poison on hit.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>venom_touch:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;2Venom Touch&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 3\n  ValidSlots: [MAINHAND]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/sharp_weapon&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    post_attack:\n      enchanted: attacker\n      affected: victim\n      effect:\n        type: apply_mob_effect\n        to_apply: minecraft:poison\n        min_duration:\n          type: linear\n          base: 1.0\n          perLevel: 1.0\n        max_duration:\n          type: linear\n          base: 2.0\n          perLevel: 1.0\n        min_amplifier: 0.0\n        max_amplifier: 0.0\n      requirements:\n        condition: minecraft:random_chance\n        chance: 0.25</code></pre>\n<h4>Multi-effect on hit (all_of)</h4>\n<p>Ignite and slow on hit, with a random chance gate.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>glacial_flare:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;bGlacial Flare&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 2\n  ValidSlots: [MAINHAND]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/sharp_weapon&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    post_attack:\n      enchanted: attacker\n      affected: victim\n      effect:\n        type: all_of\n        effects:\n          - type: ignite\n            duration: 3.0\n          - type: apply_mob_effect\n            to_apply: minecraft:slowness\n            min_duration: 2.0\n            max_duration: 2.0\n            min_amplifier: 1.0\n            max_amplifier: 1.0\n      requirements:\n        condition: minecraft:random_chance\n        chance: 0.20</code></pre>\n<h4>Custom Quick Charge with sounds</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>swift_draw:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;eSwift Draw&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 3\n  ValidSlots: [MAINHAND]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/crossbow&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    crossbow_charge_time:\n      value:\n        type: linear\n        base: -0.25\n        perLevel: -0.25\n    crossbow_charging_sounds:\n      - minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_1\n      - minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_2\n      - minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_3</code></pre>\n<h4>Protection with level-scaled damage reduction</h4>\n<p>Mimics vanilla Protection using <code>levels_squared</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>arcane_guard:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;9Arcane Guard&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 4\n  ValidSlots: [HEAD, CHEST, LEGS, FEET]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/armor&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    damage_protection:\n      value:\n        type: levels_squared\n        added: 1.0</code></pre>\n<h4>Multiple value effect entries (gated stacking)</h4>\n<p>Base reduction always applies; bonus kicks in only underwater.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>tide_ward:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;3Tide Ward&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 3\n  ValidSlots: [CHEST]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/armor&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    damage_protection:\n      entries:\n        - value:\n            type: linear\n            base: 1.0\n            perLevel: 1.0\n        - value:\n            type: constant\n            value: 3.0\n          requirements:\n            condition: minecraft:entity_properties\n            entity: this\n            predicate:\n              minecraft:flags:\n                is_in_water: true</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/EnchantData"},"enchants:enchants/enchanting-table":{"h":"<p>Enchanting on the Enchanting Table is configured, and expanded, through these settings.  Global <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"table/enchanting\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Table/Enchanting\">Enchantment-Config</a> settings can affect this.  Just like in vanilla, <code>Treasure: true</code> enchantments are not offered on the table, intended only for external discovery like loot and trades.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 10\n    MinCost: 15\n    MaxCost: 50\n    Promised: true\n    BookOffer: true\n    Reagent:\n      - LAPIS_LAZULI\n    Conditions:\n      - outside</code></pre>\n<h4>Weight</h4>\n<p>The likelihood of this enchantment being selected when offered by an enchanting table. Must be a whole number between 1 and 1024.\\ Higher values increase the chance of selection — values are weighed against all other enchantments, so keep weights in a similar range.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 10</code></pre>\n<h4>MinCost &amp; MaxCost</h4>\n<p>The minimum and maximum modified enchantment levels required to roll this enchantment.\\ Accepts either a flat scalar value, or a <code>Base</code> + <code>PerLevel</code> breakdown for level-scaling costs.</p>\n<p>Scalar shorthand:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Enchanting:\n    MinCost: 15\n    MaxCost: 50</code></pre>\n<p>Base + per-level scaling:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Enchanting:\n    MinCost:\n      Base: 15\n      PerLevel: 9\n    MaxCost:\n      Base: 65\n      PerLevel: 0</code></pre>\n<h4>Promised</h4>\n<p>Determines whether this enchantment is ever shown as a named promise in the enchanting table tooltip. Defaults to <code>true</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Enchanting:\n    Promised: true</code></pre>\n<h4>BookOffer</h4>\n<p>Determines whether books can be enchanted with this enchantment at the enchanting table. This is independent of <code>SupportedItems</code> and <code>PrimaryItems</code> — books are universally supported unless this is set to <code>false</code>. Defaults to <code>true</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Enchanting:\n    BookOffer: false</code></pre>\n<h4>Reagent</h4>\n<p>The reagent type(s) required for this enchantment to appear as a result at the enchanting table. Defaults to vanilla Lapis Lazuli only.\\ Accepts vanilla material IDs, MythicMobs/Crucible item IDs, or namespaced item model strings. Set to <code>ALL</code> to accept any reagent.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Enchanting:\n    Reagent:\n      - LAPIS_LAZULI\n      - moondust        # MythicMobs item ID\n      - nexo:sunshard   # namespaced item model string</code></pre>\n<h4>Conditions</h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/conditions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicMobs conditions</a> evaluated at the location and time of opening the enchanting table. The enchantment will only be offered if all conditions pass.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Enchanting:\n    Conditions:\n      - outside\n      - (night || dusk)</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Enchanting-Table"},"enchants:enchants/enchantment-config":{"h":"<p>A complete outline of every enchantment configuration option, with defaults and descriptions.</p>\n<blockquote><p>This is <i>not</i> a plug-and-play enchantment, it is a complete reference of every element an enchantment config might contain.</p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n#  Full enchantment example — every supported field with REQUIRED / OPTIONAL notes\n#\n#  Place files like this in:\n#    plugins/MythicMobs/packs/&lt;yourpack&gt;/Enchantments/\n#\n#  Multiple enchantments per file are allowed. The top-level key is the enchant\n#  ID. Bare IDs (no colon) are namespaced automatically using the datapack name\n#  set in config.yml. Explicit namespaces (namespace:key) are used as-is.\n# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n# REQUIRED — enchantment ID. Bare IDs get the configured datapack namespace.\n#            Use namespace:key to pin it (e.g. mythicenchants:enchantment_id).\nenchantment_id:\n\n  # REQUIRED — display name shown in item lore. Supports &amp; color codes.\n  Display: &#x27;&lt;white&gt;Example Enchantment&#x27;\n\n  # OPTIONAL — extra lore line(s) shown below the enchant name. Defaults to empty.\n  Description: &#x27;&lt;gray&gt;The enchantment with all the options!&#x27;\n\n  # OPTIONAL — rarity tier. Controls enchanting-table weight grouping and\n  #            display color. One of: COMMON, UNCOMMON, RARE, VERY_RARE.\n  #            Defaults to COMMON.\n  Rarity: COMMON\n\n  # OPTIONAL — minimum enchantment level (for grading/display). Defaults to 1.\n  MinLevel: 1\n\n  # REQUIRED (effectively) — maximum level. Defaults to 1 if omitted.\n  MaxLevel: 1\n\n  # OPTIONAL — which equipment slots activate this enchant&#x27;s skills.\n  #            List one or more: MAINHAND, OFFHAND, HEAD, CHEST, LEGS, FEET, ALL.\n  #            Defaults to [ALL].\n  ValidSlots:\n    - ALL\n\n  # OPTIONAL — datapack item filter controlling which items can receive this\n  #            enchant. Accepts tag refs (#minecraft:enchantable/sword) or\n  #            individual item keys (minecraft:diamond_sword).\n  #            Defaults to #minecraft:enchantable/weapon.\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/weapon&#x27;\n\n  # OPTIONAL — items shown as &quot;primary&quot; in the datapack (affect enchanting table\n  #            cost weighting in vanilla logic). Usually left empty.\n  PrimaryItems: []\n\n  # OPTIONAL — XP level cost per merge step in an anvil. Defaults to 1.\n  AnvilCost: 1\n\n  # OPTIONAL — tag memberships. Unnamespaced tags get the plugin&#x27;s default\n  #            namespace. Tags drive conflict resolution and loot table filtering.\n  Tags:\n    - minecraft:on_random_loot  # appears in general vanilla chest/mob loot\n    - exclusive_damage          # example custom exclusion group\n\n  # OPTIONAL — enchantments (or #tag refs) that conflict with this one.\n  #            Conflicting enchants cannot coexist on the same item.\n  ConflictingEnchants:\n    - minecraft:sharpness\n    - minecraft:smite\n    - minecraft:bane_of_arthropods\n\n  # OPTIONAL — behaviour flags block. All three default to false/true as shown.\n  Options:\n    Enabled: true # whether available/obtainable or not and whether skills work\n    Cursed: false # Signifies whether a curse or no\n    Treasure: false # Signifies whether counted as a treasure enchantment\n    RandomLoot: true # Can be generated on random loot\n    Tradeable: true # can be traded by librarians\n    TradedEquipment: true # on traded equipment or no\n    MobSpawnEquipment: true # on mob equipment\n    TooltipOrder: 42 # weighted order of tool tip from 1 being the top\n  Enchanting:\n    # OPTIONAL — relative selection weight (higher = more likely to appear).\n    #            Defaults to 1\n    Weight: 1\n\n    # OPTIONAL — minimum modified enchantment level needed to roll this enchant.\n    #            Scalar shorthand: MinCost: 15  (Base only, PerLevel defaults to 0).\n    #            Full form shown below.\n    MinCost:\n      Base: 15        # minimum cost at level 1\n      PerLevel: 9     # added per level above 1 (so level 3 min = 15 + 9*2 = 33)\n\n    # OPTIONAL — maximum modified enchantment level that can still produce this\n    #            enchant. Same scalar / full-form rules as MinCost.\n    MaxCost:\n      Base: 65\n      PerLevel: 0\n\n    # OPTIONAL — whether this enchant can appear as a named promise hint in the\n    #            table tooltip. Defaults to true.\n    Promised: true\n\n    # OPTIONAL — whether this enchant can be enchanted onto books in the table.\n    #            Defaults to true, so only needs to be defined to prevent this.\n    BookOffer: true \n\n    # OPTIONAL — reagent(s) required in the lapis slot to unlock this enchant.\n    #            Omit entirely (or omit the list) = vanilla lapis only.\n    #            Single entry &quot;ALL&quot; = any reagent accepted.\n    #            Each entry is one of:\n    #              LAPIS_LAZULI          — plain vanilla lapis\n    #              &lt;crucible-id&gt;         — MythicCrucible item internal name\n    #              &lt;model-string-path&gt;   — custom model data string key\n    Reagent:\n      - LAPIS_LAZULI\n      - moondust        # also accepts this Crucible reagent\n      - nexo:sunshard   # can read any item model string on lapis items\n\n    # OPTIONAL — MythicMobs conditions evaluated when the table is opened.\n    #            This enchant only appears as an option when all conditions pass.\n    Conditions:\n      - (night || dusk)   # time-of-day condition\n      - outside           # player must be under open sky\n\n  # OPTIONAL — MythicMobs skill lines. Omit the block if this enchant has no\n  #            active skills (e.g. a pure datapack effect enchant).\n  #\n  #  Format:  mechanic{attributes} @targeter ~onTrigger\n  #\n  #  &lt;math:EXPR&gt; or for meta/sudo skills &lt;math.EXPR&gt; substitutes a computed value. Available variables:\n  #    enchant_level, enchant_maxlevel\n  #    player_health, player_max_health\n  #    target_health, target_max_health\n  #    fall_distance, \n  #    damage  (only on ~onDamaged)\n  #    item_attack  (only on ~onAttack)\n  #  Underscore and dash forms are both accepted (enchant_level = enchant-level).\n  Skills:\n    # Deal bonus damage scaled to enchantment level\n    - damage{a=&lt;math:enchant_level*1.5&gt;} @trigger ~onAttack\n\n    # Apply a timed weakness effect to the target, duration scales with level\n    - potion{type=WEAKNESS;d=&lt;math:enchant_level*40&gt;;amp=0} @trigger ~onAttack\n\n    # Reduce incoming projectile damage proportional to current level\n    - reducedamage{a=&lt;math:damage*0.05*enchant_level&gt;;cause=PROJECTILE} @self ~onDamaged\n\n    # Apply an attribute bonus while the item is equipped / remove it on unequip\n    - enchantattribute{attribute=ATTACK_DAMAGE;a=&lt;math:enchant_level*0.5&gt;;op=ADD_NUMBER;mode=APPLY} @self ~onEquip\n    - enchantattribute{attribute=ATTACK_DAMAGE;mode=REMOVE} @self ~onUnequip</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Enchantment-Config"},"enchants:enchants/enchantment-options":{"h":"<p>Additional options for configuring enchantments to various archetypes or behaviors.  Most behavior options are controlled by the enchantment&#x27;s <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_tag_(Java_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Enchantment tags</a> in configuration.</p>\n<p>Options default to false unless defined otherwise on a config, and generally can be freely combined.</p>\n<h4>Enabled</h4>\n<p>If the enchantment is enabled at all.  Defaults to <code>true</code> so does not need to be present on active enchantments.</p>\n<p>An enchantment can be disabled with:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;red&gt;Disabled Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    Enabled: false</code></pre>\n<h4>Cursed</h4>\n<p>Considered a curse enchantment, taking a red, ominous lore format and preventing grindstone removal:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    Cursed: true</code></pre>\n<h4>Treasure</h4>\n<p>These items double their market price in villager trades:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    Treasure: true</code></pre>\n<h4>RandomLoot</h4>\n<p>These Enchantments will appear in dungeon/chest loot:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    RandomLoot: true</code></pre>\n<h4>Tradeable</h4>\n<p>These enchantments will appear on villager book trades:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n   Tradeable: true</code></pre>\n<h4>TradedEquipment</h4>\n<p>These enchantments will appear on villager-tradded gear:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    TradedEquipment: true</code></pre>\n<h4>MobSpawnEquipment</h4>\n<p>These enchantments will appear on mob equipment:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    MobSpawnEquipment: true</code></pre>\n<h4>TooltipOrder</h4>\n<p>Order of enchantments on the tooltip:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    TooltipOrder: 42</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Enchantment-Options"},"enchants:enchants/mythicstats":{"h":"<hr>\n<p>title: MythicStats</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>MythicAttributes|MythicStats</h3>\n<p>The <code>MythicAttributes|MythicStats|Stats</code> section is a declarative shorthand for applying MythicMobs stat modifiers without writing full skill line syntax. Each entry generates a pair of synthetic skill lines — one on <code>~onEquip</code> to apply the modifier, and one on <code>~onUnequip</code> to remove it.</p>\n<p>Unlike <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/attributes\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Attributes\">Attributes</a>, which writes modifiers into item metadata (visible in tooltips, persistent), <code>MythicAttributes|MythicStats|Stats</code> applies modifiers directly to the entity through MythicMobs&#x27; stat system. They are transient — not stored on the item, not visible in the tooltip, and re-applied whenever the item is equipped. You&#x27;ll notice through the Page We use Stats, MythicStats, or MythicAttributes, Either is applicable as one is an Alias of the other.</p>\n<h4>Syntax</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  MythicStats:\n    - &lt;STAT&gt; &lt;AMOUNT&gt; [TYPE]</code></pre>\n<p>Each line follows this format:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Required</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>STAT</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>The MythicMobs stat name (see <span class=\"ilink\">Stats</span>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>AMOUNT</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>A numeric value or <code>&lt;math:&gt;</code> expression</td></tr><tr><td><code>TYPE</code></td><td>No</td><td>The modifier type (see <span class=\"ilink\">Types</span>). Defaults to <code>ADDITIVE</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Example</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  MythicAttributes:\n    - POWER 10\n    - CRITICAL_STRIKE_CHANCE 5\n    - ATTACK_DAMAGE &lt;math:enchant_level*2&gt;\n    - MOVEMENT_SPEED 0.1 ADDITIVE_MULTIPLIER</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Stats</h4>\n<p>These are the built-in stats registered by MythicMobs. Custom stats defined in your MythicMobs configuration are also valid.</p>\n<h5>Damage</h5>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Stat</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>BONUS_DAMAGE</code></td><td>Flat bonus added to outgoing damage</td></tr><tr><td><code>PERCENT_DAMAGE</code></td><td>Percentage bonus to outgoing damage</td></tr><tr><td><code>CRITICAL_STRIKE_CHANCE</code></td><td>Chance to land a critical hit</td></tr><tr><td><code>CRITICAL_STRIKE_DAMAGE</code></td><td>Multiplier applied on a critical hit</td></tr><tr><td><code>CRITICAL_STRIKE_RESILIENCE</code></td><td>Reduces incoming critical hit damage</td></tr><tr><td><code>DODGE_NEGATION</code></td><td>Reduces target&#x27;s chance to dodge</td></tr><tr><td><code>PARRY_NEGATION</code></td><td>Reduces target&#x27;s chance to parry</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5>Defense</h5>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Stat</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>DEFENSE</code></td><td>Flat damage reduction</td></tr><tr><td><code>DAMAGE_REDUCTION</code></td><td>Percentage damage reduction</td></tr><tr><td><code>DODGE_CHANCE</code></td><td>Chance to completely avoid an attack</td></tr><tr><td><code>PARRY_CHANCE</code></td><td>Chance to parry an attack</td></tr><tr><td><code>PARRY_POWER</code></td><td>Damage reduction when a parry triggers</td></tr><tr><td><code>PARRY_COUNTERATTACK</code></td><td>Damage dealt on a successful parry</td></tr><tr><td><code>HEALTH_REGENERATION</code></td><td>Passive health regeneration</td></tr><tr><td><code>LIFESTEAL_CHANCE</code></td><td>Chance to lifesteal on hit</td></tr><tr><td><code>LIFESTEAL_POWER</code></td><td>Amount of health restored on lifesteal</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5>General</h5>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Stat</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>POWER</code></td><td>General power stat used in skill scaling</td></tr><tr><td><code>LOOT_BIAS</code></td><td>Influences loot roll outcomes</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5>Vanilla (mapped to Bukkit attributes)</h5>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Stat</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ATTACK_DAMAGE</code></td><td>Melee attack damage</td></tr><tr><td><code>ATTACK_SPEED</code></td><td>Attack speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>HEALTH</code></td><td>Maximum health</td></tr><tr><td><code>ARMOR</code></td><td>Armor points</td></tr><tr><td><code>ARMOR_TOUGHNESS</code></td><td>Armor toughness</td></tr><tr><td><code>MOVEMENT_SPEED</code></td><td>Movement speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>FLYING_SPEED</code></td><td>Flying speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>KNOCKBACK_RESISTANCE</code></td><td>Resistance to knockback</td></tr><tr><td><code>FOLLOW_RANGE</code></td><td>Entity follow/detection range</td></tr><tr><td><code>SCALE</code></td><td>Entity scale</td></tr><tr><td><code>STEP_HEIGHT</code></td><td>Step height (auto-climb)</td></tr><tr><td><code>JUMP_STRENGTH</code></td><td>Jump strength</td></tr><tr><td><code>GRAVITY</code></td><td>Gravity multiplier</td></tr><tr><td><code>SAFE_FALL_DISTANCE</code></td><td>Distance before fall damage begins</td></tr><tr><td><code>FALL_DAMAGE_MULTIPLIER</code></td><td>Multiplier applied to fall damage</td></tr><tr><td><code>BLOCK_BREAK_SPEED</code></td><td>Block breaking speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>BLOCK_INTERACTION_RANGE</code></td><td>Block interaction reach</td></tr><tr><td><code>ENTITY_INTERACTION_RANGE</code></td><td>Entity interaction reach</td></tr><tr><td><code>MOVEMENT_EFFICIENCY</code></td><td>Movement efficiency on slow blocks</td></tr><tr><td><code>SNEAKING_SPEED</code></td><td>Movement speed while sneaking</td></tr><tr><td><code>WATER_MOVEMENT_EFFICIENCY</code></td><td>Movement efficiency in water</td></tr><tr><td><code>OXYGEN_BONUS</code></td><td>Bonus oxygen/breath</td></tr><tr><td><code>BURNING_TIME</code></td><td>Duration of fire on entity</td></tr><tr><td><code>EXPLOSION_KNOCKBACK_RESISTANCE</code></td><td>Resistance to explosion knockback</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr>\n<h4>Modifier Types</h4>\n<p>Controls how the amount is applied relative to the entity&#x27;s base stat value.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ADDITIVE</code></td><td>Adds a flat value to the stat. Default.</td></tr><tr><td><code>ADDITIVE_MULTIPLIER</code></td><td>Multiplies the base stat — e.g. <code>0.1</code> = +10%</td></tr><tr><td><code>COMPOUND_MULTIPLIER</code></td><td>Multiplies the running total including other multipliers</td></tr><tr><td><code>SETTER</code></td><td>Overrides the stat to the exact value</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr>\n<h4>Math Expressions</h4>\n<p>The <code>AMOUNT</code> field supports <code>&lt;math:&gt;</code> expressions for level-scaling modifiers.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Stats:\n    - ATTACK_DAMAGE &lt;math:enchant_level*2&gt;\n    - CRITICAL_STRIKE_CHANCE &lt;math:enchant_level*3&gt;\n    - MOVEMENT_SPEED &lt;math:enchant_level*0.02&gt; ADDITIVE_MULTIPLIER</code></pre>\n<p>All standard enchantment variables are available: <code>enchant_level</code>, <code>enchant_maxlevel</code>, etc.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Notes</h4>\n<ul><li>Modifiers are identified internally by a stable source key derived from the enchant ID and stat name, ensuring the correct modifier is always removed on unequip.</li><li>Because modifiers are transient, they are lost on server restart and re-applied the next time the item is equipped.</li><li>Unknown stat names will log a warning and produce no effect.</li><li>For item-level attribute modifiers that appear in the item tooltip and persist on the item, use <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/attributes\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Attributes\">Attributes</a> instead.</li></ul>\n<hr>\n<h4>Comparison: Attributes vs MythicStats</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th><code>Attributes</code></th><th><code>MythicStats</code></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mechanic</td><td><code>enchantitemattribute</code></td><td><code>playerstat</code></td></tr><tr><td>System</td><td>Bukkit attribute API</td><td>MythicMobs stat system</td></tr><tr><td>Stored on</td><td>Item metadata</td><td>Entity (transient)</td></tr><tr><td>Visible in tooltip</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Persists across relog</td><td>Yes</td><td>Reapplied on login</td></tr><tr><td>Slot group</td><td>Required</td><td>Not applicable</td></tr><tr><td>Triggers</td><td><code>~onEnchant</code> / <code>~onEnchantRemove</code></td><td><code>~onEquip</code> / <code>~onUnequip</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><code>`</code></p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/MythicStats"},"enchants:vanilla/vanilla-enchantments":{"h":"<p>MythicEnchants can manage, modify and overwrite vanilla enchantments thanks to its modern data-driven approach.  These can be found in <code>plugins/MythicMobs/packs/Vanilla_Enchants/enchantments/</code> and can be fully customized just like any <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/custom-enchantments\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Custom-Enchantments\">custom enchantment</a>, overriding vanilla enchants of the same names.</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<p>📝 <code>Config</code></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>MENDING:\n  MaxLevel: 1</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Vanilla/Vanilla-Enchantments"},"enchants:table/enchanting":{"h":"<p>MythicEnchants manages the vanilla <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/enchanting_table\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">enchanting table</a>&#x27;s offerings while adding features such as live conditional enchanting using <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/enchanting-table\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Enchanting-Table\">enchantment conditions</a> and new <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"table/reagents\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Table/Reagents\">reagent types</a> beyond <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Lapis_lazuli\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Lapis Lazuli</a>.</p>\n<h3>Enchanting Table Plugin Configuration</h3>\n<p>The <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"info/config\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/info/config\">Plugin&#x27;s Config</a> features a section dedicated to global enchanting table behavior, managing the vanilla table with a variety of options when <code>custom-table: true</code>.  (Without MythicEnchants table management, many features such as reagents and enchanting conditions will not take effect).</p>\n<p>The configuration options are explained in comments in the config file itself.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>enchanting:\n  # Disables MythicEnchants providing its own emulated enchanting table.\n  # Required for reagents and conditional enchanting.\n  # All enchantments are registered using vanilla datapack offering settings.\n  custom-table: true\n  # Vanilla-override: register treasure enchants as offered in the table.\n  allow-treasure: false\n  # Whether vanilla enchantments can appear in the custom enchanting table.\n  # When false (default), only custom MythicEnchants enchantments are offered.\n  # When true, vanilla enchantments are filtered using datapack supported_items\n  # tags (authoritative item-type check) and can fill slots that have no custom\n  # enchantment available.\n  vanilla-in-table: true\n  # When true, an empty reagent slot is treated as if vanilla lapis were\n  # present — offers are computed against the &quot;vanilla&quot; reagent bucket and\n  # shown immediately when the player drops in an item. When false (default),\n  # the table waits until the player adds *something* to the reagent slot\n  # before producing offers (vanilla lapis still rolls vanilla-bucket offers,\n  # custom reagents roll their own bucket). Use `true` for the legacy\n  # always-show behavior; `false` for a reagent-gated UX.\n  assume-reagent-lapis: false\n  # Custom-table only. Replaces vanilla&#x27;s hard-coded &quot;1 power per bookshelf,\n  # capped at 15&quot; with a configurable material weight map and three per-slot\n  # equations evaluated against a `count` variable.\n  #\n  #   * `materials` — block ID → power weight. Any block listed here is counted\n  #                   at the same 30 positions vanilla scans for bookshelves.\n  #                   The value is summed (e.g. 5 BOOKSHELF + 2 EMERALD_BLOCK\n  #                   with the weights below → count = 5*1 + 2*3 = 11).\n  #   * `require-line-of-sight` — when true, follows vanilla&#x27;s air-gap rule\n  #                   (the cell between the table and a power block must be\n  #                   air). Stops players cheesing with solid walls.\n  #   * `equations` — exp4j expressions for slot1/slot2/slot3 (top→bottom in\n  #                   the table UI). Variable `count` is the summed power.\n  #                   Functions: `floor`, `ceil`, `min`, `max`, `clamp`,\n  #                   `randomInt(a,b)` (inclusive), plus all standard math.\n  #                   Omit a slot&#x27;s equation to fall back to the vanilla\n  #                   formula for that slot.</code></pre>\n<p>Bookshelves are the vanilla conduit block used for Enchantment power to increase the enchantment levels and offers.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  table-power:\n    materials:\n      BOOKSHELF: 1\n      # EMERALD_BLOCK: 3\n    require-line-of-sight: true\n    # Optional. When omitted, scans vanilla&#x27;s hand-picked 30 positions (the\n    # exact set vanilla uses for bookshelves). When present, replaces that\n    # with a chebyshev-distance cuboid scan around the table.\n    #\n    #   inner — exclusive lower bound on max(|dx|,|dz|). 2 reproduces vanilla&#x27;s\n    #           &quot;shelves can&#x27;t be adjacent to the table&quot; gap. 0 lets blocks\n    #           directly touching the table count.\n    #   outer — inclusive upper bound on max(|dx|,|dz|).\n    #   y-min / y-max — inclusive Y offsets relative to the table block.\n    #                   Vanilla equivalent is 0..1 (two layers).\n    #\n    # LOS rule for wide radii: there&#x27;s no single &quot;cell between table and shelf&quot;\n    # once the radius exceeds 2, so the check approximates by requiring the\n    # cell at (sign(dx), 0, sign(dz)) — the doorway adjacent to the table —\n    # to be replaceable. Solid wall around the table still kills the bonus.\n    # radius:\n    #   inner: 2\n    #   outer: 7\n    #   y-min: 0\n    #   y-max: 1\n    equations:\n      slot1: &quot;floor(min(max((randomInt(1,8)+floor(count/2)+randomInt(0,count))/6, 1), 10))&quot;\n      slot2: &quot;floor(min((((randomInt(1,8)+floor(count/2)+randomInt(0,count))*2)/4)+1, 15))&quot;\n      slot3: &quot;floor(max(((randomInt(1,8)+floor(count/2)+randomInt(0,count))/2)+2, min(20, count*2)))&quot;\n    # After each slot&#x27;s equation evaluates, clamp the result to this maximum.\n    # Saves wrapping every equation in min(...). Defaults shown below\n    # (10/15/30) mirror vanilla&#x27;s progression. To opt a slot out of its cap\n    # so only the global `max-base-level` applies, set it to `0`. Omitting\n    # the entire block keeps the defaults; omitting a single slot also\n    # keeps that slot&#x27;s default.\n    slot-caps:\n      slot1: 10\n      slot2: 15\n      slot3: 30\n    #\n    # Hard upper bound applied last — defaults to 30 to match vanilla&#x27;s\n    # enchanting-table UI. Lifting beyond 30 works (the algorithm will pick\n    # higher-tier enchants for the candidate pool) but the XP-cost number\n    # renders in red and demands that many player levels to confirm. Set\n    # carefully if you want deeper progression than vanilla allows.\n    max-base-level: 30</code></pre>\n<h3>Enchanting Configuration for Enchantments</h3>\n<p><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/custom-enchantments\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Custom-Enchantments\">Enchantments</a> can have their Enchanting Table behavior <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/enchanting-table\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Enchanting-Table\">configured directly</a>.</p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Table/Enchanting"},"enchants:table/reagents":{"h":"<h2>Reagents</h2>\n<h3>Overview</h3>\n<p>Reagents are items placed in the enchanting table&#x27;s lapis slot that control which enchantments appear and how table power scales. Instead of only using vanilla Lapis Lazuli, you can define custom reagent items — such as MythicCrucible items or custom model data lapis — to gate specific enchantments behind specific reagent types.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Reagents require <code>custom-table: true</code> in <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"config/config.yml\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Config/config.yml\">config.yml</a> to function.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>How Reagents Work</h3>\n<ol><li>A player places an item in the enchanting table&#x27;s lapis slot</li><li>MythicEnchants resolves the item to a <b>reagent key</b> using a <span class=\"ilink\">priority-based matcher</span></li><li>The enchantment pool is filtered to only show enchantments that accept that reagent</li><li>Table power equations may be overridden per-reagent to modify slot costs</li></ol>\n<p>Reagent items are <b>consumed</b> — they are read to determine which enchantments to offer, similar to how vanilla uses lapis.</p>\n<h3>Defining Reagents</h3>\n<p>Reagent files are loaded from:</p>\n<ul><li><code>plugins/MythicMobs/Packs/&lt;pack&gt;/Reagents/</code> (pack overlays, loaded second — can override base entries)</li></ul>\n<p>Each YAML file can declare multiple reagents as top-level keys. File names are cosmetic.</p>\n<h4>Structure</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>moondust:\n  matches:\n    mythiccrucible: moondust\n    model-strings:\n      - nexo:item/material/moondust\n    legacy-model-data: 1042\n  table-power:\n    mode: override\n    equations:\n      slot1: &quot;floor(min(count*1.5, 12))&quot;\n      slot2: null\n      slot3: &quot;floor(count*2)&quot;\n    slot-caps:\n      slot1: 12\n      slot3: 35\n    max-base-level: 35</code></pre>\n<h4>Matches Block</h4>\n<p>The <code>matches:</code> block defines how an item in the lapis slot is identified as this reagent.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mythiccrucible</code></td><td>MythicCrucible internal item name (also accepts <code>mythic</code> or <code>crucible</code> as the key)</td></tr><tr><td><code>model-strings</code></td><td>List of custom model data strings to match (case-insensitive)</td></tr><tr><td><code>legacy-model-data</code></td><td>Legacy integer custom model data value</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote><p>Non-vanilla reagents <b>must</b> have at least one matcher. The <code>vanilla</code> key is reserved and never needs matchers.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Table Power Block</h4>\n<p>The optional <code>table-power:</code> block overrides global table power calculations for this reagent.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mode</code></td><td><code>override</code> replaces global equations; <code>additive</code> adds to them</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><code>equations</code></td><td>Per-slot math expressions (<code>slot1</code>, <code>slot2</code>, <code>slot3</code>). Use <code>null</code> to inherit global. Variable <code>count</code> is the power value</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><code>slot-caps</code></td><td>Per-slot upper bounds applied after the equation</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><code>max-base-level</code></td><td>Hard ceiling on the computed base level (overrides global)</td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5>Table Power Resolution Order</h5>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>1. Compute global base value (global equation or vanilla formula)\n2. Apply reagent override/additive:\n   - OVERRIDE: replace with reagent equation (or keep global if null)\n   - ADDITIVE: add reagent equation result to global\n3. Apply cap: min(result, reagent cap or global cap)\n4. Apply ceiling: min(result, reagent ceiling or global ceiling or 30)\n5. Clamp to minimum of 1</code></pre>\n<h3>Using Reagents in Enchantments</h3>\n<p>In an enchantment&#x27;s <code>Enchanting:</code> block, the <code>Reagent</code> list controls which reagents unlock that enchantment at the table:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>LunarLight:\n  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 5\n    Reagent:\n      - moondust\n      - starshard</code></pre>\n<h4>Special Values</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>LAPIS_LAZULI</code></td><td>Vanilla lapis with no metadata (also <code>LAPIS</code> or <code>VANILLA</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>ALL</code></td><td>Enchantment appears for <b>any</b> reagent (also <code>*</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><i>(omitted)</i></td><td>If <code>Reagent</code> is not specified, defaults to vanilla lapis only</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Examples</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Only appears with moondust reagent\nLunarEnchant:\n  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 10\n    Reagent:\n      - moondust\n\n# Appears with any reagent\nUniversalEnchant:\n  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 5\n    Reagent:\n      - ALL\n\n# Appears with vanilla lapis or a specific custom item\nHybridEnchant:\n  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 8\n    Reagent:\n      - LAPIS_LAZULI\n      - starshard\n\n# No Reagent field = vanilla lapis only (default behavior)\nBasicEnchant:\n  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 15</code></pre>\n<h3>Item Resolution Order</h3>\n<p>When a player places an item in the lapis slot, MythicEnchants resolves it to a reagent key using this priority:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Priority</th><th>Method</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td><b>Declared reagent matchers</b> — checks <code>mythiccrucible</code>, <code>model-strings</code>, and <code>legacy-model-data</code> fields in order</td><td><code>moondust</code> (via Crucible internal name)</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><b>Plain vanilla lapis</b> — <code>LAPIS_LAZULI</code> material with no custom metadata</td><td><code>vanilla</code></td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><b>MythicCrucible API lookup</b> — queries MythicBukkit for the item&#x27;s internal name</td><td><code>starshard</code></td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><b>Custom model string</b> — reads Paper&#x27;s <code>CustomModelDataComponent</code> first string value</td><td><code>nexo:item/material/gem</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Vanilla Reagent Override</h3>\n<p>The reserved <code>vanilla</code> key lets you override table power for plain lapis without needing matchers:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>vanilla:\n  table-power:\n    mode: additive\n    equations:\n      slot1: &quot;1&quot;\n      slot2: &quot;1&quot;\n      slot3: &quot;1&quot;</code></pre>\n<h3>Supported Reagent Types</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Description</th><th>Matcher Field</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vanilla Lapis Lazuli</td><td>Standard <code>LAPIS_LAZULI</code> material</td><td>Automatic (keyword <code>LAPIS_LAZULI</code>)</td></tr><tr><td>MythicCrucible Items</td><td>Items created by MythicCrucible</td><td><code>mythiccrucible</code></td></tr><tr><td>Custom Model Data Strings</td><td>Items with Paper <code>CustomModelDataComponent</code> strings</td><td><code>model-strings</code></td></tr><tr><td>Legacy Custom Model Data</td><td>Items with integer custom model data</td><td><code>legacy-model-data</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Config Settings</h3>\n<p>These settings in <code>config.yml</code> affect reagent behavior:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>enchanting:\n  custom-table: true              # Must be true for reagents to work\n  assume-reagent-lapis: false     # false = wait for reagent in slot before showing offers\n                                  # true = show vanilla-eligible offers even with empty slot</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Table/Reagents"},"enchants:datapack/tags":{"h":"<h3>Custom datapack tags</h3>\n<p>You can define your own datapack tags from YAML and have MythicEnchants generate the JSON into the installed datapack. Put files at:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>&lt;MythicMobs pack&gt;/datapack/&lt;namespace&gt;/tags/&lt;registry&gt;/&lt;file&gt;.yml</code></pre>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;namespace&gt;</code> — the tag&#x27;s namespace (e.g. <code>mythicenchants</code>, <code>minecraft</code>).</li><li><code>&lt;registry&gt;</code> — the vanilla tag registry. <b><code>item</code></b> is supported today; the system is registry-keyed, so other registries can be added later by dropping files in their folder.</li></ul>\n<p>Each file declares one tag. Two shapes:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>farming_tools:                 # full form\n  replace: false\n  values:\n    - &quot;#minecraft:hoes&quot;        # tag reference (passed through)\n    - minecraft:shears         # material (bare DIAMOND_HOE or namespaced both work)\n    - mythic:Fire_Axe          # MythicMobs/Crucible item → resolved to its BASE MATERIAL\n\nmining_special:                # shorthand: a bare value list (replace = false)\n  - DIAMOND_PICKAXE\n  - mythic:Crucible_Drill</code></pre>\n<p>Generated to <code>data/&lt;namespace&gt;/tags/item/&lt;key&gt;.json</code>. Reference the tag anywhere a tag is accepted, e.g. <code>SupportedItems: &#x27;#mythicenchants:farming_tools&#x27;</code> or in <code>PrimaryItems</code>. Tags with the same id across multiple packs are merged. Unknown materials / unresolvable <code>mythic:</code> items are skipped with a warning (the rest of the tag still generates).</p>\n<blockquote><p><b><code>mythic:</code> resolves to a material, not the exact item.</b> Datapack tags match by item type, so <code>mythic:Fire_Axe</code> contributes its base material (e.g. <code>netherite_axe</code>) — the tag then matches <i>all</i> netherite axes. To restrict an enchant to the <b>specific</b> Mythic/Crucible item, see <i>StrictMythicItems</i> below.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Restricting an enchant to a specific Mythic/Crucible item</h3>\n<p>Add <code>mythic:&lt;id&gt;</code> entries to <code>PrimaryItems</code> and set <code>StrictMythicItems: true</code>:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>my_crucible_enchant:\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/sharp_weapon&#x27;\n  PrimaryItems: [&#x27;mythic:Fire_Axe&#x27;]\n  Options:\n    StrictMythicItems: true     # (top-level StrictMythicItems: true also works)</code></pre>\n<p>With the flag on, the enchant can only be applied to the exact Mythic item(s) listed — enforced at runtime on the enchanting table, anvil, the <code>enchant{}</code> mechanic, and the <code>applyEnchantment</code> API. Without <code>mythic:</code> entries the flag is a no-op. (The datapack still only knows the material, so this runtime check is what makes the restriction exact.)</p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Datapack/Tags"},"enchants:skript/skript":{"h":"<h2>MythicEnchantsSkript</h2>\n<p>A Skript addon that exposes MythicEnchants&#x27; Java facade API as Skript syntax — script against enchantment logic (apply/remove, table offers, anvil results, triggers, counters, and more) in <code>.sk</code> files without writing Java.</p>\n<p>Unlike the other addons in this list, this is a <b>standalone plugin</b>, not a <code>plugins/MythicEnchants/addons/</code> drop-in — it depends on Skript and MythicEnchants directly, as its own plugin.</p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul><li><b>147 syntax classes across 5 categories</b> — one custom type, 6 events, ~69 expressions, 44 conditions, 26 effects, all namespaced under the <code>mench</code> keyword so they&#x27;re easy to spot and grep in scripts.</li><li><b>Six events</b>, four of them cancellable, covering the full enchant lifecycle: apply, remove, skill-trigger-about-to-fire, table-offer-preparation, anvil-result-preparation, and a catch-all trigger-fire bridge for any subscribed trigger name — even on items with no matching enchant.</li><li><b>The anvil result is settable, not just readable.</b> <code>set mench anvil result to ...</code> inside the Anvil Prepare event lets a script override the anvil&#x27;s outcome entirely — the documented use case is honoring &quot;overleveled&quot; books past vanilla&#x27;s usual level-5 clamp.</li><li><b>Deep item and definition introspection.</b> Enchant levels, all/registered/custom enchant keys, enchantability, curses, total level across all equipped gear, applicable definitions for an item, rarity/reagent registry listings, tag membership, stored/book-enchant round-tripping via a portable <code>&quot;id:level&quot;</code> snapshot string, and more.</li><li><b>Live config/feature-flag conditions.</b> ~16 conditions read the server&#x27;s actual running MythicEnchants config directly — custom table enabled, datapack auto-generation, debug mode, cleanup settings, anvil/grindstone behavior — so scripts can branch on how the server is actually configured instead of hardcoding assumptions.</li><li><b>Named, expiring counters</b>, both player- and item-scoped, with tick/second expiry strings — a general-purpose scripting primitive for cooldowns, charges, or any per-player/per-item numeric state that shouldn&#x27;t need its own variable-management boilerplate.</li></ul>\n<h3>Requirements</h3>\n<ul><li>Skript 2.15+</li><li>MythicEnchants 5.12+</li><li>Paper 1.21.11+</li></ul>\n<h3>Install</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>MythicEnchantsSkript.jar -&gt; plugins/</code></pre>\n<h3><a href=\"https://github.com/Stellius-Studio/MythicEnchantsSkript/releases/tag/1.3.0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">DOWNLOAD</a></h3>\n<p>A normal plugin install, alongside Skript and MythicEnchants (not nested under either plugin&#x27;s own folder). Restart.</p>\n<h3>Syntax reference</h3>\n<p>The full syntax reference — every event, expression, condition, and effect, with signatures and examples — lives in <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"skript/syntax\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/skript/SYNTAX\"><code>SYNTAX</code></a>. This README stays at the overview level; that file is the authoritative doc for writing scripts against it.</p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/skript/skript"},"enchants:skript/syntax":{"h":"<h2>MythicEnchantsSkript — Syntax Reference</h2>\n<p>Skript addon for MythicEnchants. Requires <b>Skript 2.15+</b> and <b>MythicEnchants 5.12+</b> on Paper 1.21+. Addon version <b>1.3.0</b>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Types</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Code Name</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>MythicEnchants Enchantment</td><td><code>menchenchantment</code></td><td>A custom enchantment registered through MythicEnchants. Parseable by ID (e.g. <code>&quot;fire_slash&quot;</code> or <code>&quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot;</code>).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr>\n<h3>Events</h3>\n<p>Of the six events, four are <b>cancellable</b> via Skript&#x27;s built-in <code>cancel event</code>: enchant apply, enchant remove, prepare enchant, and skill trigger. The two newest event bridges — <b>anvil prepare</b> and <b>trigger fire</b> — are <b>not</b> cancellable; the anvil-prepare event is instead &quot;overridden&quot; by setting <code>mench anvil result</code> (see below).</p>\n<h4>On Mythic Enchantment Apply</h4>\n<p>Fires when enchantments are applied to an item via enchanting table or anvil. Cancellable.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>[mythic[al]] enchant[ment] apply\nmench enchant[ment] apply</code></pre>\n<p><b>Event values:</b> <code>player</code>, <code>item</code> (ItemStack)</p>\n<p><b>Event-only expressions:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>mench apply source</code> — <code>&quot;TABLE&quot;</code> or <code>&quot;ANVIL&quot;</code></li><li><code>mench event slot</code> — equipment slot name (e.g. <code>&quot;HAND&quot;</code>) (shared with the remove event)</li></ul>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>on mythic enchantment apply:\n    if mench apply source is &quot;TABLE&quot;:\n        send &quot;You enchanted %event-item% at the table!&quot; to player</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>On Mythic Enchantment Remove</h4>\n<p>Fires when enchantments are removed from an item via grindstone or anvil. Cancellable.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>[mythic[al]] enchant[ment] remove\nmench enchant[ment] remove</code></pre>\n<p><b>Event values:</b> <code>player</code>, <code>item</code> (ItemStack)</p>\n<p><b>Event-only expressions:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>mench remove source</code> — <code>&quot;GRINDSTONE&quot;</code> or <code>&quot;ANVIL&quot;</code></li><li><code>mench event slot</code> — equipment slot name (shared with the apply event)</li></ul>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>on mythic enchantment remove:\n    if mench remove source is &quot;GRINDSTONE&quot;:\n        send &quot;Enchantments stripped!&quot; to player</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>On Mythic Enchantment Skill Trigger</h4>\n<p>Fires before MythicEnchants dispatches an enchantment&#x27;s skills. One event fires per (enchantment, trigger) pair. Cancellable — cancelling suppresses that enchantment&#x27;s skill dispatch only.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>[mythic[al]] enchant[ment] skill trigger\nmench skill trigger</code></pre>\n<p><b>Event values:</b> <code>player</code>, <code>item</code> (ItemStack), <code>entity</code> (target, nullable), <code>menchenchantment</code> (the definition)</p>\n<p><b>Event-only expressions:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>mench trigger name</code> — uppercase trigger name (e.g. <code>&quot;ATTACK&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;EQUIP&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;TIMER&quot;</code>) (shared with trigger fire)</li><li><code>mench trigger level</code> — enchantment level on the item (skill trigger only)</li><li><code>mench trigger damage</code> — final damage value, 0 if not a damage trigger (shared with trigger fire)</li><li><code>mench trigger item attack</code> — base item attack value, 0 if not an attack trigger (shared with trigger fire)</li><li><code>mench trigger slot</code> — equipment slot name (e.g. <code>&quot;HAND&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;CHEST&quot;</code>) (shared with trigger fire)</li></ul>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>on mythic enchantment skill trigger:\n    if mench trigger name is &quot;ATTACK&quot;:\n        if mench trigger damage &gt; 20:\n            send &quot;Massive hit with %mench id of event-menchenchantment% level %mench trigger level%!&quot; to player\n    if mench trigger slot is &quot;CHEST&quot;:\n        cancel event  # suppress all chest-slot enchant skills</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>On Mythic Prepare Enchantment</h4>\n<p>Fires after MythicEnchants computes the three enchanting table offers but before they are shown to the player. Only fires when the custom enchanting table is enabled. Cancellable — cancelling leaves the vanilla offers untouched.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>[mythic[al]] prepare enchant[ment]\nmench prepare enchant[ment]</code></pre>\n<p><b>Event values:</b> <code>player</code>, <code>item</code> (ItemStack)</p>\n<p><b>Event-only expressions:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>mench table power</code> — computed table power (typically 0–15, can exceed with custom configs)</li><li><code>mench reagent key</code> — normalised reagent key (e.g. <code>&quot;minecraft:lapis_lazuli&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;crucible:moondust&quot;</code>)</li></ul>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>on mythic prepare enchantment:\n    if mench reagent key is &quot;crucible:moondust&quot;:\n        send &quot;Special reagent detected! Table power: %mench table power%&quot; to player</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>On MythicEnchants Trigger Fire</h4>\n<p>Fires whenever a subscribed trigger name fires on an item — including items with <b>no matching enchantment</b> — unlike the narrower skill-trigger event, which only fires per (enchantment, trigger) pair. Use <code>mench subscribe to trigger %string%</code> first to opt into a given trigger name. <b>Not cancellable.</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>[mythic[al]] enchant[ment] trigger fire\nmench trigger fire</code></pre>\n<p><b>Event values:</b> <code>player</code>, <code>item</code> (ItemStack), <code>entity</code> (target, nullable)</p>\n<p><b>Event-only expressions</b> (all shared with the skill-trigger event above):</p>\n<ul><li><code>mench trigger name</code></li><li><code>mench trigger damage</code></li><li><code>mench trigger item attack</code></li><li><code>mench trigger slot</code></li></ul>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>mench subscribe to trigger &quot;BLOCK_BREAK&quot;\n\non mench trigger fire:\n    if mench trigger name is &quot;BLOCK_BREAK&quot;:\n        send &quot;Trigger fired on %event-item%, even with no matching enchant!&quot; to player</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>On MythicEnchants Anvil Prepare</h4>\n<p>Fires after MythicEnchants computes the anvil combine result but before it&#x27;s shown in the anvil UI. <b>Not cancellable</b> — instead of cancelling, override the outcome by setting <code>mench anvil result</code>. This hook exists specifically so scripts can honor &quot;overleveled&quot; enchanted books past vanilla&#x27;s level clamp (e.g. allow a level-6 Sharpness book to combine onto a level-6 sword when vanilla would cap it at 5).</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>[mythic[al]] anvil prepare\nmench anvil prepare</code></pre>\n<p><b>Event values:</b> <code>player</code>, <code>item</code> (the result ItemStack)</p>\n<p><b>Event-only expressions:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>mench anvil left item</code> — the base item (anvil slot 1)</li><li><code>mench anvil right item</code> — the sacrifice item (anvil slot 2)</li><li><code>mench anvil result</code> — <b>gettable and settable.</b> See below.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Example — the standout capability, overriding the result:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>on mench anvil prepare:\n    if {_shouldOverride}:\n        set mench anvil result to {_myOverleveledBook}</code></pre>\n<p><code>mench anvil result</code> getting returns the override result if one has already been set that tick, otherwise the vanilla/core-computed result. Setting it replaces the anvil&#x27;s output outright — this is the only way to influence this event, since it cannot be cancelled.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Expressions</h3>\n<h4>Item Enchantment Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench level of %string% on %itemstack%</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>Level of a specific enchantment (by namespaced key) on an item. Returns 0 if absent. Resolves by key, so it works before the datapack is applied.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench enchantments of %itemstack%</code> / <code>%itemstack%&#x27;s mench enchantments</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>All enchantment namespaced keys on an item (vanilla and custom).</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench (registered\\|custom) enchantments of %itemstack%</code> / <code>%itemstack%&#x27;s mench (registered\\|custom) enchantments</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>Only the MythicEnchants-registered enchantment keys on an item.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench enchantability of %itemstack%</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>Resolved enchantability (config overrides + vanilla defaults). Returns <code>-1</code> if the custom table is disabled.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench curses of %itemstack%</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>IDs of all cursed MythicEnchants enchantments present on an item.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench custom item id of %itemstack%</code></td><td>String</td><td>Custom-item id (MythicMobs, Nexo, ItemsAdder, CraftEngine, etc.) detected on an item, or nothing if unrecognized.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench total [enchant[ment]] level of %string% (on\\|for) %livingentity%</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>Summed level of an enchantment across all of a living entity&#x27;s equipped items.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench (applicable\\|valid) [enchantment] definitions (for\\|of) %itemstack%</code></td><td>menchenchantments</td><td>All enchantment definitions that can be applied to an item.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_lvl} to mench level of &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot; on player&#x27;s tool\nsend &quot;%mench enchantments of player&#x27;s tool%&quot;\nsend &quot;%mench registered enchantments of player&#x27;s tool%&quot;\nsend &quot;Enchantability: %mench enchantability of player&#x27;s tool%&quot;\nset {_curses::*} to mench curses of {_item}\nset {_id} to mench custom item id of {_item}\nset {_total} to mench total level of &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot; on player\nset {_defs::*} to all mench applicable definitions for {_item}</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Definition Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench enchantment %string%</code></td><td>menchenchantment</td><td>Get a definition by ID (bare or namespaced).</td></tr><tr><td><code>[all] mench [enchantment] definitions</code></td><td>menchenchantments</td><td>All registered enchantment definitions.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench (id\\|display name\\|description\\|rarity\\|min level\\|max level\\|anvil cost\\|supported items\\|namespace\\|key\\|translation key\\|strict mythic items) of %menchenchantment%</code></td><td>Object</td><td>Gets properties of a definition: id, display name, description, rarity, min/max level, anvil cost, supported items, namespace, key, translation key, or strict mythic items (whether application is locked to its <code>mythic:</code> items).</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench max level of %string%</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>Max level of an enchantment by id, without needing a resolved definition.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench rarity of %string%</code></td><td>String</td><td>Display name of the rarity tier assigned to an enchantment id (by id, not definition).</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench conflicts of %menchenchantment%</code> / <code>%menchenchantment%&#x27;s mench conflicts</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>Raw conflicting enchantment/tag refs.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench reagents of %menchenchantment%</code> / <code>%menchenchantment%&#x27;s mench reagents</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>Accepted reagent strings. <code>&quot;VANILLA&quot;</code> if vanilla-only, <code>&quot;ALL&quot;</code> if any.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench (valid\\|enchant) slots of %menchenchantment%</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>Valid equipment slot names (e.g. <code>MAINHAND</code>, <code>HEAD</code>, or <code>ALL</code>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench tags of %menchenchantment%</code> / <code>%menchenchantment%&#x27;s mench tags</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>Tag IDs this enchantment belongs to.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_def} to mench enchantment &quot;fire_slash&quot;\nsend &quot;Name: %mench display name of {_def}%&quot;\nsend &quot;Rarity: %mench rarity of {_def}%&quot;\nsend &quot;Levels: %mench min level of {_def}%-%mench max level of {_def}%&quot;\nsend &quot;Tags: %mench tags of {_def}%&quot;\nsend &quot;Conflicts: %mench conflicts of {_def}%&quot;\nsend &quot;Reagents: %mench reagents of {_def}%&quot;\nsend mench rarity of &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot;\nsend &quot;%mench max level of &quot;&quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot;&quot;%&quot;\n\nloop all mench definitions:\n    send &quot;%mench id of loop-value%: %mench display name of loop-value%&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Rarity &amp; Reagent Registry Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>[all] mench rarities</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>Display names of every registered rarity tier (built-in and custom).</td></tr><tr><td><code>[all] mench reagent keys</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>Every registered custom reagent key.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench enchantments accepting [reagent] %string%</code></td><td>menchenchantments</td><td>Definitions that accept the given reagent key at the custom enchanting table.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_rarities::*} to all mench rarities\nset {_keys::*} to all mench reagent keys\nset {_defs::*} to mench enchantments accepting reagent &quot;crucible:moondust&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Tag Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench enchantments in tag %string%</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>All enchantment IDs that are members of a given tag.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench (resolved\\|expanded) [enchantment] (ids\\|refs) (of\\|from) %strings%</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>Expands a mix of enchantment id refs and <code>#tag</code> refs into a flat list of fully-qualified ids.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_members::*} to mench enchantments in tag &quot;mythicenchants:celestial_pack&quot;\nsend &quot;Celestial pack has %size of {_members::*}% enchantments&quot;\nset {_ids::*} to mench resolved ids of &quot;sharpness&quot;, &quot;minecraft:smite&quot; and &quot;#celestial_pack&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Stored/Book Enchant Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>[a] mench book (with\\|containing) %strings%</code></td><td>ItemStack</td><td>Creates an enchanted book carrying the given enchantments. See encoding note below.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench enchant[ment] snapshot of %itemstack%</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>Snapshot of all MythicEnchants enchantments on an item as <code>&quot;id:level&quot;</code> strings. Round-trips with <code>mench restore enchantment snapshot</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench stored enchantments of %itemstack%</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>All stored-enchantment IDs on an item (e.g. an enchanted book&#x27;s storage meta).</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench mythic stored enchantments of %itemstack%</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>Only the MythicEnchants-registered stored-enchantment IDs on an item.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench stored [enchant[ment]] level of %string% (on\\|in) %itemstack%</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>Stored enchantment level of an enchantment id on an item (e.g. a book).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b><code>&quot;id:level&quot;</code> encoding convention:</b> <code>mench book with/containing</code>, <code>mench enchantment snapshot of</code>, and <code>mench restore enchantment snapshot</code> (effect, below) all use a string format of <code>&quot;namespace:key:level&quot;</code> — the full enchant id (which itself contains a <code>:</code> for its namespace) followed by a final <code>:level</code> suffix. Parsing splits on the <b>last</b> <code>:</code> in the string, so <code>&quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash:3&quot;</code> is read as id <code>mythicenchants:fire_slash</code> at level <code>3</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_book} to mench book with &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash:3&quot;\nset {_book} to mench book containing &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash:3&quot; and &quot;mythicenchants:lunar_light:2&quot;\n\nset {_snap::*} to mench enchantment snapshot of {_item}\nmench restore enchantment snapshot {_snap::*} to {_item}\n\nset {_stored::*} to mench stored enchantments of {_book}\nset {_mythic::*} to mench mythic stored enchantments of {_book}\nset {_lvl} to mench stored enchant level of &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot; on {_book}</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Mob, Table &amp; Seed Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench override (for\\|of) [enchant[ment]] %string% on [mob] %string%</code></td><td>String</td><td>The per-mob <code>ApplicableEnchants</code> override: <code>&quot;enabled&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;disabled&quot;</code>, or <code>&quot;vanilla&quot;</code> when none is set.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench [table] offers (for\\|of) %player%</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>The enchantment ids currently offered to a player at a custom table (one per occupied slot). Empty if the table is disabled or there are no cached offers.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench enchant seed of %player%</code> / <code>%player%&#x27;s mench enchant seed</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>The player&#x27;s current enchanting seed (determines table offers).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>send &quot;%mench override for enchant &quot;&quot;minecraft:smite&quot;&quot; on mob &quot;&quot;ZOMBIE&quot;&quot;%&quot;\nset {_offers::*} to mench table offers for player\nsend &quot;Your enchant seed: %mench enchant seed of player%&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Migration Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench migration target of %string%</code></td><td>String</td><td>The enchantment ID that a given (old/removed) enchantment ID is migrated to, or nothing if not migrated.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_target} to mench migration target of &quot;mythicenchants:old_fire_slash&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Option Expressions (Config Options section)</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench raw option %string% of %string%</code></td><td>Object</td><td>Raw value from an enchantment definition&#x27;s Options section by key. No type conversion or fallback. Empty if unset.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench boolean option %string% of %string% (else\\|otherwise) %boolean%</code></td><td>Boolean</td><td>Boolean value from an Options section by key, falling back to a default if missing.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench integer option %string% of %string% (else\\|otherwise) %integer%</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>Integer value from an Options section by key, falling back to a default if missing.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench string option %string% of %string% (else\\|otherwise) %string%</code></td><td>String</td><td>String value from an Options section by key, falling back to a default if missing.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_v} to mench raw option &quot;MyCustomFlag&quot; of &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot;\nset {_v} to mench boolean option &quot;MyCustomFlag&quot; of &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot; else false\nset {_v} to mench integer option &quot;MyCustomCount&quot; of &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot; else 0\nset {_v} to mench string option &quot;MyCustomLabel&quot; of &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot; else &quot;default&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>PDC (Persistent Data Container) Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench pdc boolean %string% (of\\|on) %itemstack% (else\\|otherwise) %boolean%</code></td><td>Boolean</td><td>Boolean value stored in an item&#x27;s PDC by key, with a fallback.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench pdc integer %string% (of\\|on) %itemstack% (else\\|otherwise) %integer%</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>Integer value stored in an item&#x27;s PDC by key, with a fallback.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench pdc number %string% (of\\|on) %itemstack% (else\\|otherwise) %number%</code></td><td>Number</td><td>Decimal value stored in an item&#x27;s PDC by key, with a fallback.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench pdc string %string% (of\\|on) %itemstack% (else\\|otherwise) %string%</code></td><td>String</td><td>String value stored in an item&#x27;s PDC by key, with a fallback.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_v} to mench pdc boolean &quot;myKey&quot; of {_item} else false\nset {_v} to mench pdc integer &quot;myKey&quot; of {_item} else 0\nset {_v} to mench pdc number &quot;myKey&quot; of {_item} else 0\nset {_v} to mench pdc string &quot;myKey&quot; of {_item} else &quot;default&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Anvil/Grindstone Config Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench anvil cost multiplier</code></td><td>Number</td><td>Configured multiplier applied to anvil repair/combine costs.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench grindstone xp return percent</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>Configured percentage of XP returned when removing enchantments at the grindstone.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>send &quot;Cost multiplier: %mench anvil cost multiplier%&quot;\nsend &quot;XP return: %mench grindstone xp return percent%%%&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Anvil Prepare Event Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench anvil left [item]</code></td><td>ItemStack</td><td>The base item (anvil slot 1). Event-only (<code>mench anvil prepare</code>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench anvil right [item]</code></td><td>ItemStack</td><td>The sacrifice item (anvil slot 2). Event-only (<code>mench anvil prepare</code>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench anvil result</code></td><td>ItemStack</td><td><b>Gettable and settable.</b> Getting returns the override result if set, otherwise the computed result. Setting replaces the anvil&#x27;s output (e.g. to mint an &quot;overleveled&quot; enchanted book). Event-only (<code>mench anvil prepare</code>).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_base} to mench anvil left item\nset {_sacrifice} to mench anvil right item\n\non mench anvil prepare:\n    if {_shouldOverride}:\n        set mench anvil result to {_myOverleveledBook}</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>General Config Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench datapack name</code></td><td>String</td><td>Configured name of the MythicEnchants generated datapack.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench language</code></td><td>String</td><td>Configured MythicEnchants language/locale code.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench max enchantments per item</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>Configured maximum number of MythicEnchants enchantments allowed on a single item.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>send &quot;Datapack: %mench datapack name%&quot;\nsend &quot;Language: %mench language%&quot;\nsend &quot;Max: %mench max enchantments per item%&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Apply/Remove Event Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench apply source</code></td><td>String</td><td><code>&quot;TABLE&quot;</code> or <code>&quot;ANVIL&quot;</code>. Event-only (<code>mench enchantment apply</code>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench remove source</code></td><td>String</td><td><code>&quot;GRINDSTONE&quot;</code> or <code>&quot;ANVIL&quot;</code>. Event-only (<code>mench enchantment remove</code>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench event slot</code></td><td>String</td><td>Equipment slot name. Event-only (<code>mench enchantment apply</code> or <code>mench enchantment remove</code>).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>if mench apply source is &quot;TABLE&quot;:\nif mench remove source is &quot;GRINDSTONE&quot;:\nif mench event slot is &quot;HAND&quot;:</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Prepare Enchant Event Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench table power</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>Computed table power. Event-only (<code>mench prepare enchantment</code>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench reagent key</code></td><td>String</td><td>Normalised reagent key (e.g. <code>&quot;minecraft:lapis_lazuli&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;crucible:moondust&quot;</code>). Event-only (<code>mench prepare enchantment</code>).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>if mench table power &gt;= 15:\nif mench reagent key is &quot;crucible:moondust&quot;:</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Trigger Event Expressions (Skill Trigger &amp; Trigger Fire)</h4>\n<p>These five expressions all work in <b>both</b> <code>mench skill trigger</code> and <code>mench trigger fire</code> events, except <code>mench trigger level</code> which is skill-trigger only.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench trigger name</code></td><td>String</td><td>Trigger name (e.g. <code>&quot;ATTACK&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;EQUIP&quot;</code>). Works in skill trigger and trigger fire.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench trigger level</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>Enchantment level on the item. Skill trigger only.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench trigger damage</code></td><td>Number</td><td>Final damage value; 0 if not a damage trigger. Works in skill trigger and trigger fire.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench trigger item attack</code></td><td>Number</td><td>Base item attack value; 0 if not an attack trigger. Works in skill trigger and trigger fire.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench trigger slot</code></td><td>String</td><td>Equipment slot name (e.g. <code>&quot;HAND&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;OFF_HAND&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;HEAD&quot;</code>). Works in skill trigger and trigger fire.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>if mench trigger name is &quot;ATTACK&quot;:\nset {_lvl} to mench trigger level\nif mench trigger damage &gt; 10:\n    cancel event\nset {_base_atk} to mench trigger item attack\nif mench trigger slot is &quot;HAND&quot;:</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Counter Expressions</h4>\n<p>Counters are named, expiring <code>long</code> values scoped either to a player or to an item&#x27;s persistent data.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench [player] counter %string% of %player%</code></td><td>Long</td><td>Current value of a named player-scoped counter. <code>0</code> if unset/expired.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench [item] counter %string% of %itemstack%</code></td><td>Long</td><td>Current value of a named item-scoped counter. <code>0</code> if unset/expired.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_v} to mench player counter &quot;kills&quot; of player\nset {_v} to mench item counter &quot;uses&quot; of {_item}</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Pet Ownership Expression</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench pet owner of %livingentity%</code></td><td>Player</td><td>Resolved owner/rider of a companion entity (e.g. tamed pet or mount). Nothing if unresolved.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_owner} to mench pet owner of {_wolf}</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Table Power Expressions</h4>\n<p>Direct access to the exact math the custom enchanting table uses, independent of the <code>mench prepare enchantment</code> event.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench table power at %location%</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>Computed table power at an arbitrary location (bookshelves/state-based weight rules).</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench table slot %integer% base level (for\\|at\\|with) power %integer%</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>Base enchanting level offered for a table slot index (<code>0</code>-<code>2</code>) at a given table power.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_power} to mench table power at {_tableLoc}\nset {_lvl} to mench table slot 0 base level for power 15</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Reagent Introspection Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench reagent key (for\\|of) %itemstack%</code></td><td>String</td><td>The reagent pool key an item resolves to (custom or <code>vanilla:</code>-prefixed). Nothing if it isn&#x27;t a declared reagent.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench reagent pool entries of %string%</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>Raw pool entries declared for a reagent key.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_key} to mench reagent key for {_item}\nset {_entries::*} to mench reagent pool entries of &quot;my_reagent&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Table Offer Detail Expressions</h4>\n<p>Parallel arrays to <code>mench table offers for %player%</code> (enchantment ids) — same index maps to the same offer slot.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench [table] offer costs (for\\|of) %player%</code></td><td>Integers</td><td>XP-level costs of a player&#x27;s current table offers.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench [table] offer levels (for\\|of) %player%</code></td><td>Integers</td><td>Enchantment levels of a player&#x27;s current table offers.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_costs::*} to mench offer costs for player\nset {_levels::*} to mench offer levels for player</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>MythicMobs Item Bridging Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench mythic item type of %itemstack%</code></td><td>String</td><td>MythicMobs mythic item type ID of an item. Nothing if not a Mythic item or MythicMobs is unavailable.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench material (for\\|of) [mythic] %string%</code></td><td>Material</td><td>Resolves a mythic item reference (e.g. <code>&quot;my_item&quot;</code>) to its backing vanilla <code>Material</code>. Nothing if unresolved.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_type} to mench mythic item type of {_item}\nset {_mat} to mench material for mythic &quot;my_item&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Datapack Tag Introspection Expressions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>[all] mench known enchantable tags</code></td><td>Strings</td><td>Every datapack enchantable tag reference known to MythicEnchants.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_tags::*} to all mench known enchantable tags</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Conditions</h3>\n<h4>Item Conditions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>%itemstack% has mench enchant[ment] %string%</code></td><td>Whether the item has the enchantment (by namespaced key). Supports negation (<code>doesn&#x27;t have</code>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>%itemstack% is mench enchanted</code></td><td>Whether the item carries at least one MythicEnchants-registered enchantment. Supports negation.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%itemstack% has [a] mench curse</code></td><td>Whether an item has at least one cursed MythicEnchants enchantment. Supports negation.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%itemstack% is mench stored enchanted</code></td><td>Whether an item&#x27;s stored enchantments (e.g. a book) include at least one MythicEnchants-registered enchantment. Supports negation.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%itemstack% has [a] mench active enchant[ment] for trigger[s] %strings%</code></td><td>Whether an item has a MythicEnchants enchantment active for at least one of the given trigger names. Supports negation.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%itemstack%&#x27;[s] mench enchant[ment] tooltip is hidden</code></td><td>Whether an item&#x27;s enchantment tooltip is hidden. Supports negation.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%itemstack% has mench pdc [key] %string%</code></td><td>Whether an item has a value stored in its PDC under the given key. Supports negation.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%itemstack% mench matches %string%</code></td><td>Whether an item matches an item reference string (vanilla material, <code>&quot;mythic:ID&quot;</code>, or a custom-item integration ref). Supports negation.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%string% mench (is\\|can be) applied to %itemstack%</code></td><td>Whether an enchantment id can be applied to an item (supported item types, strict mythic items, etc). Supports negation (<code>can&#x27;t be applied to</code>).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>All support negation.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>if player&#x27;s tool has mench enchantment &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot;:\nif {_item} has a mench curse:\nif {_book} is mench stored enchanted:\nif {_item} has a mench active enchant for triggers &quot;ATTACK&quot; and &quot;KILL&quot;:\nif {_item}&#x27;s mench enchantment tooltip is hidden:\nif {_item} has mench pdc key &quot;myKey&quot;:\nif {_item} mench matches &quot;mythic:excalibur&quot;:\nif &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot; mench can be applied to {_item}:</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Definition Conditions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>%menchenchantment% is mench cursed</code></td><td>Whether the definition is marked as a curse.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%menchenchantment% is mench treasure</code></td><td>Whether the definition is treasure-only.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%menchenchantment% is mench tradeable</code></td><td>Whether villagers may offer the enchantment.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%menchenchantment% is mench enabled</code></td><td>Whether the definition is enabled.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%string% is mench registered</code></td><td>Whether an enchantment ID exists in the registry.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%string% is mench migrated</code></td><td>Whether an enchantment ID has a configured migration target.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%string% is [a] mench orphaned enchant[ment]</code></td><td>Whether an enchantment ID is orphaned (no longer registered and not migrated).</td></tr><tr><td><code>%string% is [a] mench curse enchant[ment]</code></td><td>Whether a vanilla enchantment (resolved by namespaced key) is considered a curse by MythicEnchants&#x27; anvil/grindstone logic.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>All support negation (<code>isn&#x27;t mench cursed</code>, <code>is not mench registered</code>, etc.).</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_def} to mench enchantment &quot;fire_slash&quot;\nif {_def} is mench cursed:\n    send &quot;This enchantment is a curse!&quot;\nif &quot;fire_slash&quot; is mench registered:\n    send &quot;Fire Slash is registered&quot;\nif &quot;mythicenchants:old_fire_slash&quot; is mench migrated:\n    send &quot;Migrated to %mench migration target of &quot;&quot;mythicenchants:old_fire_slash&quot;&quot;%&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Apply-Result Conditions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>[the] last mench apply succeeded</code></td><td>Whether the most recent <code>mench apply</code> effect applied the enchantment.</td></tr><tr><td><code>[the] last mench apply (failed\\|did(n&#x27;t\\| not) succeed)</code></td><td>Inverse — true when the last <code>mench apply</code> did not apply (unknown key, datapack not applied, or blocked by <code>StrictMythicItems</code>).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Check on the line right after a <code>mench apply</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>mench apply &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot; at level 3 to player&#x27;s tool\nif last mench apply succeeded:\n    send &quot;Enchanted!&quot; to player</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Tag &amp; Conflict Conditions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>%string% is in mench tag %string%</code></td><td>Whether an enchantment ID is a member of a tag. Supports negation.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%menchenchantment% mench conflicts with %menchenchantment%</code></td><td>Whether two definitions conflict (checks both directions, resolves tag refs). Supports negation (<code>doesn&#x27;t mench conflict with</code>).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>if &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot; is in mench tag &quot;mythicenchants:celestial_pack&quot;:\n    send &quot;Fire Slash is in the Celestial Pack!&quot;\n\nset {_a} to mench enchantment &quot;fire_slash&quot;\nset {_b} to mench enchantment &quot;ice_blade&quot;\nif {_a} mench conflicts with {_b}:\n    send &quot;These enchantments conflict!&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Mob Conditions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>%string% has mench [mob] overrides</code></td><td>Whether a MythicMobs mob id has any per-mob enchant applicability overrides configured. Supports negation.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>if &quot;ZOMBIE&quot; has mench overrides:\n    send &quot;This mob has custom enchant applicability rules.&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Config/Feature-Flag Conditions</h4>\n<p>These all check a live config value and support negation.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench custom [enchanting] table is enabled</code></td><td>Whether the custom enchanting table feature is enabled.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench datapack is enabled</code></td><td>Whether the datapack integration is enabled.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench datapack auto-generates</code></td><td>Whether the datapack is configured to auto-generate.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench debug(ging)? is enabled</code></td><td>Whether debug logging is enabled.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench checks? for updates</code></td><td>Whether MythicEnchants checks for updates.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench cleanup is enabled</code></td><td>Whether cleanup of disabled/orphaned enchantments is enabled.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench cleanup is silent</code></td><td>Whether cleanup runs silently.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench has migrations</code></td><td>Whether any enchantment migrations are configured.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench treasure is allowed at [the] table</code></td><td>Whether treasure-only enchantments can appear at the enchanting table.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench vanilla is in [the] table</code></td><td>Whether vanilla enchantments can appear alongside MythicEnchants ones at the table.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench anvil combining is allowed</code></td><td>Whether combining MythicEnchants enchantments at the anvil is allowed.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench anvil use is free</code></td><td>Whether anvil use is configured to be free (no XP/item levy cost).</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench anvil bypass[es] too expensive</code></td><td>Whether the anvil bypasses vanilla&#x27;s &quot;too expensive&quot; repair cost cap.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench anvil supported items (is\\|are) enforced</code></td><td>Whether the anvil enforces an enchantment&#x27;s <code>SupportedItems</code> restriction.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench anvil shows cost when unaffordable</code></td><td>Whether the anvil shows repair cost even when the player can&#x27;t afford the combine.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench grindstone removal is allowed</code></td><td>Whether removing MythicEnchants enchantments at the grindstone is allowed.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench grindstone keeps curses</code></td><td>Whether the grindstone keeps curse enchantments instead of removing them.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>if mench custom table is enabled:\nif mench datapack auto-generates:\nif mench debugging is enabled:\nif mench checks for updates:\nif mench cleanup is enabled:\nif mench cleanup is silent:\nif mench has migrations:\nif mench treasure is allowed at the table:\nif mench vanilla is in the table:\nif mench anvil combining is allowed:\nif mench anvil use is free:\nif mench anvil bypasses too expensive:\nif mench anvil supported items are enforced:\nif mench anvil shows cost when unaffordable:\nif mench grindstone removal is allowed:\nif mench grindstone keeps curses:</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Counter Condition</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench [player] counter %string% of %player% matches %string%</code></td><td>Whether a player counter&#x27;s current value matches a range expression: <code>&quot;5&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;&gt;4&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;&gt;=5&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;&lt;10&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;&lt;=9&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;5-10&quot;</code>, or <code>&quot;5to10&quot;</code>. Supports negation (<code>doesn&#x27;t match</code>). Only a player-scoped form is provided — read an item counter first with the expression above if you need to range-check it.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>if mench player counter &quot;kills&quot; of player matches &quot;&gt;=10&quot;:\n    send &quot;Double digits!&quot; to player</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Pet Ownership Condition</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>%player% is [the] mench pet owner of %livingentity%</code></td><td>Whether a player is the resolved owner/rider of a companion entity. Supports negation.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>if player is the mench pet owner of {_wolf}:\n    send &quot;That&#x27;s your pet!&quot; to player</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Reagent Condition</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>%string% is [a] mench declared reagent</code></td><td>Whether a reagent key is declared in the reagent registry. Supports negation.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>if &quot;my_reagent&quot; is a mench declared reagent:</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Vanilla Curse Flag Conditions</h4>\n<p>Vanilla Minecraft&#x27;s Curse of Binding and Curse of Vanishing, tracked separately from MythicEnchants&#x27; own <code>Cursed:</code> option system used by custom enchantments.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>%itemstack% has [a] mench vanilla binding curse</code></td><td>Whether an item has vanilla Curse of Binding. Supports negation.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%itemstack% has [a] mench vanilla vanishing curse</code></td><td>Whether an item has vanilla Curse of Vanishing. Supports negation.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>if {_item} has a mench vanilla binding curse:</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Datapack Tag Introspection Condition</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>%string% is [a] mench known enchantable tag</code></td><td>Whether a datapack tag reference is a known enchantable tag. Supports negation.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>if &quot;#minecraft:enchantable/sword&quot; is a mench known enchantable tag:</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Effects</h3>\n<h4>Enchantment Effects</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench apply %string% at level %integer% to %itemstack%</code></td><td>Applies an enchantment by namespaced key to an item. Bypasses level limits. Requires the enchantment to exist in the registry (datapack applied). Can fail silently — check <code>last mench apply succeeded</code> after.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench apply %string% at level %integer% to %itemstack% for %player% and fire trigger</code></td><td>Same as above, but also dispatches the <code>ENCHANT_APPLY</code> skill trigger for that player, exactly as if applied through the anvil or table — use this when a scripted apply should trigger the enchant&#x27;s own on-apply skills.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench remove %string% from %itemstack%</code></td><td>Removes an enchantment by namespaced key from an item. Resolves by key, so it works before the datapack is applied.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench copy enchant[ment]s from %itemstack% to %itemstack%</code></td><td>Copies all MythicEnchants enchantments from one item onto another.</td></tr><tr><td><code>unregister mench enchant[ment] %string%</code></td><td>Removes a definition from the registry by id (deindexes tags, reagents, triggers). Does not alter the generated datapack until the next boot.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>mench apply &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot; at level 3 to player&#x27;s tool\nif last mench apply failed:\n    send &quot;That enchantment can&#x27;t go on this item.&quot; to player\nmench apply &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot; at level 3 to player&#x27;s tool for player and fire trigger\nmench remove &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot; from player&#x27;s tool\nmench copy enchantments from {_oldItem} to {_newItem}\nunregister mench enchantment &quot;yourplugin:starfall&quot;</code></pre>\n<blockquote><p><b>Registering</b> new definitions is a Java-API operation (<code>MythicEnchantsAPI.register(...)</code> with the <code>EnchantmentDefinition.builder</code>), not a Skript effect — brand-new enchantments require a server restart to enter the datapack/<code>Registry.ENCHANTMENT</code>, so runtime script-side creation has limited use. See <code>docs/API.md</code>.</p></blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h4>Stored/Book Enchant Effects</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench restore enchant[ment] snapshot %strings% to %itemstack%</code></td><td>Restores a list of <code>&quot;id:level&quot;</code> strings (as produced by <code>mench enchantment snapshot of</code>) onto an item. See the encoding note in the Expressions section above.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>set {_snap::*} to mench enchantment snapshot of {_item}\n# ... later ...\nmench restore enchantment snapshot {_snap::*} to {_item}</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>PDC Effects</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench set pdc boolean %string% (of\\|on) %itemstack% to %boolean%</code></td><td>Sets a raw boolean value in an item&#x27;s PDC by key.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench set pdc integer %string% (of\\|on) %itemstack% to %integer%</code></td><td>Sets a raw integer value in an item&#x27;s PDC by key.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench set pdc number %string% (of\\|on) %itemstack% to %number%</code></td><td>Sets a raw decimal value in an item&#x27;s PDC by key.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench set pdc string %string% (of\\|on) %itemstack% to %string%</code></td><td>Sets a raw string value in an item&#x27;s PDC by key.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench remove pdc [key] %string% (from\\|of) %itemstack%</code></td><td>Removes a value stored in an item&#x27;s PDC by key.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>mench set pdc boolean &quot;myKey&quot; of {_item} to true\nmench set pdc integer &quot;myKey&quot; of {_item} to 5\nmench set pdc number &quot;myKey&quot; of {_item} to 3.5\nmench set pdc string &quot;myKey&quot; of {_item} to &quot;myValue&quot;\nmench remove pdc key &quot;myKey&quot; from {_item}</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Tooltip Effects</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench hide [the] enchant[ment] tooltip (of\\|on) %itemstack%</code></td><td>Hides the enchantment tooltip on an item.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench show [the] enchant[ment] tooltip (of\\|on) %itemstack%</code></td><td>Shows the enchantment tooltip on an item.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>mench hide the enchantment tooltip of {_item}\nmench show the enchantment tooltip on {_item}</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Seed Effects</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench reroll [enchant] seed of %player%</code></td><td>Rerolls the player&#x27;s enchanting seed (changes table offers).</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench reroll %player%&#x27;[s] [enchant] seed</code></td><td>Alternative form.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>mench reroll enchant seed of player\nsend &quot;Your enchanting table offers have been refreshed!&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Trigger Subscription Effects</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench subscribe to trigger %string%</code></td><td>Subscribes to a named MythicEnchants/MythicMobs trigger so that <code>mench trigger fire</code> events fire for it, even for items with no matching enchantment.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench unsubscribe from trigger %string%</code></td><td>Unsubscribes from a named trigger, stopping <code>mench trigger fire</code> events for it (unless another subscriber still needs it).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>mench subscribe to trigger &quot;BLOCK_BREAK&quot;\n# ... later ...\nmench unsubscribe from trigger &quot;BLOCK_BREAK&quot;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Debug/Maintenance Effects</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench enable debug[ging]</code></td><td>Enables MythicEnchants debug logging at runtime.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench disable debug[ging]</code></td><td>Disables MythicEnchants debug logging at runtime.</td></tr><tr><td><code>regenerate mench datapack</code></td><td>Regenerates and re-installs the MythicEnchants datapack from the currently loaded enchantment definitions. Newly added enchantments still require a server restart to be usable — this only refreshes the datapack payload.</td></tr><tr><td><code>reload mench enchant[ment] files</code></td><td>Reloads all enchantment definition YAML files from disk, re-indexing the registry, tags, and reagents.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>mench enable debugging\nmench disable debug\nregenerate mench datapack\nreload mench enchantment files</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Counter Effects</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench add %integer% to [player] counter %string% of %player% [expiring in %string%]</code></td><td>Adds a delta to a player counter. Duration string accepts <code>&quot;5t&quot;</code> (ticks), <code>&quot;5s&quot;</code> (seconds), <code>&quot;-1&quot;</code>/<code>&quot;never&quot;</code>/<code>&quot;forever&quot;</code> (no expiry). Omitting the expiry clause never expires the counter.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench set [player] counter %string% of %player% to %integer% [expiring in %string%]</code></td><td>Sets a player counter to an exact value, with the same optional expiry.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench remove [player] counter %string% (from\\|of) %player%</code></td><td>Removes a player counter entirely.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench add %integer% to item counter %string% of %itemstack% [expiring in %string%]</code></td><td>Adds a delta to an item counter (persisted onto the item).</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench set item counter %string% of %itemstack% to %integer% [expiring in %string%]</code></td><td>Sets an item counter to an exact value (persisted onto the item).</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench remove item counter %string% (from\\|of) %itemstack%</code></td><td>Removes an item counter entirely.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>mench add 1 to player counter &quot;kills&quot; of player\nmench add 1 to player counter &quot;combo&quot; of player expiring in &quot;5s&quot;\nmench set player counter &quot;kills&quot; of player to 0\nmench remove player counter &quot;combo&quot; from player\n\nmench add 1 to item counter &quot;uses&quot; of {_item}\nmench set item counter &quot;streak&quot; of {_item} to 3 expiring in &quot;10s&quot;\nmench remove item counter &quot;streak&quot; from {_item}</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Table Offer Effect</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench invalidate [table] offers (for\\|of) %player%</code></td><td>Invalidates the cached table offers for a player, forcing recomputation next time the table opens.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>mench invalidate table offers for player</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Vanilla Curse Flag Effects</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mench (add\\|remove) [a] vanilla binding curse (to\\|from) %itemstack%</code></td><td>Adds or removes vanilla Curse of Binding on an item.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mench (add\\|remove) [a] vanilla vanishing curse (to\\|from) %itemstack%</code></td><td>Adds or removes vanilla Curse of Vanishing on an item.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>mench add a vanilla binding curse to {_item}\nmench remove a vanilla vanishing curse from {_item}</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Cancel Event</h4>\n<p>Of the six MythicEnchants events, four support Skript&#x27;s native <code>cancel event</code>:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>on mythic enchantment skill trigger:\n    if mench trigger name is &quot;ATTACK&quot;:\n        if player is in world &quot;spawn&quot;:\n            cancel event  # suppress enchantment skills in spawn</code></pre>\n<ul><li><b>Apply/Remove events:</b> cancelling suppresses MythicEnchants&#x27; skill dispatch for that trigger, but does NOT revert the underlying Bukkit operation.</li><li><b>Skill trigger event:</b> cancelling skips the skill call for that specific enchantment only.</li><li><b>Prepare enchant event:</b> cancelling leaves the vanilla offers untouched.</li><li><b>Trigger fire event:</b> NOT cancellable — this is a pure notification bridge, there is no vanilla operation to suppress.</li><li><b>Anvil prepare event:</b> NOT cancellable — instead, &quot;override&quot; its outcome with <code>set mench anvil result to ...</code>.</li></ul>\n<hr>\n<h3>Full Example Script</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>on mythic enchantment skill trigger:\n    # Suppress all enchant skills in the spawn world\n    if player is in world &quot;spawn&quot;:\n        cancel event\n        stop\n\n    # Log high-damage enchantment hits\n    if mench trigger name is &quot;ATTACK&quot;:\n        if mench trigger damage &gt; 15:\n            log &quot;%player% dealt %mench trigger damage% damage with %mench id of event-menchenchantment% level %mench trigger level%&quot;\n\non mythic enchantment apply:\n    # Announce rare enchantment applications\n    set {_def} to mench enchantment &quot;mythicenchants:legendary_strike&quot;\n    if {_def} is set:\n        if mench apply source is &quot;TABLE&quot;:\n            broadcast &quot;&amp;6%player% just enchanted their %event-item% with Legendary Strike!&quot;\n\non mythic prepare enchantment:\n    # Show reagent info\n    if mench reagent key is not &quot;minecraft:lapis_lazuli&quot;:\n        send &quot;&amp;dSpecial reagent: %mench reagent key% (Power: %mench table power%)&quot; to player\n\n# Subscribe to a trigger that has no matching enchantment requirement\nmench subscribe to trigger &quot;BLOCK_BREAK&quot;\n\non mench trigger fire:\n    if mench trigger name is &quot;BLOCK_BREAK&quot;:\n        send &quot;&amp;7Trigger fired on %event-item%.&quot; to player\n\n# Honor &quot;overleveled&quot; enchanted books past vanilla&#x27;s level clamp at the anvil\non mench anvil prepare:\n    set {_left} to mench anvil left item\n    set {_right} to mench anvil right item\n    if {_right} is not set:\n        stop\n    set {_bookLevel} to mench stored enchant level of &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot; in {_right}\n    if {_bookLevel} &gt; mench max level of &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot;:\n        # Vanilla would clamp this combine — build our own overleveled result instead.\n        set {_snap::*} to mench enchantment snapshot of {_left}\n        set {_result} to mench anvil result\n        mench restore enchantment snapshot {_snap::*} to {_result}\n        mench apply &quot;mythicenchants:fire_slash&quot; at level {_bookLevel} to {_result}\n        set mench anvil result to {_result}\n\n# Curses, options, PDC helpers, and tooltip hiding on a crafted &quot;cursed relic&quot;\ncommand /makerelic:\n    permission: mench.relic\n    trigger:\n        set {_relic} to mench book with &quot;mythicenchants:doom_curse:1&quot;\n        mench set pdc string &quot;relic_owner&quot; of {_relic} to &quot;%player%&quot;\n        mench set pdc boolean &quot;relic_bound&quot; of {_relic} to true\n        mench hide the enchantment tooltip of {_relic}\n        give {_relic} to player\n        if {_relic} has a mench curse:\n            send &quot;&amp;4Beware — this relic is cursed!&quot; to player\n\n# Command to inspect an enchantment\ncommand /enchinfo &lt;text&gt;:\n    permission: mench.info\n    trigger:\n        if arg-1 is not mench registered:\n            send &quot;&amp;cEnchantment not found.&quot;\n            stop\n        set {_def} to mench enchantment arg-1\n        send &quot;&amp;aEnchantment: &amp;f%mench display name of {_def}%&quot;\n        send &quot;&amp;aID: &amp;f%mench id of {_def}%&quot;\n        send &quot;&amp;aRarity: &amp;f%mench rarity of {_def}%&quot;\n        send &quot;&amp;aLevels: &amp;f%mench min level of {_def}%&amp;7-&amp;f%mench max level of {_def}%&quot;\n        send &quot;&amp;aTags: &amp;f%mench tags of {_def}%&quot;\n        send &quot;&amp;aConflicts: &amp;f%mench conflicts of {_def}%&quot;\n        send &quot;&amp;aReagents: &amp;f%mench reagents of {_def}%&quot;\n        if {_def} is mench cursed:\n            send &quot;&amp;c(Curse)&quot;\n        if {_def} is mench treasure:\n            send &quot;&amp;e(Treasure)&quot;</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/skript/SYNTAX"},"enchants:api/api":{"h":"<h4>Adding the Dependency</h4>\n<h5>Maven</h5>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"xml\"><code>&lt;dependency&gt;\n    &lt;groupId&gt;com.stelliusstudio&lt;/groupId&gt;\n    &lt;artifactId&gt;MythicEnchants&lt;/artifactId&gt;\n    &lt;version&gt;1.2.0&lt;/version&gt;\n    &lt;scope&gt;provided&lt;/scope&gt;\n&lt;/dependency&gt;</code></pre>\n<h5>Gradle (Kotlin DSL)</h5>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"kotlin\"><code>dependencies {\n    compileOnly(&quot;com.stelliusstudio:MythicEnchants:1.2.0&quot;)\n}</code></pre>\n<h5>Gradle (Groovy)</h5>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"groovy\"><code>dependencies {\n    compileOnly &#x27;com.stelliusstudio:MythicEnchants:1.2.0&#x27;\n}</code></pre>\n<h4>plugin.yml Dependency</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>depend: [MythicEnchants]\n# Or soft dependency\nsoftdepend: [MythicEnchants]</code></pre>\n<h4>Accessing the API</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"java\"><code>import com.stelliusstudio.mythicenchants.MythicEnchants;\nimport com.stelliusstudio.mythicenchants.api.EnchantmentAPI;\n\npublic class MyPlugin extends JavaPlugin {\n    \n    private EnchantmentAPI api;\n    \n    @Override\n    public void onEnable() {\n        // Check if MythicEnchants is loaded\n        if (getServer().getPluginManager().getPlugin(&quot;MythicEnchants&quot;) == null) {\n            getLogger().severe(&quot;MythicEnchants not found!&quot;);\n            getServer().getPluginManager().disablePlugin(this);\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        // Get API instance\n        api = MythicEnchants.getAPI();\n        getLogger().info(&quot;Successfully hooked into MythicEnchants!&quot;);\n    }\n}</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/API/API"},"enchants:skript/skript-support":{"h":"<p>_Coming in a Future Update_</p>\n<blockquote><p>Feel free to give feedback on features you&#x27;d hope to see!</p></blockquote>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Skript/Skript-Support"},"enchants:addons/addons":{"h":"<h3>MythicEnchantsLibrary</h3>\n<p>An enchant bank. Players deposit enchanted books into a vault that stores the levels — not the physical books — against their account, then pull stored levels onto any eligible item from a config-driven Applicator GUI. SQLite out of the box, MySQL supported; also works as a read-only catalog in display-only mode. → <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mythicenchantslibrary/library\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/MythicEnchantsLibrary/library\">README</a></p>\n<p>Install: drop the built jar in <code>plugins/MythicEnchants/addons/</code>.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"uploads/485d7f287e749266b7d9eb106e34f6dc/mythicenchantslibrary-1.0.0.jar\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/uploads/485d7f287e749266b7d9eb106e34f6dc/MythicEnchantsLibrary-1.0.0.jar\">MythicEnchantsLibrary-1.0.0.jar</a></p>\n<h3>MythicEnchantsPacketLore</h3>\n<p>Replaces the vanilla enchantment tooltip with a custom, packet-rendered one — rarity colors, roman numerals, configurable formats, and scrolling descriptions when an item carries more enchants than fit on screen. The real item is never touched; only the vanilla tooltip flag is switched off, and everything else is generated live per outgoing packet. Requires PacketEvents. → <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mythicenchantspacketlore/lore\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/MythicEnchantsPacketLore/lore\">README</a></p>\n<p>Install: drop the built jar in <code>plugins/MythicEnchants/addons/</code>.</p>\n<p>Requires <a href=\"https://github.com/retrooper/packetevents\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">PacketEvents</a> 2.13.0+ installed separately as its own plugin — soft-guarded, so the addon simply stays inactive if PacketEvents is missing rather than failing to load.</p>\n<p>Install: drop the built jar in <code>plugins/MythicEnchants/addons/</code>, install PacketEvents alongside it.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"uploads/c2f4c7245424de096626b62e35040776/mythicenchantspacketlore-1.0.0.jar\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/uploads/c2f4c7245424de096626b62e35040776/MythicEnchantsPacketLore-1.0.0.jar\">MythicEnchantsPacketLore-1.0.0.jar</a></p>\n<h3>MythicEnchantsLegacyMigrator</h3>\n<p>A one-off, opt-in migration tool for servers upgrading from the old Lumine &quot;MythicEnchants 1.x&quot; plugin. Nothing runs automatically — <code>/mench legacymigrate</code> dry-runs a scan of <code>plugins/MythicMobs/Enchantments/</code> for old-schema enchants, and <code>/mench legacymigrate apply</code> rewrites matched files in place (with a <code>.bak</code> backup) for the next restart to pick up. → <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mythicenchantslegacymigrator/migrations\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/MythicEnchantsLegacyMigrator/Migrations\">README</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"uploads/fb04a9f0d9698c89cfb239292e3f90a9/mythicenchantslegacymigrator-1.0.0.jar\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/uploads/fb04a9f0d9698c89cfb239292e3f90a9/MythicEnchantsLegacyMigrator-1.0.0.jar\">MythicEnchantsLegacyMigrator-1.0.0.jar</a></p>\n<h3>MythicEnchantsAnvilSplit</h3>\n<p>A physical anvil that lands on a dropped enchanted item strips its MythicEnchants enchants off into a real enchanted book nearby. Vanilla anvil physics (placement, fall damage, downgrade chance) are completely untouched — splitting is a side effect of the impact, not a replacement for it. Also reachable as a MythicMobs mechanic, no anvil required. → <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mythicenchantsanvilsplit/anvilsplitting\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/MythicEnchantsAnvilSplit/AnvilSplitting\">README</a></p>\n<p>Install: drop the built jar in <code>plugins/MythicEnchants/addons/</code>.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"uploads/d24c41cf84049b85fdefbc83626942de/mythicenchantsanvilsplit-1.0.0.jar\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/uploads/d24c41cf84049b85fdefbc83626942de/MythicEnchantsAnvilSplit-1.0.0.jar\">MythicEnchantsAnvilSplit-1.0.0.jar</a></p>\n<h3>MythicEnchantsOverleveled</h3>\n<p>Lets an allowlisted set of enchants be minted onto books above their normal <code>MaxLevel</code>, and makes the anvil honor that exact level instead of vanilla clamping it back down. Nothing is overleveled by default — each enchant needs its own cap entry. → <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mythicenchantsoverleveled/overlevel\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/MythicEnchantsOverleveled/Overlevel\">README</a></p>\n<p>Install: drop the built jar in <code>plugins/MythicEnchants/addons/</code>.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"uploads/2fe314302ff00aeb9a17f77f2451fbb4/mythicenchantsoverleveled-1.0.0.jar\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/uploads/2fe314302ff00aeb9a17f77f2451fbb4/MythicEnchantsOverleveled-1.0.0.jar\">MythicEnchantsOverleveled-1.0.0.jar</a></p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/addons/addons"},"enchants:mythicenchantsanvilsplit/anvilsplitting":{"h":"<h2>MythicEnchantsAnvilSplit</h2>\n<p>A physical anvil that falls and lands on a dropped item strips that item&#x27;s MythicEnchants enchants off and drops them nearby as an enchanted book. The anvil itself lands and behaves exactly like vanilla — placement, damage, downgrade chance all proceed as normal. Splitting is a side effect of the impact, not a replacement for it.</p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul><li><b>No GUI, no command.</b> Drop an enchanted item, drop an anvil on it (sand/gravel-supported and knocked loose, dispenser-fired, or any other way to get a <code>FallingBlock</code> anvil moving), and the split happens on landing.</li><li><b>Vanilla physics untouched.</b> The anvil places, takes fall damage, and rolls its usual damage/downgrade chance exactly as it would with this addon absent.</li><li><b>Real enchanted books.</b> The resulting book carries genuine <code>EnchantmentStorageMeta</code> stored enchants — usable on any anvil, stackable with other books of the same enchants, and rendered correctly by MythicEnchantsPacketLore if installed.</li><li><b>Configurable scope.</b> Choose whether curses are eligible to be split off, whether plain vanilla enchants split too (MythicEnchants-registered enchants always do), a radius around the impact to search for items, and whether one impact/cast peels off a single enchant at a time (in tooltip order) or every eligible enchant at once (optionally capped).</li><li><b>Also reachable without an anvil.</b> The same split logic is exposed as a MythicMobs mechanic, so it can run from a skill, NPC interaction, or quest reward.</li></ul>\n<h3>Install</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>MythicEnchantsAnvilSplit.jar -&gt; plugins/MythicEnchants/addons/</code></pre>\n<p>Restart. Any anvil that lands on a dropped enchanted item now splits it automatically.</p>\n<h3>Configuration (<code>config.yml</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Default</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>enabled</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Master switch.</td></tr><tr><td><code>radius</code></td><td><code>1.0</code></td><td>Search radius (blocks) around the anvil&#x27;s landing block for dropped items.</td></tr><tr><td><code>include-vanilla-enchants</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td><code>false</code> splits only MythicEnchants-registered enchants; <code>true</code> also pulls plain vanilla enchants into the book.</td></tr><tr><td><code>split-curses</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Whether cursed MythicEnchants enchants are eligible to be split off. <code>false</code> leaves curses on the original item.</td></tr><tr><td><code>skip-books</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Never split an item that is itself an enchanted book.</td></tr><tr><td><code>split-mode</code></td><td><code>all-at-once</code></td><td><code>one-at-a-time</code> pulls exactly one enchant per split — whichever currently sits first in tooltip order (ascending <code>TooltipOrder</code>, unordered enchants last) — so repeated impacts/casts peel enchants off one by one. <code>all-at-once</code> pulls every eligible enchant in a single pass, subject to <code>max-enchants-per-split</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>max-enchants-per-split</code></td><td><code>0</code></td><td>Cap on enchants pulled into one resulting book. Only consulted when <code>split-mode: all-at-once</code>. <code>0</code> = no limit.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Mechanic</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>Skills:\n  - splititem{slot=hand} @self ~onInteract</code></pre>\n<p><code>splititem</code> (alias <code>anvilsplit</code>) performs the same split on the target&#x27;s held item, without needing a physical anvil. <code>slot</code>/<code>s</code> accepts <code>hand</code> (default) or <code>offhand</code>.</p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/MythicEnchantsAnvilSplit/AnvilSplitting"},"enchants:mythicenchantslegacymigrator/migrations":{"h":"<h2>MythicEnchantsLegacyMigrator</h2>\n<p>A one-off migration tool for servers upgrading from the old Lumine &quot;MythicEnchants 1.x&quot; plugin to the modern MythicEnchants. It is <b>not</b> loaded automatically — nothing runs at boot, and it only touches files when you explicitly ask it to.</p>\n<h3>Why this is a separate addon</h3>\n<p>Legacy migration used to run automatically inside core on every enchant-file load. That caused real problems on servers that never had a legacy install: the detection heuristics could misfire on unrelated/hand-written modern enchants and register duplicate-named enchantments. Since migration is a one-time, opt-in operation, it now lives here instead — core no longer touches legacy schemas at all.</p>\n<h3>Usage</h3>\n<ol><li>Drop <code>MythicEnchantsLegacyMigrator.jar</code> into <code>plugins/MythicEnchants/addons/</code>.</li><li>Restart the server (or reload addons).</li><li>Run <code>/mench legacymigrate</code> to dry-run — this scans <code>plugins/MythicMobs/Enchantments/</code> (recursively) and reports which files contain old-schema enchantments, without writing anything.</li><li>Run <code>/mench legacymigrate apply</code> to actually rewrite the matched files in place. Each rewritten file gets a one-time <code>&lt;name&gt;.yml.bak</code> backup alongside it.</li><li><b>Restart the server.</b> The addon only rewrites files on disk — core&#x27;s <code>EnchantmentLoader</code> already finished parsing enchants for the current boot by the time addons load, so the modernised files take effect on the next start.</li></ol>\n<p>Permission: <code>mench.legacymigrate</code></p>\n<h3>What gets migrated</h3>\n<p>Field mapping is verified against the real 1.x plugin source (<code>io.lumine.mythicenchants</code>), not guessed from a template:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Legacy (1.x)</th><th>Modern</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Cursed</code> / <code>Treasure</code> (top-level)</td><td><code>Options.Cursed</code> / <code>Options.Treasure</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>EnchantableItems</code> (material list)</td><td><code>SupportedItems</code> (inferred tag) + <code>Enchanting.PrimaryItems</code> (preserved list)</td></tr><tr><td><code>EnchantingTable.MinExperience</code> / <code>MaxExperience</code></td><td><code>Enchanting.MinCost.Base</code> / <code>Enchanting.MaxCost.Base</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>EnchantingTable.MinLevel</code> / <code>MaxLevel</code></td><td>dropped — no modern analogue</td></tr><tr><td><code>MergeCostPerLevel</code></td><td>dropped — no safe modern analogue, review anvil cost by hand</td></tr><tr><td><code>Display</code>, <code>Rarity</code>, <code>MinLevel</code>/<code>MaxLevel</code>, <code>ValidSlots</code>, <code>ConflictingEnchants</code>, <code>Skills</code>, <code>Stats</code></td><td>unchanged — already schema-compatible</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>An <code>Enchanting.Weight</code> of <code>5</code> is synthesised for any migrated enchant, since 1.x had no per-enchant table-weight concept (odds were entirely rarity-driven via a separate <code>rarities.yml</code>). Tune weights by hand afterward.</p>\n<p>Two 1.x-only skill-line conditions have no modern equivalent and are <b>flagged only, never rewritten</b> — <code>?enchantlevel{level=N}</code> and <code>?enchantslot{slot=X}</code>. Review those lines by hand.</p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/MythicEnchantsLegacyMigrator/Migrations"},"enchants:mythicenchantslibrary/library":{"h":"<h2>MythicEnchantsLibrary</h2>\n<p>An enchant bank for MythicEnchants. Players deposit enchanted books into a vault, which stores the levels — not the physical books — against their account. From there they open an Applicator, place any eligible item, and pull stored levels onto it.</p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul><li><b>Levels aren&#x27;t tied to one item.</b> Deposit a book once, apply the levels to whatever item you actually want them on, whenever you want.</li><li><b>Both GUIs are config-driven.</b> Layout is an ASCII grid with a symbol legend in YAML — icons, colors, names, lore, even MythicMobs items as buttons. Reskinning either GUI doesn&#x27;t need Java.</li><li><b>The applicator filters to what&#x27;s valid.</b> Place an item in and the enchant list shows only what that item can actually take. The level slider is clamped to what&#x27;s banked and to the enchant&#x27;s max level.</li><li><b>Transactions roll back cleanly.</b> Deposits and withdrawals go through the database transactionally. If applying an enchant fails partway through (e.g. a datapack isn&#x27;t active), whatever was consumed from the vault is refunded.</li><li><b>Not just a command.</b> <code>openlibrary</code> is a MythicMobs mechanic, so the vault or applicator can be opened from an NPC, a right-clicked item, a quest reward, or any other skill trigger.</li><li><b>No manual database setup.</b> SQLite works out of the box; MySQL is supported too. The driver and connection pool download themselves on first run into an isolated classloader, so nothing is bundled into the jar or collides with another plugin&#x27;s copy of the same libraries.</li><li><b>Optional display-only mode.</b> Turns the addon into a read-only enchant catalog — every enchant shown at max level, nothing stored or spent. Useful as a reference tool even without the banking economy.</li></ul>\n<h3>Commands</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>/mench library            open the vault\n/mench library vault      same as above\n/mench library apply      open the applicator directly</code></pre>\n<p>Permission: <code>mench.library</code></p>\n<h3>Mechanic</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>Skills:\n  - openlibrary{mode=vault} @self ~onInteract\n  - openlibrary{mode=apply} @self ~onInteract</code></pre>\n<p><code>mode</code> (alias <code>m</code>) accepts <code>vault</code> (default) or <code>apply</code>.</p>\n<h3>How the vault works</h3>\n<p>Drag an enchanted book into the deposit slot and its levels get credited to the player, per enchant. The main view pages through everything they&#x27;ve banked, shown as stacked enchanted books — stack size is the level count, up to the configured cap. A button jumps straight to the applicator.</p>\n<h3>How the applicator works</h3>\n<p>Place any item in the center slot. The enchant list updates to show only what&#x27;s applicable to that specific item. Pick one, use the level buttons to choose a target level — bounded by what the item already has plus what&#x27;s banked, and by the enchant&#x27;s own max level — then confirm. Only the difference in levels is spent, not the full total.</p>\n<h3>Per-enchant control</h3>\n<p>Keep an enchant out of the library entirely:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>my_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;Superstar&quot;\n  Options:\n    ExcludeFromLibrary: true</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/MythicEnchantsLibrary/library"},"enchants:mythicenchantsoverleveled/overlevel":{"h":"<h2>MythicEnchantsOverleveled</h2>\n<p>Lets specific, allowlisted enchants be minted onto enchanted books above their normal <code>MaxLevel</code>, and makes the anvil honor that book&#x27;s exact level instead of vanilla silently clamping the result back down.</p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul><li><b>Per-enchant allowlist, not a global cap raise.</b> Nothing is overleveled by default — each enchant needs its own entry in <code>per-enchant-caps</code> before it can exceed its <code>MaxLevel</code> at all. An enchant with no entry behaves identically to a server without this addon installed.</li><li><b>The anvil result is honored exactly.</b> Vanilla clamps a merged enchant&#x27;s level back to <code>MaxLevel</code> before this addon ever sees the result, so it rebuilds the anvil&#x27;s output item from scratch and asserts the sacrifice book&#x27;s overleveled level as final — layered on top of whatever core/vanilla already computed for every other enchant on the item.</li><li><b><code>/mench book</code> can mint overleveled books directly.</b> This addon overrides core&#x27;s own <code>book</code> subcommand so admins can hand out a book above <code>MaxLevel</code> in one command, gated by its own permission separate from the base <code>mench.book</code> node.</li><li><b>A public API for other addons.</b> <code>OverleveledAPI.get()</code> exposes <code>getEffectiveCeiling()</code>/<code>isOverleveled()</code>/<code>createOverleveledBook()</code> so other plugins, addons, or MythicMobs mechanics (e.g. a custom loot table or drop mechanic) can mint overleveled books programmatically, or ask &quot;how far can this enchant go?&quot; before doing their own math. <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"../mythicenchantsscrolls\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/../MythicEnchantsScrolls\">MythicEnchantsScrolls</a>&#x27;s <code>add</code>-mode collision math already uses this.</li><li><b>Deliberately narrow scope.</b> No loot table, custom enchanting table, or villager trade integration — overleveled books only ever come from <code>/mench book</code> or the API, by design.</li></ul>\n<h3>Install</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>MythicEnchantsOverleveled.jar -&gt; plugins/MythicEnchants/addons/</code></pre>\n<p>Restart. <code>config.yml</code> is written to <code>plugins/MythicEnchants/addons/MythicEnchantsOverleveled/</code> with an empty allowlist — nothing is overleveled until you add entries.</p>\n<h3>Configuration (<code>config.yml</code>)</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>enabled: true\n\nper-enchant-caps: {}\n\nrequire-permission: &quot;mench.overleveled.create&quot;\n\ndebug: false</code></pre>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Default</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>enabled</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Master switch. When <code>false</code>, the anvil listener no-ops entirely and <code>/mench book</code> refuses any level above an enchant&#x27;s plain <code>MaxLevel</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>per-enchant-caps</code></td><td><code>{}</code></td><td>Maps a full namespaced enchant id (vanilla or MythicEnchants custom, e.g. <code>minecraft:sharpness</code>, <code>mythicenchants:fire_slash</code>) to a non-negative integer bonus above <code>MaxLevel</code>. <code>MaxLevel: 5</code> + cap <code>3</code> = an effective ceiling of <code>8</code>. Lookup is case-insensitive; negative values are rejected with a load-time warning.</td></tr><tr><td><code>require-permission</code></td><td><code>&quot;mench.overleveled.create&quot;</code></td><td>Permission needed to mint a book above <code>MaxLevel</code> via <code>/mench book</code>. In-range books only need the base <code>mench.book</code> permission. Leave blank to let anyone with <code>mench.book</code> create overleveled books too.</td></tr><tr><td><code>debug</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Logs each overleveled enchant applied during an anvil combine — enchant, book level, ceiling, applied level, player.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Commands</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>/mench book &lt;player&gt; &lt;enchantment&gt; &lt;level&gt;</code></pre>\n<p>Overrides core&#x27;s own <code>book</code> subcommand — identical behavior for in-range levels, and additionally allows levels up to an enchant&#x27;s effective ceiling (<code>MaxLevel</code> + <code>per-enchant-caps</code> bonus) if the sender has <code>require-permission</code> (or it&#x27;s blank). Permission: <code>mench.book</code>.</p>\n<h3>API</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"java\"><code>OverleveledAPI api = OverleveledAPI.get();\nif (api != null) {\n    ItemStack book = api.createOverleveledBook(&quot;minecraft:sharpness&quot;, 6);\n}</code></pre>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>getEffectiveCeiling(Enchantment)</code></td><td>Highest level this enchant may be minted at — <code>MaxLevel</code> + its <code>per-enchant-caps</code> bonus, or the plain <code>MaxLevel</code> if overleveling is disabled or the enchant has no cap entry.</td></tr><tr><td><code>isOverleveled(Enchantment, int level)</code></td><td>Whether <code>level</code> exceeds the enchant&#x27;s normal <code>MaxLevel</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>createOverleveledBook(String enchantId, int level)</code></td><td>Resolves a namespaced enchant id and mints a book at <code>level</code>, clamped to the effective ceiling. <code>null</code> if the id doesn&#x27;t resolve.</td></tr><tr><td><code>createOverleveledBook(Enchantment, int level)</code></td><td>Same, given an already-resolved <code>Enchantment</code>.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><code>OverleveledAPI.get()</code> returns <code>null</code> if the addon isn&#x27;t loaded — always null-check.</p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/MythicEnchantsOverleveled/Overlevel"},"enchants:mythicenchantspacketlore/lore":{"h":"<h2>MythicEnchantsPacketLore</h2>\n<p>Replaces the vanilla enchantment tooltip on MythicEnchants items with a custom, packet-rendered one — rarity-colored names, roman numerals, descriptions, configurable format strings. Applies to every enchanted item on the server as soon as it&#x27;s installed, no per-item setup.</p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul><li><b>Custom tooltip styling.</b> Rarity colors, roman numerals instead of &quot;Level 3&quot;, and configurable name/description formats.</li><li><b>The real item is untouched.</b> Only the vanilla display is switched off (<code>ItemFlag.HIDE_ENCHANTS</code>/<code>HIDE_STORED_ENCHANTS</code>, a normal server-side item flag). What players see is generated live, per packet — no fake enchant data is ever written to the item.</li><li><b>Scrolling tooltips.</b> When an item has more enchants than fit in the configured line limit, the descriptions rotate through the full list instead of being cut off. Rotation can auto-advance on a timer, or be triggered by pressing F over the item, or by picking it up and placing it back down. Each viewer scrolls independently.</li><li><b>Works on enchanted books, same as gear.</b> No separate configuration needed.</li><li><b>Dupe-safety guards.</b> Scrolling refreshes are withheld from creative-mode players, while an anvil is open, and while anything is on the player&#x27;s cursor — situations where resending item state could conflict with client-authoritative state.</li><li><b>Fails safe without PacketEvents.</b> If it&#x27;s missing, the addon logs a clear message and stays inactive rather than throwing errors.</li></ul>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/MythicEnchantsPacketLore/lore"},"hud:commands":{"h":"<p>Commands are primarily for console access to configure HUD behaviors during gameplay.\\ For example, using the <code>/hud popup</code> command to reveal a pop-up message or icon for a period of time.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th><b>Command</b></th><th><b>Permission</b></th><th><b>Description</b></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>/hud version</code></td><td><code>mythichud.version</code></td><td>Prints version information. Always send a screenshot of this command&#x27;s output when submitting a bug report.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/hud reload</code></td><td><code>mythichud.reload</code></td><td>Reloads the plugin and all its configurations.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/hud reload all</code></td><td><code>mythichud.reload.all</code></td><td>Reloads the plugin and all its configurations, generating a new resource pack.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/hud pack generate</code></td><td><code>mythichud.pack.generate</code></td><td>Generates a new resource pack.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/hud pack steps</code></td><td><code>mythichud.pack.steps</code></td><td>Prints the steps taken to generate a resource pack. Useful for checking the functionality of plugin integrations.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/hud pack cache list</code></td><td><code>mythichud.pack.cache.list</code></td><td>Lists the entries in the pack cache.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/hud pack cache clear</code></td><td><code>mythichud.pack.cache.clear</code></td><td>Clears the pack cache or removes the provided cache entry.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/hud layout</code></td><td><code>mythichud.layout</code></td><td>Toggle a HUD Layout for a player.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/hud popup</code></td><td><code>mythichud.popup</code></td><td>Trigger a HUD popup for a player, for a set duration.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Commands"},"hud:compatibility":{"h":"<p>Some plugins that handle resource packs for your server may take extra steps to configure.\\ MythicHUD offers a simple export compatibility option in its <code>/MythicHUD/config.yml</code>:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>copy-pack:\n  enabled: false\n  path: &quot;Nexo/pack/external_packs/MythicHUD&quot;</code></pre>\n<p>This configuration, when enabled, would copy the <code>/MythicHUD/built-pack/</code> assets to another destination, such as <code>/plugins/myPack/assets/</code> as configured above.  You can send MythicHUD&#x27;s assets to any pack management plugin/directory in this way.</p>\n<p><b>Some plugins modify core shaders MythicHUD uses for its displays, and must be configured so they do not conflict with HUD rendering.</b></p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Crucible:</h4>\n<ul><li>Crucible can automatically pull MythicHUD&#x27;s assets if its <code>/MythicMobs/config/config-generation.yml</code> is configured with</li></ul>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>Generation:\n  MergeMythicHUD: true</code></pre>\n<ul><li><code>/hud reload</code> must be used <i>before</i> <code>/mm i generate</code> generates the Crucible resource pack to get HUD asset updates.</li></ul>\n<hr>\n<h4>Nexo</h4>\n<ul><li>Nexo has a separate hook which can be enabled with <code>nexo-hook: true</code>.</li></ul>\n<p>This will handle merging of all files automatically, no need to change any setting or copy files manually. The MythicHUD ResourcePack will automatically be injected into Nexo when it generates it&#x27;s ResourcePack</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>ItemsAdder</h4>\n<ul><li>In <code>ItemsAdder/config.yml</code> disable some text shader related elements:<ul><li>Disable <a href=\"https://itemsadder.devs.beer/plugin-usage/text-effects-1.17+\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ItemsAdder Text Effects</a>.</li><li>Disable <a href=\"https://itemsadder.devs.beer/plugin-usage/scoreboard/hide-scoreboard-numbers-1.17+\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ItemsAdder Hide Scoreboard Numbers</a>.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>text_effects:\n  enabled: false\n  hide_scoreboard_numbers: false\n  hide_scoreboard_numbers_old_clients: false</code></pre>\n<ul><li>Configure MythicHUD to send its pack assets to ItemsAdder in its <code>MythicHUD/config.yml</code>:</li></ul>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>copy-pack:\n  enabled: true\n  path: ItemsAdder/contents/mythichud/resourcepack</code></pre>\n<ul><li>for &quot;hide exp level&quot; to work also change the following settings in <code>plugins/itemsadder/config.yml</code></li></ul>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>huds:\n  enabled: false\n  force_color:\n    enabled: false\n    color: &#x27;#FFFFFF&#x27;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Mod Compatibility</h3>\n<h4>Lunar Client</h4>\n<p><b>Note:</b> As of Lunar Client v2.22.16, there is no longer an issue and Lunar Client is compatible\\ In order to make HUDs appear correctly on the Lunar Client, Boss Bar settings must be set to not use Custom Boss Bars. <a href=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/uploads/07a8d653c44a5168e168aa1103055d9d/LunarClient_Settings.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"imglink\">🖼 LunarClient_Settings</a></p>\n<h4>Feather Client</h4>\n<p>In order to make HUDs appear correctly on the Feather Client, Boss Bar settings must use White Text color, Text Shadow, and be set to not overwrite text color: <a href=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/uploads/2dae5dd4582eccc70472a8952e6c861d/FeatherClient_Settings.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"imglink\">🖼 FeatherClient_Settings</a></p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Compatibility"},"hud:getting-started":{"h":"<h4>Before Server Start</h4>\n<p>MythicHUD is installed like most plugins - simply drag the <code>MythicHUD.jar</code> to your server&#x27;s <code>/plugins/</code> folder, then (re)start your server.</p>\n<p>If you were a HappyHUD user, you can also try <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"migrating-from-happyhud\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Migrating-from-HappyHUD\">Migrating from HappyHUD</a> before this setup process.</p>\n<h4>After Server Start</h4>\n<p>Now that your server has started you should see <code>/plugins/MythicHUD</code> in your plugins directory.\\ This is where all the configuration for the plugin will be stored.</p>\n<h4>Resource Pack</h4>\n<p>If you were to join the server at this point the display would not work, likely showing <code>▯</code> characters.  This is because MythicHUD&#x27;s displays are font characters delivered via a resource pack; without it, the textures cannot load.</p>\n<p><b>Texture Pack Updates</b></p>\n<p>If you are working with MythicHUD and encounter these ▯ characters, that means your pack is not loaded properly - start troubleshooting there first!</p>\n<p>MythicHUD exports its assets to the <code>/plugins/MythicHUD/built-pack/</code> folder, which needs to be merged into your server&#x27;s resource pack.  If your server is not using a resource pack, you will have to <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Tutorials/Creating_a_resource_pack#Creating_a_resource_pack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">create a resource pack</a> to host MythicHUD assets in.</p>\n<p>You can merge the contents of the <code>/MythicHud/built-pack/</code> folder into your resource pack&#x27;s assets.  Most changes you make with HUDs will require you to merge the updated assets like this again.</p>\n<p><b>If you are using a pack management plugin such as Crucible, Oraxen or ItemsAdder,</b>\\ make sure to check the extra <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"compatibility\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Compatibility\">Compatibility</a> steps for setup!</p>\n<p>Once you&#x27;re all set you can start learning about <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"hud-components\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/HUD-Components\">HUD Components</a>!</p>\n<h4>Using HUDs</h4>\n<p>By default, the <code>default-layout</code> HUD will be on for players.  This can be configured in its files, and in-game can be toggled with the <code>/hud layout</code> <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"commands\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Commands\">Commands</a>.</p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Getting-Started"},"hud:home":{"h":"<p>Welcome to the MythicHUD wiki!\\ MythicHUD is still in active development, so documentation and syntax is subject to change as features evolve and expand.  Reach out in the <a href=\"https://discord.com/invite/K3tqXfT\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Discord</a> for support about any questions!</p>\n<p>If you are just <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"getting-started\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Getting-Started\">Getting Started</a>, follow the guide to learn about the pieces of the plugin and HUDs, and soon start making your own!</p>\n<h4><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"migrating-from-happyhud\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Migrating-from-HappyHUD\">Migrating from HappyHUD</a></h4>\n<p><b>Before replacing HappyHUD with MythicHUD, make at least one backup of your server&#x27;s <code>/plugins/HappyHUD</code> folder.\\ This is _critically important_: we cannot provide support for users who lost data because a backup was not created</b>.</p>\n<h4><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mythichud-api\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/MythicHUD-API\">MythicHUD API</a></h4>\n<p>Developers may utilize MythicHUD&#x27;s rich API for enhanced integration and customization.</p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Home"},"hud:what's-new-in-mythichud?":{"h":"<h3>v2.0.0</h3>\n<p>(under construction)</p>\n<h3>v1.2.0</h3>\n<p>(under construction)</p>\n<h3>v1.0.0</h3>\n<p><b>Additions</b></p>\n<ol><li>Support for server versions 1.20.6 through 1.21.1. Paper removed a necessary snapshot version of Adventure, so it is not possible to target 1.20.5 with paperclip-userdev.</li><li>Support for client versions 1.20.5 through 1.21.1. A new <code>mythichud-modern</code> overlay is added to provide the updated shader for those versions.</li><li>Proper API publishing. Documentation for API consumers is coming for a later release, but it is possible to do so now if you are so inclined to figure it out.</li><li>Automatic migration from HappyHUD. As long as the plugin data folder exists, MythicHUD will attempt to migrate the installation and guide users to ensure functionality.</li><li>Development builds! Users can now keep track of project activity from our Discord server. Downloadable builds will be added soon.</li></ol>\n<p><b>Removals</b></p>\n<ol><li>Support for Spigot and Bukkit servers. Support will be added back in a later release. Currently, the plugin will function in minimal state.</li><li>Dependency on ProtocolLib. While useful in some contexts, ProtocolLib is has undesirable implications for performance and maintainability.</li></ol>\n<p><b>Changes</b></p>\n<ol><li>Significant internal refactoring and optimization</li><li>Fully asynchronous, native implementation of packet injection. By dropping ProtocolLib, we now use a fully custom packet handling implementation, allowing for markedly better performance.</li></ol>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/What's-New-in-MythicHUD?"},"hud:conditions":{"h":"<p>Conditions can be used to modify HUD appearance based on logical checks against placeholders.</p>\n<h4>Condition Formatting</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>conditions:\n- &lt;condition type&gt;{&lt;condition arguments&gt;} &lt;outcome&gt; &lt;action&gt; &lt;action variable&gt;</code></pre>\n<h5>Condition Type</h5>\n<p>This is the type of check you are making</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th><b>Type</b></th><th><b>Description</b></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/effect\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/Effect\">effect</a></td><td>Check potion effects active on the user.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/gamemode\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/Gamemode\">gamemode</a></td><td>Check the user&#x27;s gamemode.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/placeholder\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/Placeholder\">placeholder</a></td><td>Compare placeholders and inputs logically.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/progress\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/Progress\">progress</a></td><td>Compare the value output of a listener.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5>Condition Arguments</h5>\n<p>Configuration for what the condition is calculating, such as what <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/effect\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/Effect\">Potion Effect</a> to be checking for.</p>\n<h5>Outcome</h5>\n<p>This is the condition outcome required for actions to take place. This defaults to <code>true</code>.\\ <code>false</code> may be used to run actions on a false condition outcome.</p>\n<h5>Action</h5>\n<p>This is what the Condition&#x27;s Outcome will effect:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Description</th><th>Variable</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Hide</td><td>If the condition is resolves to false, the hud will be hidden.</td><td>N/A</td><td>N/A</td></tr><tr><td>Color</td><td>If the condition resolves to true, the hud will be recolored. Supports HEX.</td><td>Color</td><td><code>green</code> or <code>#55ff55</code></td></tr><tr><td>Texture</td><td>If the condition resolves to true, the hud will be retextured.</td><td>Texture Path</td><td><code>assets/sword/fill_health.png</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5>Example Conditions</h5>\n<p>This condition will turn the HUD asset&#x27;s to the color green if the user has the &quot;luck&quot; effect.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>conditions:  #Hide if the fill layer is empty.\n  - progress{l=fill;o=&gt;;v=0} true hide\n#Color the hud green if the user has the luck effect.\n  - effect{e=luck} true color green</code></pre>\n<p>When you only need a single condition, it may be written inline as a plain string instead of a list:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>conditions: progress{l=fill;o=&gt;;v=0} true hide</code></pre>\n<p>The <code>default-layout</code> uses conditions to hide the oxygen bar until its value is in use:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>vanilla-air:\n  conditions:  #Hide if the fill layer is empty.\n    - progress{l=fill;o=&lt;;v=100%} true hide\n  layers:\n    icon:\n      texture:\n        path: assets/vanilla/air.png\n      offset:\n        x: -5\n        y: 2\n    fill:\n      texture:\n        path: assets/vanilla/exp_bar_short_fill.png\n      color: &quot;#525aff&quot;\n      offset:\n        x: 0\n        y: 0\n      function:\n        listener: air\n        increment: 13\n        orientation: horizontal\n    outline:\n      texture:\n        path: assets/vanilla/exp_bar_short_outline.png</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions"},"hud:conditions/effect":{"h":"<p>Checks for potion effects on the player.  Can look for multiple effects.\\ Effect names are sourced from <a href=\"https://hub.spigotmc.org/javadocs/bukkit/org/bukkit/potion/PotionEffectType.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SpigotAPI documentation</a>.</p>\n<h4>Attributes</h4>\n<hr>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th><b>Attribute</b></th><th>Aliases</th><th><b>Description</b></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>effect</code></td><td><code>effects</code>, <code>e</code></td><td>The potion type(s) to check for.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Example</h4>\n<hr>\n<p>Colors the <code>lucky_charm</code> Asset green in its HUD if the user has the LUCK effect:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>lucky_charm:\n  conditions:\n  - effect{e=luck} true color green\n  layers:\n    icon:\n      texture:\n        path: assets/luck/clover.png\n      offset:\n        x: -5\n        y: 2</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/Effect"},"hud:conditions/gamemode":{"h":"<p>Checks the player&#x27;s gamemode.</p>\n<h4>Attributes</h4>\n<hr>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th><b>Attribute</b></th><th>Aliases</th><th><b>Description</b></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>gamemode</code></td><td><code>gamemodes</code>, <code>gm</code></td><td>The gamemode(s) to look for.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Example</h4>\n<hr>\n<p>Hides the <code>lucky_charm</code> Asset in its HUD if the player is in Creative or Spectator mode:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>lucky_charm:\n  conditions:\n  - gamemode{gm=creative,spectator} false hide\n  layers:\n    icon:\n      texture:\n        path: assets/luck/clover.png\n      offset:\n        x: -5\n        y: 2</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/Gamemode"},"hud:conditions/logical-operator":{"h":"<p>Certain conditions can use operations to compare two values.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th><code>Symbol</code></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Greater Than</td><td><code>&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater than or Equal to</td><td><code>&gt;=</code>, <code>=&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td>Equal to</td><td><code>=</code>, <code>==</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less than or Equal to</td><td><code>&lt;=</code>, <code>=&lt;</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less than</td><td><code>&lt;</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>These should only be expected to work on placeholders/input that parse numerically!</b></p>\n<h4>Range Operators</h4>\n<p>Range operators check whether a value falls between two bounds. The value format is <code>lower..upper</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th><code>Symbol</code></th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Inclusive range (both ends)</td><td><code>..</code></td><td><code>value &gt;= lower &amp;&amp; value &lt;= upper</code></td></tr><tr><td>Exclusive lower, inclusive upper</td><td><code>&lt;..</code></td><td><code>value &gt; lower &amp;&amp; value &lt;= upper</code></td></tr><tr><td>Inclusive lower, exclusive upper</td><td><code>..&lt;</code></td><td><code>value &gt;= lower &amp;&amp; value &lt; upper</code></td></tr><tr><td>Exclusive range (both ends)</td><td><code>&lt;..&lt;</code></td><td><code>value &gt; lower &amp;&amp; value &lt; upper</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>The <code>-</code> symbol is also accepted as an alias for <code>..</code> (inclusive both ends).</p>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/Logical-Operator"},"hud:conditions/mythicconditions":{"h":"<h4>Mythic Condition</h4>\n<p>Evaluate any <a href=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/Conditions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicMobs Condition</a> against the player. Requires MythicMobs to be installed.</p>\n<p>The argument inside <code>{}</code> is passed directly to MythicMobs as a condition line. Any condition supported by MythicMobs can be used here.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Argument</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>(raw)</code></td><td>A valid MythicMobs condition line.</td><td><code>{onGround}</code> <code>{inCombat}</code> <code>{night}</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5>Example</h5>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>conditions:\n# Hide if player is not on the ground.\n- mythic{onGround} false hide\n# Color the hud red if player is in combat.\n- mythic{inCombat} true color red\n# Change texture at night.\n- mythic{night} true texture assets/hud/night_overlay.png</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/MythicConditions"},"hud:conditions/placeholder":{"h":"<p>Compares placeholders and inputs logically.</p>\n<p>If only the placeholder (attribute <code>1</code>) is defined, the condition will check it for <code>true</code>/<code>false</code>. If both values provided are numbers, they will compare using the <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/logical-operator\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/Logical-Operator\">Logical Operator</a> provider. If a string is provided, the values will be checked if they match.</p>\n<h4>Attributes</h4>\n<hr>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th><b>Attribute</b></th><th>Aliases</th><th><b>Description</b></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>placeholder</code></td><td><code>ph</code>, <code>1</code></td><td>The first value/placeholder to compare.</td></tr><tr><td><code>value</code></td><td><code>val</code>, <code>v</code>, <code>2</code></td><td>The second value/placeholder to compare.</td></tr><tr><td><code>operation</code></td><td><code>oper</code>, <code>o</code></td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/logical-operator\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/Logical-Operator\">Logical Operator</a> to compare with.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>When using a <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/logical-operator\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/Logical-Operator\">range operator</a>, the <code>value</code> attribute must be in the format <code>lower..upper</code>.\\ The placeholder value is parsed as a number and checked against the range.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4>\n<hr>\n<p>Various condition examples using the Player PAPI expansion:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Hide if player&#x27;s direction is not south.\n- placeholder{ph=%player_direction%;v=S} false hide\n# Hide if player is flying.\n- placeholder{ph=%player_is_flying%;v=yes} true hide\n# Hide if player&#x27;s light level is less than 5.\n- placeholder{ph=%player_light_level%;v=5;o=&gt;} true hide\n# Hide if player&#x27;s light level is not between 5 and 10 (inclusive).\n- placeholder{ph=%player_light_level%;v=5..10;o=..} true hide</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/Placeholder"},"hud:conditions/progress":{"h":"<p>Evaluate the output of an asset layer&#x27;s listener.</p>\n<h4>Attributes</h4>\n<hr>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th><b>Attribute</b></th><th>Aliases</th><th><b>Description</b></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>layer</code></td><td><code>lay</code>, <code>l</code></td><td>The asset layer with the listener to evaluate.</td></tr><tr><td><code>value</code></td><td><code>val</code>, <code>v</code></td><td>The value to compare the layer progress against - can be a percent. For range operators, use <code>lower..upper</code> (e.g. <code>20..80</code> or <code>20%..80%</code>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>operation</code></td><td><code>oper</code>, <code>o</code></td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/logical-operator\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/Logical-Operator\">Logical Operator</a> to compare with.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>When using a <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/logical-operator\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/Logical-Operator\">range operator</a>, the <code>value</code> must be <code>lower..upper</code>. Appending <code>%</code> to either bound (or both) switches to percent-based evaluation.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4>\n<hr>\n<p>Hides the Asset in its HUD layout if the <code>air</code> listener used in the <code>fill</code> asset layer is ever less than 100% (so air is in use):</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>vanilla-air:\n  conditions:  #Hide if the fill layer is empty.\n    - progress{l=fill;o=&lt;;v=100%} true hide\n  # Color red when health fill is between 0% and 25% (inclusive).\n  # - progress{l=fill;o=..;v=0%..25%} true color red\n  layers:\n    icon:\n      texture:\n        path: assets/vanilla/air.png\n      offset:\n        x: -5\n        y: 2\n    fill:\n      texture:\n        path: assets/vanilla/exp_bar_short_fill.png\n      color: &quot;#525aff&quot;\n      offset:\n        x: 0\n        y: 0\n      function:\n        listener: air\n        increment: 13\n        orientation: horizontal</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Conditions/Progress"},"hud:components/asset-layers":{"h":"<p>Asset layers are the pieces that come together to make a single <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"components/assets\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Components/Assets\">Asset</a> &quot;piece&quot; of a HUD. Layers each have a single role/feature, and are configured in the order they will visually appear from top to bottom.  For example, A <code>shadow</code> layer would probably be at the bottom of your asset layers, since it should be behind everything.  An <code>icon</code> would likely be on top, so nothing blocks the static texture.</p>\n<h3>Arrangement</h3>\n<h4>Alignment</h4>\n<p>Asset layers move in the direction of their alignment, from their start position:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th><b>align:</b></th><th><code>left</code></th><th><code>center</code></th><th><code>right</code></th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Outlined</h4>\n<p>This will give a shadow-backdrop outline to the asset layer.  This can be customized as a HEX code including alpha layer, such as this red at 100% opacity:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  shadow: &quot;#ff0000ff&quot;</code></pre>\n<h4>Offset</h4>\n<p>The core positioning of the asset layer - this moves the asset based on the origin point for the whole Asset (where it is placed in <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"layouts\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Layouts\">HUD Layouts</a> ).  This is how to position various layers around within an asset, to make a single object ready to arrange within a HUD.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  offset:\n    x: -5  # pixels left/right\n    y: 2   # pixels up/down\n    z: 0   # render layer (depth), optional</code></pre>\n<p>The offset may also be written inline as a comma-separated string of <code>x, y, z</code>.  Omitted values default to <code>0</code>, so all of these are valid:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  offset: &quot;-5, 2&quot;      # x: -5, y: 2\n  offset: &quot;-5, 2, 1&quot;   # x: -5, y: 2, z: 1</code></pre>\n<h4>Color</h4>\n<p>Some layers can be colored, such as tinting a texture or a font color.  Supports named colors from minimessage and hex color codes.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  color: white\n  color: &quot;#ffbb00&quot;</code></pre>\n<h4>Scale</h4>\n<p>A layer can be scaled, changing the pixel resolution of the input texture by this multiplier.\\ For example, this would take a 32px square texture and display it as a 16px square texture:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  scale: 0.5</code></pre>\n<h3>Contents</h3>\n<h4>Text Layer</h4>\n<p>Text layers can be static or contain placeholders, either from the layer&#x27;s listener or PlaceholderAPI.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th><b>Listener Placeholder</b></th><th><b>Description</b></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>%{layer-key}-value%</code></td><td>The <code>value</code> of the listener.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%{layer-key}-max%</code></td><td>The <code>max</code> of the listener.</td></tr><tr><td><code>%{layer-key}-percent%</code></td><td>The percentage output of the listener.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>The <code>{layer-key}</code> to be used here is the name of the asset layer whose listener you are displaying, usually the name of the functional text layer to display the value(s) of the bar the asset is for.</p>\n<h5>Background</h5>\n<p>A text layer can render a <b>dynamic background</b> behind its text - a nine-slice PNG that automatically stretches to fit the width of whatever text is currently displayed.  This is ideal for nameplates, value bubbles, or any text that changes length at runtime.</p>\n<p>The texture is sliced into a fixed-width left cap, a fixed-width right cap, and a tileable center column.  The caps stay intact while the center stretches to fill the space behind the text, so the corners/edges of your background never distort.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  background:\n    texture: ui/text_bg   # the background PNG (required to enable the background)\n    cap: 4                # px of the left &amp; right edges that stay intact\n    padding: 2            # px the background extends past the text on each side\n    offset:\n      y: 0                # fine-tune the background&#x27;s vertical position</code></pre>\n<p>The background is only applied when <code>background.texture</code> is set.  The background is automatically centered vertically on the text; use <code>offset.y</code> to nudge it up or down.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>texture</code></td><td>Path to the background PNG, relative to <code>/MythicHUD/textures/</code>. Enables the background.</td><td>none</td></tr><tr><td><code>cap</code></td><td>Width (px) of the left &amp; right caps that are not stretched.</td><td><code>0</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>padding</code></td><td>Extra px the background extends past the text on each side.</td><td><code>0</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>offset.y</code></td><td>Vertical offset (px) for fine-tuning the background&#x27;s placement.</td><td><code>0</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><code>cap</code> and <code>padding</code> can each be set per-side for asymmetric backgrounds:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  background:\n    texture: ui/text_bg\n    cap:\n      left: 6\n      right: 2\n    padding:\n      left: 4\n      right: 4</code></pre>\n<h6>Example</h6>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>nameplate:\n  text: &quot;%player_name%&quot;\n  font: default\n  align: center\n  background:\n    texture: assets/death-message/outline.png\n    cap: 5\n    padding: 3\n  offset:\n    x: 0\n    y: 0</code></pre>\n<h4>Static Texture Layer</h4>\n<p>This layer type is for rendering a single, positioned texture.  These are often used for the background of a bar to fill behind it as the front, functional layer empties, or a static icon.</p>\n<h5>Example</h5>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>outline:\n  texture:   # looking within the `/MythicHUD/textures/` folder\n    path: assetsvanilla/exp_bar_short_outline.png  \n  align: right\n  outlined: false\n  color: white\n  offset:\n    x: 0\n    y: 0</code></pre>\n<h4>Functional Texture Layer</h4>\n<p>This is a layer for a segmented texture to be linked to one of the configured <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"listeners\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Listeners\">Listeners</a>, to create a bar which will fill/empty based on the listener&#x27;s returned percentage.</p>\n<p>Uses other layer configurations, and has a <code>function</code> section to configure how the bar represents the <code>listener</code>:</p>\n<h5>Listener</h5>\n<p>Listeners determine the percentage fill a bar texture renders.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>function:\n    listener: health</code></pre>\n<h5>Increment</h5>\n<p>The increment is the amount of sections your layer should split into.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>function:\n    increment: 13</code></pre>\n<h6>Orientation</h6>\n<p>The way the layer should deplete from. Can either be Horizontal or Vertical.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>function:\n    orientation: horizontal</code></pre>\n<h6>Reversed</h6>\n<p>Whether or not the layer should deplete the other way. This option defaults to false.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>function:\n    reversed: true</code></pre>\n<h5>Example</h5>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>fill:\n  texture:   # looking within the `/MythicHUD/textures/` folder\n    path: assets/vanilla/exp_bar_short_fill.png\n  align: right\n  outlined: false\n  color: &quot;#f23a3a&quot;\n  scale: 0.5\n  offset:\n    x: 0\n    y: 0\n  function:\n    listener: health\n    increment: 13\n    orientation: horizontal\n    reversed: false</code></pre>\n<h4>Repeated Textures</h4>\n<p>Both the Static and Functional texture layers support a <code>texture.type</code>, controlling how the texture is rendered:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th><code>texture.type</code></th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>split</code></td><td><b>(default)</b> The texture is split/cropped into segments, fading in/out as a single bar.</td></tr><tr><td><code>repeated</code></td><td>The whole texture is drawn multiple times in a row, like a row of icons.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>A <code>repeated</code> texture stamps a copy of the icon side-by-side a number of times, with optional pixel spacing between each copy.  This is perfect for icon-style displays such as a row of hearts, ammo pips, or stars.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>spacing</code></td><td>Pixels of gap between each repeated copy of the icon.</td><td><code>1</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5>Static Repeated</h5>\n<p>On a Static Texture Layer the icon is repeated a fixed number of times.  The count and spacing are read from the <code>texture</code> section.  This is great for a background row of empty hearts to sit behind a functional layer:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>empty-hearts:\n  texture:\n    path: assets/vanilla/heart_empty.png\n    type: repeated\n    increment: 10   # always draw 10 empty hearts\n    spacing: 1      # 1px between each heart\n  align: left\n  offset:\n    x: 0\n    y: 0</code></pre>\n<h5>Functional Repeated</h5>\n<p>On a Functional Texture Layer the number of copies drawn scales with the layer&#x27;s <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"listeners\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Listeners\">Listener</a>, from <code>0</code> up to the configured <code>increment</code>.  This turns a single icon into a discrete, icon-by-icon bar (e.g. a row of hearts that empties one heart at a time).  The count and spacing come from the <code>function</code> section.  Layered on top of the static <code>empty-hearts</code> row above, this draws full hearts according to the player&#x27;s health:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>hearts:\n  texture:\n    path: assets/vanilla/heart.png\n    type: repeated\n  align: left\n  offset:\n    x: 0\n    y: 0\n  function:\n    listener: health\n    increment: 10   # full health shows 10 hearts\n    spacing: 1      # 1px between each heart</code></pre>\n<h4>Head Layer</h4>\n<p>This layer renders a player&#x27;s Minecraft skin face as a pixel-art bitmap display in the HUD. The skin face is sampled as an 8×8 grid, with the hat overlay composited on top if present. Skins are fetched and cached asynchronously; if a skin cannot be loaded, the head renders as solid black.</p>\n<h5>Size</h5>\n<p>Controls how many pixels wide/tall each skin pixel renders. The total display width is <code>size × 8</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>head:\n  size: 4  # default, renders as a 32px square</code></pre>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th><code>size</code></th><th>Display size</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>8px</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>32px (default)</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>64px</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5>Target</h5>\n<p>The player whose head to display.  Supports showing based on player-names &amp; UUIDs, meaning you can display offline-players too. Also supports PlaceholderAPI to output a specific player based on a placeholder. If not specified, will show HudHolder&#x27;s head by default</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>head:\n  target: boy0000\n  #target: 9cc444cd-47cf-4660-96b7-17a7bfef302c\n  #target: &quot;%some_placeholder%&quot;</code></pre>\n<h5>Example</h5>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>self-head:\n  head:\n    size: 4\n  align: left\n  offset:\n    x: 0\n    y: 0\n\nkiller-head:\n  head:\n    size: 4\n    target: &quot;%last_attacker%&quot;\n  align: left\n  offset:\n    x: 36\n    y: 0</code></pre>","u":"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythichud/-/wikis/Components/Asset-Layers"}});
